Page 200 thalweg: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{was wotd|2009|September|23}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|talweg}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from 19th century {{bor|en|de|Thalweg}}, from {{af|de|Thal|gloss1=valley|Weg|gloss2=way, course|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtaːlvɛç/|/ˈtɑːlvɛɡ/|/ˈθɑːlwɛɡ/}}<ref name="OED">“[http://dictionary.oed.com/cgi/entry/50250258 thalweg]” listed in the '''Oxford English Dictionary''' [2<sup>nd</sup> Ed.; 1989]</ref> <ref>{{cite-web |url=https://www.lexico.com/definition/thalweg |accessdate=16 May 2020 |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220204063018/https://www.lexico.com/definition/thalweg |archivedate=4 February 2022 |title=Archived copy }}</ref>
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-thalweg.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɑl.vɛɡ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|thalwege|s}}

# {{lb|en|geology|geography|cartography}} The [[line]] that connects the [[lowest]] [[points]] in a [[valley]] or river [[channel]], and thus the line of [[fastest]] [[flow]] or [[deepest]] water along a [[river]]’s [[course]].

====Usage notes====
* The alternative spelling {{m|en|talweg}} is consistent with the [[w:German spelling reform of 1901|German spelling reform of 1901]]. <ref name="OED"/>

====Translations====
{{trans-top|line that connects the lowest points in a valley or river channel}}
* Catalan: {{t|ca|tàlveg|m}}
