==English==
{{wikipedia|Atlas (disambiguation)|Atlas|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈætləs/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-atlas.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ætləs|s=2}}
* {{hmp|en|atlas}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*telh₂- (bear)}}
From {{bor|en|la|Ā̆tlās}}, from {{der|en|grc|Ἄτλας}}, either from {{m|grc|ἁ-|pos=copulative prefix}} + {{der|en|ine-pro|*telh₂-||bear, undergo, endure}} or of {{der|en|qsb-grc|-}} origin.

====Proper noun====
{{en-proper noun|~|es}}

# {{lb|en|Greek god}} The son of [[Iapetus]] and [[Clymene]], war leader of the [[Titan]]s ordered by the god [[Zeus]] to support the sky on his shoulders; father to the [[Hesperides]], the [[Hyades]], and the [[Pleiades]]; king of the legendary [[Atlantis]].
# A [[placename]]:
## {{lb|en|astronomy}} A [[moon]] of [[Saturn]].
## {{lb|en|astronomy}} A [[crater]] in the last [[quadrant]] of the moon.
## {{lb|en|astronomy}} A triple star system in the Pleiades open cluster (M45) also known as 27 Tauri.
# {{lb|en|countable}} {{surname|en}}.
# {{lb|en|rocketry|military|US}} An SM-65, an early [[ICBM]], soon developed into a long-lived [[orbital]] [[launch vehicle]] [[series]].

