Page 294 ultima Thule: -------- begin text --------
{{also|ultima Thule|Ultima Thule|ultima Thulé|Ultima Thulé}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|la|ultima Thule|ultima Thūlē}}, nominative feminine singular of {{m|la|ultimus||furthest}} + {{m|la|Thule}}, from mediaeval geography; originally from the {{der|en|grc|Θούλη}}, a (possibly mythical) island to the north of Britain.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A place beyond the borders of the known world.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1880|author=w:Henry Wadsworth Longfellow|title=Ultima Thule|chapter=Dedication to G. W. G. |passage='''Ultima Thule'''! Utmost Isle! / Here in thy harbors for a while / We lower our sails; a while we rest / From the unending, endless quest.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=306|passage=It is impossible to define a reason for the Gulf Settlements attaining this unenviable notoriety, unless it is owing to the remoteness of their locality, and the kind of '''''Ultima Thule''''' that part of Australia seems to be.}}
# Highest achievement.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|ultima thule|Ultima Thule}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top}}
* French: {{t+|fr|ultima Thulé}}, {{t|fr|ultime Thulé}}
* Japanese: {{t+|ja|極北|tr=kyokuhoku}}
* Spanish: {{t|es|última Tule|f}}
{{trans-bottom}}

==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|la|Ultima Thūlē}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|[[ultimus|ultima]]<+> [[Thūlē]]<1.both>}}

# {{lb|la|cartography}} {{l|en|ultima Thule}}

====Declension====
{{la-ndecl|ultima<+> Thūlē<1.both>}}
