==Afrikaans==

===Etymology===
Translation of {{der|af|en|The Bay}}, a colloquial name for {{m|en|Port Elizabeth}}, which is located on the western portion of {{m|en|Algoa Bay}}.

===Proper noun===
{{af-proper noun}}

# {{lb|af|informal}} {{place|af|formerly known as [[Port Elizabeth]], a <<city>> and <<port>> in <<p/Eastern Cape>>, <<c/South Africa>>|t=Gqeberha}}
#: {{ux|af|Ons het 'n wonderlike dag in die '''Baai''' gehad!|t=We had wonderful day in '''Port Elizabeth'''!}}

====Usage notes====
This term is most often used with the definite article {{m|af|die}}, but note that the article is not usually capitalised unless appearing as part of a title or at the start of a sentence.

====Descendants====
* {{desc|xh|iBhayi|eBhayi}}
* {{desc|zu|iBhayi}}

===See also===
* {{l|af|baai|t=bay}}

