====Noun====
{{nb-noun-n1}}

# a [[#English|layer]] {{q|a single thickness of some material covering a surface}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1874|author=w:Henrik Ibsen|title=Peer Gynt|page=9|passage=lag af tåger|t=layers of mists}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1904|author=w:Hans E. Kinck|title=Emigranter|page=121|passage=[de fykende snøkorn] roed sig lag paa lag|t=[the fumbling snowflakes] calmed layer upon layer}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2005|author=Elisabeth Botterli; et al.|title=Madonna-gåten|page=|passage=de [hadde] nettopp byttet vinduer. Tre lag isolerglass|t=they [had] just changed windows. Three layers of insulating glass}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2008|author=w:Kari Bøge|title=Komponisten|page=|passage=selv krystall kan sendes i posten om en pakker det i mange nok lag med bobleplast|t=even crystal can be sent in the mail if one packs it in many enough layers of bubble wrap}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2010|author=Margit Vea|title=Kjøkkenpatruljen|page=|passage=bruk en liten sikt og dryss et tynt lag med melis over pannekaken|t=use a small sieve and sprinkle a thin layer of icing sugar over the pancake}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2011|author=Lars Mytting|title=Hel ved|page=44|passage=harde tresorter [på peisen] om kvelden … gir et fint lag glør som fyrer opp neste ilegg|t=hard woods [on the fireplace] in the evening… gives a nice layer of embers that fires up the next insert}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2011|author=w:Ingeborg Arvola|title=Grisehjerter|page=|passage=de ytterste lagene av en løk|t=the outer layers of an onion}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2012|author=Line Nyborg|title=Du vet ikke hvem jeg er|page=|passage=lag på lag med tapet|t=layer upon layer of wallpaper}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2012|author=w:Britt Karin Larsen|title=Før snøen kommer|page=|passage=lag på lag med plagg|t=layer upon layer of garments}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2021|author=w:Monica Isakstuen|title=Mine venner|page=167|passage=jeg liker et tynt lag smør under pålegget|t=I like a thin layer of butter under the topping}}
## {{lb|nb|masonry}} a [[#English|horizontal]] row of [[#English|bricks]] (in a [[#English|masonry]]) bounded by two [[#English|horizontal]] joints
## {{lb|nb|mostly|geology}} a [[#English|horizontal]] widespread [[#English|mass]] of [[#English|soil]] or [[#English|rock]], formed by [[#English|deposition]]
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1897|author=w:Fridtjof Nansen|title=Fram over Polhavet I|page=89|passage=lagene i fjeldet staar paa ende, er brukket og bølet|t=the layers of the rock stand on end, are broken and bulging}}
## {{lb|nb|colloquial}} a [[#English|layer]]; [[#English|part]], [[#English|section]] {{q|part of a whole that one imagines divided along horizontal lines}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1884|author=w:Alexander L. Kielland|title=Fortuna|page=148|passage=i dette land har de øvre lag staaet næsten stille i et par generationer|t=in this country the upper layers have stood almost still for a few generations}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1911|author=w:Sigrid Undset|title=Jenny|page=217|passage=de dypeste lag i deres begges væsen|t=the deepest layers of their being}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=2008|author=Kurt Sweeney|title=Kjegler|page=|passage=siste lag med toleranse flerres vekk|t=last layer of tolerance several away}}
# the [[#English|correct]] or [[#English|usual]] way in which something is arranged; [[#English|correct]] and [[#English|regular]] order, [[#English|condition]], etc.
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2010|author=Peter Serck|title=Natten|page=|passage=jeg [tok det] som et tegn på at vårt venninneforhold ennå sto ved lag|t=I [took it] as a sign that our friendship was still standing}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1929|author=w:Sverre Steen|title=Ferd og fest|page=205|passage=hver ferdemann hadde til plikt å legge en sten til varden når han fór forbi for at den kunde holdes ved lag og helst bli større|t=each traveler had a duty to lay a stone at the cairn when he passed by so that it could be kept at bay and preferably become larger}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1994|author=w:Atle Næss|title=Østre linje|page=|passage=krona var av samme verdi som før krigen og verden skulle sånn sett være i lage igjen|t=the krona was of the same value as before the war and the world was thus to be regular again}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1879|author=w:Peter Christen Asbjørnsen|title=Norske Folke- og Huldre-Eventyr|page=108|passage=huset kom saa rent af lage, at det gav sig i alle laft|t=the house came so clean of the ordinary, that it gave way in every nook and cranny}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1917|author=w:Knut Hamsun|title=Markens Grøde I|page=91|passage=hun hadde stelt alt av lage for dem|t=she had taken care of everything regular for them}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1909|author=w:Henrik Ibsen|title=Efterladte Skrifter I|page=405|passage=verden er af lave|t=the world is of the ordinary}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1873|author=w:Henrik Ibsen|title=Kærlighedens komedie|page=91|passage=bring ham ej af lave|t=do not disturb him}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1879|author=w:Peter Christen Asbjørnsen|title=Norske Folke- og Huldre-Eventyr|page=35|passage=saa lagde jeg i paa nyt lag|t=then I made it all over again}}
#: {{ux|nb|stå ved '''lag'''|still have its validity; remain unchanged|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|nb|holde ved '''lag'''|preserve something in old custom|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|nb|være/komme i '''lag/lage'''|be/come in its usual custom|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|nb|være/komme av '''lage'''|be/get out of their usual or proper custom|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|nb|på nytt '''lag'''|again; with new strength/courage|inline=1}}
# normal and [[#English|good]] [[#English|mood]] or [[#English|temperament]]
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1907|author=w:Bjørnstjerne Bjørnson|title=Bjørnstjerne Bjørnsons fortællinger|page=301|passage=[han] var ikke til at få i lag|t=[he] was not to get in a good mood}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1896|author=w:Thomas Krag|title=Ada Wilde|page=241|passage=fruen var i bedre lav forrige gang|t=the lady was in a better mood last time}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1918|author=w:Gabriel Scott|title=Kilden|page=22|passage=fisken er i det rigtige lave|t=the fish is in the real temperament}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1927|author=w:Regine Normann|title=Nordlandsnatt|page=35|passage=hun [var] amper og ute av lag|t=she [was] amp and out of the ordinary mood}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1929|author=w:Johan Bojer|title=Folk ved sjøen|page=241|passage=[han måtte] skøie med henne, når han var i laget til det|t=[he had to] joke with her, when he was in the mood for it}}
#: {{syn|nb|godlag}}
#: {{ant|nb|ulag}}
# {{lb|nb|etiquette}} [[#English|correct]] and [[#English|polite]] [[#English|language]] or [[#English|manner]]
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1852|author=w:Henrik Wergeland|title=Samlede Skrifter II|page=20|passage=aaretakten kan jeg kjende: uden regel, uden lag|t=the rate of the year I can know: without rule, without manners}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1890|author=w:Henrik Ibsen|title=Hedda Gabler|page=4|passage=jeg er rigtig så ræd for, at jeg ikke skal gøre det til lags for den unge fruen|t=I'm really so scared I'm not going to make it fun for the young lady}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1918|author=w:Gabriel Scott|title=Kilden|page=101|passage=[hun] vet ikke hvordan hun bedst skal te sig for at være Markus til lag|t=[she] does not know how best to behave in order to make Markus satisfied}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2007|author=w:Ragnhild Nilstun|title=Min lange reise ender her|page=|passage=Hanna fikk tøye seg i alle retninger, forsøkte å gjøre dem alle til lags|t=Hanna had to stretch in all directions, trying to please them all}}
#: {{ux|nb|være/gjøre noen til '''lag(s)'''|be/act so that it suits someone; that someone is satisfied|inline=1}}
## {{n-g|Used to indicate an approximate amount of something.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=2010|author=Tore Rem|title=Født til frihet|page=9|passage=huset bør være verdt et sted mellom 120 og 150 000 kroner, men er beheftet med om lag 60 000 i lån|t=The house should be worth somewhere between 120 and 150,000 kroner, but is encumbered with about 60,000 in loans}}
##: {{cot|nb|om lag|omtrent}}
## {{lb|nb|mostly|dialectal}} {{n-g|Used to indicate an [[approximate]] amount of something, with the prepositions {{m|nb|på|t=on}} and {{m|nb|ved|t=by}}.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1907|author=w:Bjørnstjerne Bjørnson|title=Bjørnstjerne Bjørnsons fortællinger|page=98|passage=hvem på lag er den stærkeste der over på eders side?|t=just about who is the strongest over there on your side?}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1892|author=w:Henrik Ibsen|title=Bygmester Solness|page=71|passage=[den 19. september eller] så ved lag|t=[on September 19 or] so approximately}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1897|author=w:Fridtjof Nansen|title=Fram over Polhavet I|page=524|passage=vore nye askekjælker var nu paa lag færdige|t=our new ash sledges were now about finished}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1918|author=w:Gabriel Scott|title=Kilden|page=142|passage=han steger ut paa det lav klokken fire|t=he steps out at about four o'clock}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1960|author=w:Johan Bojer|title=Samlede verker IV|page=165|passage=her blir mest som et sanatorium paa lag|t=here is mostly like a sanatorium approximately}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1960|author=w:Johan Bojer|title=Vår egen stamme|page=93|passage=kor på lag var det han strauk|t=choir about was what he flunked}}
## {{n-g|Used in the definite form with the preposition ''[[i]]'' (in) and a superlative adjective to indicate a high degree of something.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1918|author=w:Gabriel Scott|title=Kilden|page=164|passage=benstellet [på hummeren] er i tyndeste laget|t=the tooth frame [on the lobster] is very thin}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1920|author=w:Peter Egge|title=Inde i Fjordene|page=353|passage=Siri var i seneste laget|t=Siri was very late}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1992|author=w:Torgrim Eggen|title=Gjeld|page=266|passage=anda er i feteste laget for ham, men den er nydelig tilberedt|t=the duck is too fat for him, but it is beautifully cooked}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1988|author=w:Arild Nyquist|title=Giacomettis forunderlige reise|page=|passage=denne historien virket litt i eventyrligste laget – for å si det pent|t=this story seemed a bit in the more adventurous theme - to say the least}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=2002|author=w:Geir Pollen|title=Når den gule solen brenner|page=|passage=spillelæreren syntes det var i tidligste laget å gi seg i kast med Mozarts klarinettkonsert|t=the playing teacher thought it was a bit early to embark on Mozart's clarinet concerto}}
# {{lb|nb|mostly|dialectal}} [[#English|manner]]; [[#English|being]], [[#English|appearance]] {{q|characteristic mode of acting or behaving}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1925|author=w:Sigrid Undset|title=Olav Audunssøn i Hestviken I|page=207|passage=[hun likte] hans rolige, godlidende lag|t=[she liked] his calm, good-natured way of being}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1925|author=w:Peter Egge|title=Hansine Solstad|page=96|passage=[det var] noget i alt hans lag som pekte paa at han visste hvem han var|t=[there was] something in all his manners that pointed out that he knew who he was}}
# an [[#English|individual]] and [[#English|natural]] way of treating [[#English|people]]; way of approaching [[#English|something]]
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1877|author=w:Jørgen Moe|title=Samlede Skrifter II|page=16|passage=at bringe folkets fortællere til aabent og uforbeholdent at meddele sig – forudsætter et eget lag at behandle dem paa|t=to bring the narrators of the people to openly and unreservedly communicate - presupposes a separate way to treat them on}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1992|author=w:Eilert Sundt|title=Om giftermål i Norge|page=214|passage=stenbrydere og sådan grove arbeidsmænd have så lidet lag på at indrette det hyggeligt for sig i det logement|t=quarrymen and such rude workers have so little ways to arrange it cozy for themselves in that lodging}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1917|author=w:Knut Hamsun|title=Markens Grøde I|page=133|passage=hun hadde lag med børn|t=she had a way with children}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1920|author=w:Sigrid Undset|title=Kransen|page=194|passage=alle vitenskaper og kunster tror jeg den manden hadde faat laget for av Gud selv|t=all sciences and arts I believe the man had been made for by God himself}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1923|author=w:Hans Aanrud|title=Fortællinger I|page=152|passage=han havde faaet et sligt lag til at snakke passelig grovt med kvindfolkene|t=he had got such a way to talk suitably rudely with the women}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1990|author=w:Atle Næss|title=Kraften som beveger|page=|passage=hun hadde et særlig lag med supper, de var kraftige og mettende|t=she had a special way with soups, they were powerful and filling}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2020|author=w:Tove Nilsen|title=Den eneste broren|page=163|passage=du har laget, jeg merker det, du har laget|t=you have a way with it, I notice it, you have a way}}
# a [[#English|gathering]], [[#English|company]]; [[#English|togetherness]], [[#English|companionship]]
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1926|author=w:Bjørnstjerne Bjørnson|title=Samlede Digte I|page=27|passage=[vi] legte sammen i skog og lage’|t=[we] played together in the woods and in company}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1917|author=w:Hans Aanrud|title=Fortællinger for barn I|page=231|passage=Astrid satte sig bort til bordet i lag med jenterne|t=Astrid sat down at the table together with the girls}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1927|author=w:Johan Bojer|title=Samlede verker III|page=18|passage=tak for laget i sommer da!|t=thanks for the company this summer then!}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1915|author=w:Anders Krogvig|title=Fra det nationale gjennembruds tid. Breve fra Jørgen Moe til P. Chr. Asbjørnsen og andre|page=15|passage=[romjulen gikk] med lag og lystighet, dans og optog, julebukker og lekemoro|t=[Christmas time went] with companionship and merriment, dancing and processions, Yule goats and playing}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1923|author=w:Hans Aanrud|title=Fortællinger I|page=10|passage=nei, han Far faar bli; den skammen vil jeg [dvs. Iver Langseth] ikke ha, at’n Far har brudt lag paa Langseth|t=no, father may stay; that shame I will [meaning Iver Langseth] not have, that father has left Langseth}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1879|author=w:Peter Christen Asbjørnsen|title=Norske Folke- og Huldre-Eventyr|page=331|passage=paa hjemveien kom han i lag med grander og bygdefolk|t=on the way home he came in contact with grander and villagers}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1917|author=w:Knut Hamsun|title=Markens Grøde II|page=18|passage=jeg var tilfreds jeg kunde slaa lag med dig|t=I was satisfied I could follow with you}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1908|author=w:Knut Hamsun|title=Rosa|page=327|passage=hun møtte ham paa vejen og slog sig i lag med ham|t=she met him on the road and joined him}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1886|author=w:Alexander L. Kielland|title=Sne|page=18|passage=[husmennene] gav sig ilag med granen|t=[the housekeepers] joined the spruce}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1917|author=w:Knut Hamsun|title=Markens Grøde II|page=27|passage=hun hadde opdaget hvad han var i lag med|t=she had discovered what he was up to}}
