#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1875|author=w:Henrik Ibsen|title=Digte|page=100|passage=længre vest er en skumklædt grund, der gav [yachten] det glatte lag|t=further west is a foam-covered ground that gave [the yacht] the shooting cannons}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1929|author=w:Olaf Benneche|title=Tordenskjold|page=116|passage=– Klar ved kanonene der! Gi ham det glatte lag, fyr!|t=- Ready for the cannons there! Give him the shooting cannons, fire!}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1873|author=w:Henrik Ibsen|title=Kærlighedens komedie|page=137|passage=fast aldrig var vi enige, vi gav hinanden tidt det glatte lag|t=though we never agreed, we often gave each other the full truth}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1946|author=w:Joachim Holst-Jensen|title=Holst-Jensen ruller opp|page=95|passage=da tok sinnet meg, jeg riposterte i anmelderens egen avis og ga ham det glatte lag|t=then the mind took me, I reposted in the reviewer's own newspaper and gave him the honest truth}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1995|author=John Ege|title=Dominoklubben|page=|passage=jeg ga han det glatte lag, spurte om han hadde lært å kjøre drosje i Kardemomme by|t=I gave him the harsh truth, asked if he had learned to drive a taxi in Cardamom town}}
