{{wikipedia|Names of China}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|grc|Τζίνιτζα||rare}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|grc}}, but probably from {{der|grc|sa|^चीन||[[China]]}}, possibly via {{der|grc|ar|^صِين|t=[[China]]; the [[Chinese]]}} and usually held to derive from {{der|grc|och|^秦||[[Qin]]}}. See "[[w:Names of China#Sinae|Names of China]]" at [[w:Main Page|Wikipedia]].

===Pronunciation===
{{grc-IPA|period=byz1}}<!-- This pronunciation should not show anything before Byzantine -->

===Proper noun===
{{head|grc|proper noun}}

# {{lb|grc|culture}} a [[land]] and [[people]] of [[East Asia]] [[usually]] [[identified]] as the [[southern]] [[Chinese]]
#* '''6th century''', [[w:Cosmas Indicopleustes|Cosmas Indicopleustes]], ''[[w:Christian Topography|Christian Topography]]'', II, 45:
#*: {{quote|grc|Αὕτη δὲ ἡ χώρα τοῦ μεταξίου ἐστὶν ἐν τῇ ἐσωτέρᾳ πάντων Ἰνδίᾳ, κατὰ τὸ ἀριστερὸν μέρος εἰσιόντων τοῦ Ἰνδικοῦ πελάγους, περαιτέρω πολὺ τοῦ Περσικοῦ κόλπου καὶ τῆς νήσου τῆς καλουμένης παρὰ μὲν Ἰνδοῖς, Σελεδίβα, παρὰ δὲ τοῖς Ἕλλησι, [[Ταπροβάνη]], [[Τζίνιστα]] οὕτω καλουμένη, κυκλουμένη πάλιν ἐξ ἀριστερῶν ὑπὸ τοῦ Ὠκεανοῦ, ὥσπερ καὶ ἡ [[Βαρβαρία]] κυκλοῦται ἐκ δεξιῶν ὑπ᾽ αὐτοῦ... Περαιτέρω δὲ τῆς [[Τζίνιστα]] οὔτε πλέεται οὔτε οἰκεῖται.
|translation=Now this country of silk is situated in the remotest of all the Indies, and lies to the left of those who enter the Indian sea, far beyond the Persian Gulf, and the island called by the Indians Selediba and by the Greeks Taprobanê. It is called '''Tzinista''', and is surrounded on the left by the ocean, just as Barbaria is surrounded by it on the right... Beyond '''Tzinista''' there is neither navigation nor any land to inhabit.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|grc|Θῖνα}}, {{l|grc|Θῖναι}}, {{l|grc|Σῖναι}}

====See also====
* {{sense|modern China}} {{l|el|Κίνα}}
-------- end text --------
Page 569 Τζίνιτζα: -------- begin text --------
==Ancient Greek==

===Proper noun===
{{head|grc|proper noun}}

# {{lb|grc|rare|culture}} {{alt form|grc|Τζίνιστα|nodot=a}}: the [[southern]] [[Chinese]]; [[their]] [[land]], [[China]]
#* '''1878''', Thomas Rawson Birks translating Franz Delitzsch's citation of Neumann in his [https://archive.org/stream/commentaryonbook00birk#page/n7/mode/2up Commentary on the Book of Isaiah], [https://archive.org/stream/commentaryonbook00birk#page/246/mode/2up p. 247]:
#*: {{quote|grc|The name [[Θῖναι|Θ''ῖναι'']], [[w:Strabo|Strabo]], [[Σῖναι|Σ''ῖναι'']], [[w:Claudius Ptolemy|Ptol.]], [[Τζίνιτζα|Τ''ζίνιτζα'']], [[w:Cosmas Indicopleustes|Kosmas]], did not obtain currency first from the founder of the dynasty [[wikt:Tsin|Tsin]]; but, long before this, [[wikt:Tsin|Tsin]] was the name of a feudal kingdom in [[wikt:Shensi|Shensi]], one of the western provinces of the Sinese land, and [[w:Feitsa|Feitsa]], the first feudal King of [[wikt:Tsin|Tsin]], began to reign as early as {{smallcaps|b.c.}}&nbsp;897.}}
