==Assyrian Neo-Aramaic==
{{aii-root|ܐ ܬ ܪ}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|aii|arc|אַתְרָא|tr=ʾaṯrā|t=country; idem}}, from {{der|aii|sem-pro|*ʔaṯar-}}; cognate to {{cog|he|אֲשֶׁר|tr=ashér|pos=relative pronoun}}, {{m|he|אֲתָר|tr=atár|t=site}}, {{cog|gez|አሰር}}, {{m|gez|አሠር|t=trace, vestige; way, road; relic}}, {{cog|ar|أَثَر|t=trace, vestige, impression, relic}} and {{cog|akk|ašrum|𒆠|tr=ašrum|t=place, site}}. Also related to the preposition {{m|aii|ܒܵܬ݇ܪ|t=behind, after}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Standard}} {{IPA|aii|[ˈʔaθraː]}}
* {{a|Nineveh Plains}} {{IPA|aii|[ˈʔaθˤrˤa]}}
* {{a|Urmian}} {{IPA|aii|[ˈʔatraː]}}

===Noun===
{{aii-noun|ܐܲܬ݂ܪܵܐ|m-s|pl=ܐܲܬ݂ܪ̈ܵܘܵܬ݂ܹܐ}}

# [[country]], [[land]]
# {{ellipsis of|aii|ܐܲܬ݂ܪܵܐ ܕܐܲܒ݂ܵܗܵܬ݂ܹ̈ܐ|t=[[homeland]], [[fatherland]]}}

