{{c|aii|Geography|Political subdivisions|Time}}

==Classical Syriac==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|syc|sem-pro|*ʔaṯar-}}. Cognate to {{cog|arc|אַתְרָא|tr=ʾaṯrā|t=idem}}, {{cog|he|אֲשֶׁר|tr=ʾăšĕ́r|pos=relative pronoun}}, {{cog|gez|አሰር}}, {{m|gez|አሠር|t=trace, vestige; way, road; relic}}, {{cog|ar|أَثَر|t=trace, vestige, impression, relic}}, {{cog|akk|ašrum|𒆠|tr=ašrum|t=place, site}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|syc|[ˈʔaθ.rɑ]}} {{q|singular}}
* {{IPA|syc|[ˈʔaθ.re]|[ʔaθ.rawˈwɑ.θɑ]}} {{q|plural}}

===Noun===
{{syc-noun|tr=ʾaṯrā|m|ܐܬܪܘܬܐ|ܐܬܪܐ|pltr=ʾaṯrawwāṯā|pltr2=ʾaṯrē}}

# [[place]], [[spot]]
# [[region]], [[land]], [[country]]
# [[district]], [[province]]
# [[inhabitants]]
# [[means]]
# {{lb|syc|figuratively}} [[room]], [[space]]; [[opportunity]], [[time]]; [[delay]]

====Usage notes====
Usually, the plural {{m|syc|ܐܬܪܐ|tr=ʾaṯrē}} is a [[paucal]] plural (from two to ten) while the plural {{m|syc|ܐܬܪܘܬܐ|tr=ʾaṯrawwāṯā}} is a multiple plural (eleven or more).

====Inflection====
{{syc-decl-noun
|sg.abs.=[[ܐܬܪ]]
|sg.cstr.=[[ܐܬܪ]]
|sg.emph.=[[ܐܬܪܐ]]
|pl.abs.=[[ܐܬܪܘܢ]] ,[[ܐܬܪܝܢ]]
|pl.cstr.=[[ܐܬܪܘܬ]] ,[[ܐܬܪܝ]]
