==Assyrian Neo-Aramaic==

===Etymology 1===
{{aii-root|ܓ ܠ ܐ}}
Compare {{cog|he|גּוֹלֶה|tr=golé}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Standard}} {{IPA|aii|[ɡɑːljɑː]}}

====Noun====
{{aii-noun|ܓܵܠܝܵܐ|m-s|f=ܓܵܠܝܼܬܵܐ|pl=ܓܵܠܝܹ̈ܐ}}

# [[exile]], [[diasporan]]
# [[captive]], [[prisoner]]
#: {{syn|aii|ܐܲܣܝܼܪܵܐ}}

=====Inflection=====
{{aii-infl-noun-m-ircnstr|ܓܵܠܝ|ܓܵܠܹܐ}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|aii|ܓܵܠܘܼܬܵܐ|t=[[exile]], [[diaspora]]}}
* {{l|aii|ܓܵܠܘܼܬܵܢܵܝܵܐ}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|aii|arc|גַּלְיָא|tr=galyā}}, equivalent to the passive participle of {{m|aii|ܓܵܠܹܐ|t=to reveal}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Standard}} {{IPA|aii|[ɡɪl.jɑː]}}

====Adjective====
{{aii-adjective|ܓܸܠܝܵܐ|f=ܓܠܝܼܬܵܐ|pl=ܓܸܠܝܹ̈ܐ}}

# [[revealed]]
# [[uncovered]], [[bare]], [[exposed]]
# [[prominent]], [[apparent]]
# [[evident]], [[obvious]], [[clear]]

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|aii|ܓܠܝܼܚܵܐ}}, {{l|aii|ܩܪܝܼܚܵܐ}}, {{l|aii|ܦܬܝܼܚܵܐ}}, {{l|aii|ܚܸܙܝܵܐ}}, {{l|aii|ܡܸܬܚܲܙܝܵܢܵܐ}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col-auto|aii|ܓܸܠܝܵܐܝܼܬ݂|ܓܸܠܝܘܼܬܵܐ|ܦܵܝܹܫ ܓܸܠܝܵܐ}}

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Standard}} {{IPA|aii|[d͡ʒɪl.jɑː]}}

====Adjective====
{{aii-adjective|ܓ̰ܸܠܝܵܐ|f=ܓ̰ܠܝܼܬܵܐ|pl=ܓ̰ܸܠܝܹ̈ܐ}}

# {{lb|aii|phonetics}} followed by the phonetic sign [[ܡܓܠܝܢܐ|majlyānā]]
#: {{coordinate terms|aii|ܩܸܫܝܵܐ|ܪܲܟܝܼܟ݂ܵܐ|ܛܠܝܼܩܵܐ}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{sense|majlyānā}} This is usually used in the feminine form since the names of the letters are feminine.

===Etymology 4===
{{aii-root|ܓ ܠ ܠ}}
Also attested in {{cog|syc|ܓܠܠܐ|tr=glālā}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Standard}} {{IPA|aii|[ɡalijːjɑː]}}

====Noun====
{{aii-noun|ܓܲܠܝܼܵܐ|m-s|pl=ܓܲܠܝܼܹ̈ܐ}}

# {{lb|aii|geography}} [[floodplain]], [[valley]]

=====Inflection=====
{{aii-infl-noun-m|ܓܲܠܝܼ}}

{{cln|aii|verb forms|past participles}}
