Page 627 ܝܒܫܐ: -------- begin text --------
==Assyrian Neo-Aramaic==
{{aii-root|ܝ ܒ ܫ}}

===Etymology===
{{lbor|aii|syc|-}}, from {{der|aii|arc|יַבְשָׁא|tr=yaḇšā}}; cognate to {{cog|ar|يُبْس|tr=yubs}}, {{cog|he|יַבָּשָׁה|tr=yabashá}} and {{cog|hbo|יובש|יֹבֶשׁ|tr=yṓḇeš}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Standard}} {{IPA|aii|[ˈjawʃɑː]}}
* {{a|Urmian}} {{IPA|aii|[ˈjavʃɑː]}}

===Noun===
{{aii-noun|ܝܲܒ݂ܫܵܐ|m}}

# {{lb|aii|geography}} [[earth]], [[dry]] [[land]]
#: {{syn|aii|ܒܸܪܙܵܐ}}
#: {{ant|aii|ܝܵܡܵܐ}}

====Inflection====
{{aii-infl-noun-m-ircnstr|ܝܲܒ݂ܫ|ܝܼܒ݂ܸܫ}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|aii|ܝܲܒ݂ܫܵܢܵܝܵܐ|t=of dry places, [[terrestrial]]}}

==Classical Syriac==

===Etymology===
From the root {{syc-root-entry|ܝ|ܒ|ܫ}} related to dryness. Compare {{cog|ar|يُبْس|tr=yubs}} and {{cog|he|יובש|יֹבֶשׁ|tr=yṓḇeš}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|syc|[javʃɑ(ʔ)]}} {{a|singular}}
* {{IPA|syc|[javʃe(ʔ)]}} {{a|plural}}

===Noun===
{{syc-noun|m|ܝܒܫܐ}}

# {{lb|syc|geography}} [[earth]], [[dry]] [[land]]
# {{lb|syc|dialectal}} [[Houbara bustard]]

====Inflection====
{{syc-decl-noun-m|ܝܒܫ}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|syc|ܝܡܐ}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|yb$}}
* {{R:Costaz 1963}}, p. 136a
* {{R:Payne Smith 1902}}, p. 185b
* {{R:Sokoloff 2009}}, p. 562a

===Anagrams===
* {{l|syc|ܒܝܫܐ}}
* {{l|syc|ܫܒܝܐ}}

