Page 628 ܝܡܐ: -------- begin text --------
==Assyrian Neo-Aramaic==

===Etymology 1===
{{aii-root|ܐ ܡ ܗ}}
Variant of {{m|aii|ܐܸܡܵܐ}}, from {{inh|aii|arc|אִמָּא|tr=ʾimmā}} with a shift from an initial /ʔ/ to /j/, from {{inh|aii|sem-pro|*ʔimm-}}; compare {{cog|tru|ܐܶܡܐ}}, {{cog|ar|أُمّ|tr=ʔumm}}, {{cog|he|אֵם|tr=em}} and {{m|he|אִמָּא|tr=ímma}}.

The second sense is from {{bor|aii|akk|ummat erî|t=lower milestone, grindstone}}. The first element, ummat, is the construct form of {{l|akk|ummatu|t=main part}} while the second element erî is the genetive form of {{l|akk|erû|t=lower stone of hand-mill}}. Based on folk etymology or a reinterpretation of the Akkadian term, the word was reinterpreted as “mother” in Aramaic. In some dialects, the fourth sense then evolved from this.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Standard}} {{IPA|aii|[ˈjɪm.mɑː]|[ˈjɪm.mä]}}
* {{a|Nineveh Plains}} {{IPA|aii|[ʔɪmma]|[jɪmma]}}
* {{a|Urmian}} {{IPA|aii|[ˈjɪ.mɒ]}}

====Noun====
{{aii-noun|ܝܸܡܵܐ|f|pl=ܝܸܡܵܬܹ̈ܐ|pl2=ܝܸܡܵܘܵܬ݂ܵܐ|m=ܒܵܒܵܐ|m2=ܐܲܒ݂ܵܐ}}

# [[mother]] {{gloss|female parent who gets pregnant and gives birth to a child}}
# lower millstone of a mill; lower grindstone of a hand-mill
# {{lb|aii|Tergawar}} [[colostrum]], [[first milk]]
# {{lb|aii|Tyare}} boulder that has rolled or is rolling down a slope
# [[malignant]] [[tumor]]

=====Inflection=====
{{aii-infl-noun-m-fempl|ܝܸܡ|ܝܸܡ}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|aii|ܝܸܡ ܩܪܵܝܬܵܐ|t=[[mater lectionis]]}}
* {{l|aii|ܝܸܡܵܝܵܐ|t=[[motherly]], [[maternal]]}}
*: {{l|aii|ܠܸܫܵܢܵܐ ܝܸܡܵܝܵܐ|t=[[mother tongue]]}}
* {{l|aii|ܝܸܡܘܼܬܵܐ|t=[[motherhood]], [[maternity]]}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|aii|ܐܲܡܘܼܡܵܐ|t=[[mold]], [[matrix]]}}
* {{l|aii|ܐܘܼܡܬܵܐ|t=[[nation]]}}
* {{l|aii|ܐܸܡܗܵܬܹ̈ܐ|t=female [[ancestor]]s}}

===Etymology 2===
{{aii-root|ܝ ܡ ܡ}}
A Northwest Semitic innovation; compare {{cog|uga|𐎊𐎎}}, {{cog|he|יָם|tr=yam}}, and also borrowed into {{cog|ar|يَمّ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Standard}} {{IPA|aii|[ˈjɑːmɑː]|[ˈjä.mä]}}
* {{a|Urmian}} {{IPA|aii|[ˈjɒ.mɒ]}}

====Noun====
{{aii-noun|ܝܵܡܵܐ|m|pl=ܝܲܡܡܹ̈ܐ}}

# [[sea]] {{gloss|large body of salt water}}
#: {{ant|aii|ܝܲܒ݂ܫܵܐ|t1=dry land}}
# [[beach]] {{gloss|pebbly or sandy shore, especially by the sea between high- and low-water marks}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This term is grammatically masculine, and normally masculine in the [[w:Alqosh|Alqosh]]/[[w:Nineveh Plains|Nineveh Plains]] dialect(s) however may be feminine in others.

=====Inflection=====
{{aii-infl-noun-m-ircnstr-irp|ܝܵܡ|ܝܲܡܡ|ܝܲܡ|ܝܲܡܡܲܝ̈}}

=====Hyponyms=====
