*: {{l|aii|ܒܹܝܬ ܢܲܗܪܝܼܢ|t=[[Mesopotamia]]}}

{{cln|aii|nouns with irregular plurals}}
{{c|aii|Canals|Geography}}

==Classical Syriac==
{{syc-rootbox|ܢ ܗ ܪ}}
{{wikipedia|lang=arc}}

===Alternative forms===
* Hebrew script: {{l|arc|sc=Hebr|נהרא}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|syc|sem-pro|*nahar-|t=river}}. Cognate with {{cog|ar|نَهْر}} and {{cog|he|נָהָר|tr=nahár}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|syc|[nahrɑ(ʔ)]}} {{a|singular}}
* {{IPA|syc|[nahre(ʔ)]|[nahrawwɑθɑ(ʔ)]}} {{a|plural}}

===Noun===
{{syc-noun|m|ܢܗܪܘܬܐ|ܢܗܪܐ|tr=nahrā}}

# [[river]], [[stream]]
#: {{synonyms|syc|ܫܚܠܐ}}
# [[branch]] of a river
# [[canal]]

====Usage notes====
Usually, the plural {{m|syc|ܢܗܪܐ|tr=nahrē(ʾ)|sc=Syrc}} is a [[paucal]] plural (from two to ten) while the plural {{m|syc|ܢܗܪܘܬܐ|tr=nahrawwāṯā(ʾ)|sc=Syrc}} is a multiple plural (eleven or more).

