Page 632 delta: -------- begin text --------
{{also|DELTA|Delta}}
==Translingual==
[[file:delta flag.svg|frameless|right|border|upright]]

===Noun===
{{head|mul|noun}}

# {{alt case|mul|Delta|nodot=1}} {{ng|of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet}}.

==English==
{{letter_disp2|gamma|[[image:Greek_uc_delta.png|36px]][[image:Greek_lc_delta.png|26px]]|epsilon|δέλτα|Δ|δ}}
{{slim-wikipedia}}
[[File:Lena_River_Delta_-_Landsat_2000.jpg|thumb|{{w|Lena River}} '''delta''' (landform at the mouth of a river).]]

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|δέλτα}}, borrowed from a Phoenician word for "door", ultimately from {{der|en|sem-pro|*dalt-}}. {{doublet|en|dalet}}.
* {{sense|river}} from the triangular shape of the majuscule Greek letter delta &Delta;
* {{sense|USSF}} from the [[delta wing]], symbol of the USSF, a triangular wing, shaped like the majuscule Greek letter delta &Delta;

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɛltə/|[ˈdɛɫtə]}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-delta.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛltə|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The fourth letter of the modern [[Greek alphabet]] ''[[Δ]]'', ''[[δ]]''.
# A landform at the mouth of a river where it empties into a body of water.
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Nile Delta|Nile '''Delta'''}}}}
# {{lb|en|international standards}} {{alt case|mul|Delta|nodot=1}} {{ng|from the {{w|NATO Phonetic Alphabet|NATO/ICAO Phonetic Alphabet}}.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|physics|engineering}} The symbol ''[[Δ]]''; A change in a quantity, likely from "d" for "difference".
#: {{ux|en|[[Δ]]V - "'''delta''' vee"(change in velocity, used in rocketry and orbital mechanics)}}
# {{lb|en|finance}} The rate of change in an [[option]] value with respect to the [[underlying]] [[asset]]'s [[price]].
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} A value in [[delta notation]] indicating the relative abundances of [[isotope]]s.
# {{lb|en|computing}} The set of differences between two versions of a file.
#: {{ux|en|When you update the file, the system will only save the '''deltas'''.}}
# {{lb|en|computing|informal}} A small but noticeable effect. Compare {{m|en|epsilon}}.
#: {{ux|en|This will slow the main code path down, but only by '''delta'''.}}
# {{lb|en|surveying}} The [[angle]] subtended at the [[center]] of a circular [[arc]].
# A type of [[cargo bike]] that has one wheel in front and two in back.
# {{lb|en|electrical|often|attributive}} The closed figure produced by connecting three coils or circuits successively, end for end, especially in a three-phase system.
#: {{ux|en|'''delta''' winding; '''delta''' connection; '''delta''' current}}
# {{lb|en|US|military|U.S. Space Force}} A military unit, nominally headed by a [[colonel]], equivalent to a [[USAF]] operations [[wing]], or an army [[regiment]].
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} a star that is usually the fourth brightest of a constellation.
# {{lb|en|physics}} one of four [[baryons]] consisting of [[up]] and [[down]] quarks with a combined [[spin]] of 3/2: [[&Delta;++|&Delta;<sup>++</sup>]] (uuu), [[&Delta;+|&Delta;<sup>+</sup>]] (uud), [[&Delta;0|&Delta;<sup>0</sup>]] (udd), or [[&Delta;&minus;|&Delta;<sup>&minus;</sup>]] (ddd)
# {{lb|en|medicine}} {{short for|en|delta variant}} {{gloss|variant of the [[SARS-CoV-2]] virus}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|USSF}} {{l|en|garrison}} {{q|a support wing equivalent}}

====Hypernyms====
