Identical to Proto-Turkic ''{{l|trk-pro|*burun|t=before, earlier than}}'' (See {{l|ba|борон|t=before}}).

Cognate with
{{cog|oui|tr=burun|t=nose}};
{{cog|tt|борын||t=nose}},
{{cog|kk|мұрын||t=nose}},
{{cog|alt|мурун|t=nose}},
{{cog|uz|burun||t=nose}},
{{cog|ug|بۇرۇن||t=nose}},
{{cog|tk|burun||t=nose}},
{{cog|sah|мурун||t=nose}},
etc.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ba|[mʊ̞.ˈrʊ̞n]}}
* {{hyphenation|ba|мо|рон}}

===Noun===
{{ba-noun}}

# {{qualifier|animal's}} [[nose]], [[snout]], [[muzzle]]
# {{qualifier|elephant's}} [[trunk]]
# {{qualifier|insects}} [[proboscis]]; [[rostrum]]
# {{qualifier|vehicles}} [[nose]] ''(of boat, airplane, etc.)''
#: {{ux|ba|Кәмәнең '''мороно'''.|translation=The '''nose''' of the boat.}}
# {{qualifier|vessels}} [[nose]], [[beak]], [[snout]]
# {{lb|ba|geography}} [[cape]], [[promontory]]
#: {{ux|ba|Австралияның көнсығыш нөктәһе — Байрон '''мороно'''.|translation=Australia's eastern''(most)'' point is '''Cape''' Byron.}}

