==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|non-oen|brō}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*brōwō||bridge; brow}}, possibly from {{der|sv|ine-pro||*bʰruH-|beam; bridge}}, which may be the same root as {{m|ine-pro|*h₃bʰrúHs||(eye)brow}}, whence {{m|sv|bryn}}. Compare {{cog|nb|bro}}, {{cog|is|brú||bridge}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/bruː/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-bro.ogg|audio}}
* {{rhymes|sv|uː|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|c}}

# [[bridge]] (a construction that spans a divide)
#: {{ux|sv|Stan mellan '''broarna'''|The town between the bridges (Stockholm old town)}}
#: {{ux|sv|Släpp ingen djävul över '''bron''', håll ut en stund ännu!|Let no devil across the bridge, hold out yet a while!}}
# [[road bank]] (a road reenforced with stone or timber, in particular across wetlands)
# [[quay]]
#: {{syn|sv|brygga|skeppsbro}}
# [[porch]]
#: {{syn|sv|förstubro}}
#: {{ux|sv|Jag får min motion när jag går ifrån '''bron''' och till vår garageuppfart.|I get my exercise when I walk from the porch to our driveway.}}

