Page 769 quart: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/kwɔːt/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/kwɔɹt/|/kɔɹt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-quart.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{homophones|en|court}} {{qualifier|General American, without the /w/ sound in 'quart'}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)t|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|quart}}, {{m|enm|quarte}}, from {{der|en|fro|quarte}}, {{m|fro|carte}}, from {{der|en|la|quartus|t=one-fourth}}. Cognate with {{cog|es|cuarto||quarter; room, quarters}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A unit of liquid [[capacity]] equal to two [[pint]]s; one-fourth (quarter) of a gallon. Equivalent to 1.136 liters in the UK and 0.946 liter (liquid quart) or 1.101 liters (dry quart) in the U.S.
# {{lb|en|cards}} Four [[successive]] [[card]]s of the same [[suit]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1908|author=Cavendish|title=The laws of piquet adopted|passage=A tierce major is good against any other tierce; a '''quart''' minor is good against a tierce major.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[fourth]]; a [[quarter]]; hence, a region of the earth.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=II|canto=X|stanza=14|passage=Camber did possesse the Westerne '''quart'''.}}

