Page 816 olin: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Olin}}
==Central Nahuatl==

===Etymology===
From {{der|nhn|nci|olin}}.

===Noun===
{{head|nhn|noun}}

# Earth [[movement]]

[[Category:Amecameca Central Nahuatl]]
[[Category:Milpa Alta Central Nahuatl]]
{{c|nhn|Geography}}

==Classical Nahuatl==
{{was fwotd|nci|2019|March|19}}
[[Image:Olin.jpg|thumb|right|The [[glyph]] for the day sign ''olīn'' “quake”, from the [[w:Codex Magliabechiano|Codex Magliabechiano]].]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|nci|ollin}}, {{l|nci|uli}} {{qualifier|obsolete spellings}}

===Etymology===
[[apocope|Apocopic]] [[deverbal]] formation from {{m|nci|olīni||to move; get going}} or {{m|nci|olīnia||to agitate; shift; displace}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nci|[ˈo.liːn̥]}}

===Noun===
{{nci-noun|i|olīn}}

# the seventeenth of the twenty [[day sign]]s of the {{m|nci|tōnalpōhualli}}; a conceptual [[depiction]] of [[movement]] as two intertwining [[band]]s of color
#* '''16th c.:''' ''[[w:Codex Magliabechiano|Codex Magliabechiano]]'', f. 13r.
#*: {{quote|nci|chicume '''uli''' la / primera . silab / breue. y laul ti / ma luenga. q / quiere dezir ti / en. tienble latie / rra.
|translation=chicume '''uli'''. the first syllab[le] short, and the last one long. which means “[seven] the earth shakes”.}}

====Usage notes====
* Similarly to {{m|nci|cipactli}}, the translation of the day sign ''olīn'' varies. Andrews proposes “quake”, though “movement”, suggested by the root verb {{m|nci|olīnia||to move with difficulty}}, is a more common translation.

====Related terms====
* {{l|nci|olīnini}}
* {{l|nci|tlālolīniliztli}}

===References===
* {{cite-book|author=[[w:Rémi Siméon|Rémi Siméon]]|year=1885|title=Diccionario de la lengua náhuatl o mexicana|publisher=Siglo Veintiuno Editores|page=354}}
* {{cite-book|author=Laurette Séjourné|year=1981|title=El pensamiento náhuatl cifrado por los calendarios|publisher=Siglo Veintiuno Editores|page=32}}

==Estonian==

===Verb===
{{head|et|verb form}}

# {{inflection of|et|olema||1|s|past|indc}}

==Finnish==

===Verb===
