# {{defdate|after 1871}} [[steppe]], [[savanna]], [[prairie]]

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ja|kusahara}}
{{ja-kanjitab|くさ|わら|yomi=k}}{{ja-kanjitab|くさ|はら|yomi=k}}

Compound of {{compound|ja|sort=くさはら|草|tr1=kusa|t1=[[grass]]|原|tr2=hara|t2=[[wild]] or [[uncultivated]] [[field]], [[plain]], [[flatland]]}}.<ref name="KDJ2"/><ref name="DJR"/><ref name="SMK5"/><ref name="DDJS">{{R:Digital-Daijisen}}</ref><ref name="K">{{R:Kojien}}</ref>

First cited with the ''kusahara'' reading to a text from the late 1500s.<ref name="KDJ2"/>

Occasionally encountered with an alternative reading of ''kusawara''.<ref name="NHK"/>

