Page 1006 ilhuicaatl: -------- begin text --------
{{also|ilhuicatl}}
==Central Nahuatl==

===Noun===
{{head|nhn|noun}}

# [[ocean]]

[[Category:Milpa Alta Central Nahuatl]]

==Classical Nahuatl==
{{was fwotd|nci|2013|October|16}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|nci|ylhuica atl}}, {{l|nci|ylhuicaatl}} {{qualifier|obsolete spellings}}

===Etymology===
Equivalent to {{compound|nci|ilhuicatl|t1=sky|ātl|t2=water}}, because ocean water appears to meet the sky in the horizon.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nci|[iɬ.wiˈka.aːt͡ɬ]}}

===Noun===
{{nci-noun|i|ilhuicaātl}}

# [[sea]], [[ocean]]
#* '''16c''', [[w:Bernardino de Sahagún|Bernardino de Sahagún]], [[w:Florentine Codex|Florentine Codex]], vol. 3. f. 223r. col. 1.
#*: […] llamase tan bien &nbsp;'''ylhuicaatl''' / que quiere dezir agua, que se iunto / conel cielo. Porque los antiguos habi / tadores deſta tierra, pensauan que / elcielo se iunta conel agua enlamar, como ſi fuese una casa, queel agua / ſon las paredes : yel cielo eſta sobre / las. Y poreſto llaman alamar '''ylhui''' / '''caatl''', como si dixesen, agua que se / iunta con el cielo […]
#*:: […] it [the sea] is also called &nbsp;'''ylhuicaatl''', which means "water that joined with the sky", because the ancient inhabitants of this land thought that the sky joined the water in the sea, as if it were a house, where the water is the walls and the sky is above them, and because of this they call the sea '''ylhuicaatl''', as if saying "water that joins with the sky" […]
#* {{quote-book|nci|year=1555|author=w:Alonso de Molina|title=[[w:Aquí comiença un vocabulario en la lengua castellana y mexicana|Aqui comienca vn vocabulario en la lengua castellana y mexicana]]|section=f. 164v
|passage=Mar generalmente. uey atl.'''ylhuica atl'''.
|translation=The sea in general. uey atl.'''ylhuica atl'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|nci|year=1571|author=w:Alonso de Molina|title=w:Vocabulario en lengua castellana y mexicana y mexicana y castellana|section=f. 82r. col. 1
|passage=Mar generalmente. vey atl. '''ylhuica atl'''.
|translation=The sea in general. vey atl. '''ylhuica atl'''.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|nci|huey atl|huey ātl}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|nci|ilhuicaatentli|ilhuicaātēntli}}

===References===
* {{cite-book|author=J. Richard Andrews|year=2003|title=Workbook for Introduction to Classical Nahuatl, Revised Edition|publisher=University of Oklahoma Press|page=229}}

[[Category:Classical Nahuatl terms using regularized orthography]]
[[Category:nci:Geography]]
[[Category:nci:Nature]]
