==Classical Nahuatl==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|nci|tepētl|olōlli|t1=mountain|t2=ball, sphere}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nci|[te.peː.oˈloː.lːi]}}

===Noun===
{{nci-noun|a|tepēolōlli}}

# [[round]]ed [[mountain]] or [[hill]]; [[mound]]
#* {{quote-book|nci|year=1555|author=w:Alonso de Molina|title=[[w:Aquí comiença un vocabulario en la lengua castellana y mexicana|Aqui comienca vn vocabulario en la lengua castellana y mexicana]]|section=f. 63v
|passage=Cerro redondo. &nbsp;'''tepeololli'''. tepeyaualli.
|translation=A rounded mountain. &nbsp;'''tepeololli'''. tepeyaualli.}}
#* {{quote-book|nci|year=1571|author=w:Alonso de Molina|title=w:Vocabulario en lengua castellana y mexicana y mexicana y castellana|section=f. 34v. col. 1
|passage=Cerro redondo. tepeyaualli. '''tepeololli'''.
|translation=A rounded mountain. tepeyaualli. '''tepeololli'''.}}
#* ''Idem'', f. 102v. col. 1.
#*: Tepeyaualli. cerro redondo. […] / '''Tepeololli'''. lo meſmo es que tepeyaualli.
#*:: Tepeyaualli. a rounded mountain. […] / '''Tepeololli'''. it is the same thing as tepeyaualli.

