==Classical Syriac==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|syc|sem-pro|*ʔuḏn-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical Edessan}} {{IPA|syc|[ˈʔɛð.nɑ]}}
* {{a|Eastern Syriac}} {{IPA|syc|[ˈʔɪð.nɑ]}}
* {{a|Western Syriac}} {{IPA|syc|[ˈʔeð.no]}}

===Noun===
{{syc-noun|tr=ʾeḏnā|f|ܐܕܢܗܬܐ|ܐܕܢܬܐ|ܐܕܢܐ|pltr=ʾeḏnē|pltr2=ʾeḏnāṯā|pltr3=ʾeḏnāhāṯā}}

# {{lb|syc|anatomy}} [[ear]]
#* [[Peshitta]], [[Matthew]] 11:15:
#*: {{quote|syc|ܡܢ ܕܐܝܬ ܠܗ '''ܐܕ̈ܢܐ''' ܕܢܫܡܥ ܢܫܡܥ.|tr=man də-ʾīṯ lēh '''ʾeḏnē''' ḏə-nešmaʿ nešmaʿ.|He that hath '''ears''' to hear, let him hear.}}
# {{lb|syc|animal anatomy}} [[fish]] [[gill]]
# {{lb|syc|figuratively}} anything that sticks out; [[handle]], [[promontory]], [[bay]], [[gulf]]
# [[bottle]] [[opening]]
# {{lb|syc|by extension}} bottle

====Usage notes====
Usually, the plural {{m|syc|ܐܕܢܐ|tr=ʾeḏnē}} is used for literal senses while {{m|syc|ܐܕܢܬܐ|tr=ʾeḏnāṯā}} and {{m|syc|ܐܕܢܗܬܐ|tr=ʾeḏnāhāṯā}} are used for figurative senses.

