==Classical Syriac==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|syc|sem-pro|*kanap-}}. Compare {{cog|ar|كَنَف|tr=kanaf}} and {{cog|he|כָּנָף|tr=kānāp̄}}. The sense of "pterygium" is a {{sl|syc|grc|πτερύγιον|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|syc|[kɛn(ə)fɑ(ʔ)]}} {{a|singular}}
* {{IPA|syc|[kɛn(ə)fe(ʔ)]|[kɛn(ə)fɑθɑ(ʔ)]}} {{a|plural}}

===Noun===
{{syc-noun|f|ܟܢܦܬܐ|ܟܢܦܐ}}

# [[side]], [[edge]], [[border]], [[outer]] [[part]]
# [[wing]]
# {{lb|syc|anatomy}} [[lap]], [[bosom]], [[arm]]s
# {{lb|syc|sewing}} [[flap]], [[hem]]; [[skirt]], [[cloak]]
# {{lb|syc|geography}} [[bay]], [[gulf]]
# [[covering]], [[overshadowing]], [[protection]]
# [[pinnacle]], [[peak]]
# {{lb|syc|architecture}} [[battlement]], [[merlon]]
