Page 1031 ܠܫܢܐ: -------- begin text --------
==Assyrian Neo-Aramaic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|aii|arc|לִשָּׁנָא|tr=liššānā}}, from {{inh|aii|sem-pro|*lišān-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Standard}} {{IPA|aii|[lɪʃˈʃɑːnɑː]}}

===Noun===
{{aii-noun|ܠܸܫܵܢܵܐ|m|pl=ܠܸܫܵܢܹ̈ܐ}}

# {{lb|aii|anatomy}} [[tongue]]
#: {{ux|aii|'''ܠܸܫܵܢܹܗ''' ܐܲܪܝܼܟ݂ܵܐ|t=He talks back; He bickers|lit='''His tongue''' is long.}}
# {{lb|aii|linguistics}} [[language]]
#: {{ux|aii|ܥܸܠܬܵܐ ܕܐܵܗܵܐ ܢܲܫܝܼܫܘܼܬܵܐ، ܝܼܠܵܗ̇ ܠܲܝܬܵܝܘܼܬܵܐ ܕܩܸܢܛܪ̈ܘܿܢܹܐ ܕܡܲܠܘܿܦܹܐ ܠܸܫܵܢܵܐ ܕܥܲܡܹܗ.|t=The reason for this weakness, is the non-existence of centres for teaching the language of his people.}}
#* [[Acts]] 2:6:
#*: {{quote|aii|ܐܝܼܡܲܢ ܕܫܡܝܼܥ ܠܗܘܿܢ ܠܗ̇ܘ ܩܵܠܵܐ، ܓ̰ܡܝܼܥ ܠܹܗ ܟܠܹܗ ܟܸܢܫܵܐ ܘܫܓ݂ܝܼܫ ܠܹܗ ܣܵܒܵܒ ܟܠ ܚܲܕ݇ ܡܸܢܵܝܗܝ ܫܡܝܼܥ ܠܹܗ ܐܸܠܵܝܗܝ ܗܲܡܙܘܼܡܹܐ '''ܒܠܸܫܵܢܵܐ''' ܕܓܵܢܹܗ|t=Now when this was noised abroad, the multitude came together, and were confounded, because that every man heard them speak '''in the language''' of his own.}}

====Declension====
{{aii-infl-noun-m|ܠܸܫܵܢ}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|aii|ܒܠܸܫܵܢܵܐ|t=through peaceful talk}}

{{c|aii|Language}}

==Classical Syriac==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|syc|sem-pro|*lišān-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical Edessan}} {{IPA|syc|[lɛʃˈʃɑ.nɑ]}}
* {{a|Eastern Syriac}} {{IPA|syc|[lɪʃˈʃɑ.nɑ]}}
* {{a|Western Syriac}} {{IPA|syc|[leˈʃo.no]}}

===Noun===
{{syc-noun|tr=leššānā|m|ܠܫܢܐ|pltr=leššānē}}

# {{lb|syc|anatomy}} [[tongue]]
# {{lb|syc|phonetics}} [[pronunciation]], [[articulation]]
# {{lb|syc|linguistics}} [[language]], [[speech]]
#* [[Peshitta]], [[Acts]] 2:6:
#*: {{quote|syc|ܘܟܕ ܗܘܐ ܩܠܐ ܗܘ. ܟܢܫ ܟܠܗ ܥܡܐ ܘܐܫܬܓܫ. ܡܛܠ ܕܫܡܥ ܗܘܐ ܐܢܫ ܐܢܫ ܡܢܗܘܢ ܕܡܡܠܠܝܢ ܗܘܘ ܒ'''ܠܫ̈ܢܝܗܘܢ.'''|tr=wə-ḵaḏ həwā qālā haw, kənaš kollēh ʿammā wə-ʾeštəḡeš, meṭṭol də-šāmaʿ [hə]wā [ʾ]nāš [ʾ]nāš menhōn da-məmalləlīn [hə]waw bə-'''leššānayhōn'''.|Now when this was noised abroad, the multitude came together, and were confounded, because that every man heard them speak in '''his own language'''.}}
# [[nation]], [[people]]
# [[judgement]]
# {{lb|syc|figuratively|geography}} [[narrow]] [[stretch]] of [[land]] or [[water]]; [[isthmus]], [[channel]]
# tongue-[[shaped]] [[ornament]]; [[wedge]]

====Inflection====
{{syc-decl-noun-m|ܠܫܢ}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|l$n|N|date=2011-11-04}}
* {{R:Costaz 1963|page=174b}}
* {{R:Payne Smith 1902|page=245a-b}}
* {{R:Sokoloff 2009|page=698a-b}}

{{c|syc|Language}}
