==Classical Syriac==

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{syc-root-entry|ܕ|ܒ|ܪ}}. Compare {{cog|akk|𒆳𒁀𒊒|ts=madbaru|t=desert, wilderness, steppe, hinterlands; Arabia}} and {{cog|he|מִדְבָּר|tr=miḏbār}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|syc|[maðb(ə)rɑ(ʔ)]}} {{qualifier|singular}}
* {{IPA|syc|[maðb(ə)re(ʔ)]}} {{qualifier|plural}}

====Noun====
{{syc-noun|m|ܡܕܒܪܐ|tr=maḏbrā}}

# [[desert]], [[wilderness]]
# [[steppe]]

=====Inflection=====
{{syc-decl-noun-m|ܡܕܒܪ}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|syc|ܡܕܒܪܝܐ}}
* {{l|syc|ܡܕܒܪܢܝܐ}}

===Etymology 2===
From the root {{syc-root-entry|ܕ|ܒ|ܪ}} related to leading. Compare {{cog|he|מְדַבֵּר|tr=məḏabbēr}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|syc|[m(ə)ðavrɑ(ʔ)]}} {{qualifier|singular}}
* {{IPA|syc|[m(ə)ðavre(ʔ)]}} {{qualifier|plural}}

====Noun====
{{syc-noun|m|ܡܕܒܪܐ}}

# [[leader]], [[guide]]

=====Inflection=====
{{syc-decl-noun-m|ܡܕܒܪ}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|mdbr}}
* {{R:Costaz 1963}}, p. 58a
* {{R:Payne Smith 1902}}, p. 251b
* {{R:Sokoloff 2009}}, p. 712a

