Page 1033 ܡܘܪܐ: -------- begin text --------
==Classical Syriac==

===Etymology 1===
Ultimately from a Semitic source, possibly via {{bor|syc|grc|μύρρᾱ}}. Compare {{cog|ar|مُرّ|tr=murr}} and {{cog|he|מור|מֹר|tr=mōr}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|syc|[mu(r)rɑ]}}

====Noun====
{{syc-noun-unc|m|tr=murrā}}

# [[myrrh]]

=====Inflection=====
{{syc-decl-noun-unc-m|ܡܘܪ}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|syc|grc|μόρον}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|syc|[morɑ]}} {{qualifier|singular}}
* {{IPA|syc|[more]}} {{qualifier|plural}}

====Noun====
{{syc-noun|f|ܡܘܪܐ|tr=mōrā|pltr=mōrē}}

# ''[[morus]]'', [[mulberry]] [[tree]]

=====Inflection=====
{{syc-decl-noun-m|ܡܘܪ}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{bor|syc|grc|μοῖρα}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|syc|[murɑ]}}

====Noun====
{{syc-noun|f|ܡܪܣ|ܡܝܪܣ|ܡܘܪܐܣ|ܡܘܪܣ|tr=mūrā}}

# [[step]], [[stage]], [[level]]
# {{lb|syc|geometry|geography|astronomy}} [[degree]] (of a [[circle]], of [[longitude]]/[[latitude]], of a [[star]], etc.)
# [[share]], [[portion]]

===Etymology 4===
From {{bor|syc|grc|Μοῖρα}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|syc|[murɑ]}}

====Proper noun====
{{head|syc|proper noun|tr=mūrā|g=f}}

# {{lb|syc|Greek mythology}} [[Moera]], [[Fate]]

===References===
* {{R:CAL|mwr}}
* {{R:CAL|mwr%232|N}}
* {{R:Costaz 1963|page=190b}}
* {{R:Payne Smith 1902|page=259a}}
* {{R:Sokoloff 2009|page=729a}}

