==Old Irish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sga|/r͈os/}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|sga|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}
From {{inh|sga|cel-pro|*ɸrossos}}, from {{der|sga|ine-pro|*pro-||before}} + {{m|ine-pro|*steh₂-||to stand}}. The same construction as {{cog|sa|प्रस्थ||plateau}}, but probably coined separately in the two languages.<ref>{{R:cel:Matasovic 2009|page=142}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{sga-noun|m|ruis|ruis}}

# A {{l|en|promontory}}.
# A {{l|en|wood}}.
#* {{RQ:sga-Corm|Y|1079}}
#*: {{lang|sga|'''ross''' .i. trēde fordingair .i. '''ros''' fidbuide, {{...}}}}
#*:: '''wood''', that is, a triad of meanings, that is, a wood of yellow trees, {{...}}

=====Inflection=====
{{sga-decl-o-masc|ruis|dat_sg=rus|acc_pl=rusu}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|ga|ros|t=wood}}
* {{desc|gd|ros|t=promontory}}

===Etymology 2===
Possibly from {{der|sga|ine-pro|*pr̥so-}}, which is most likely a borrowing from a non-Indo-European language. See also {{cog|la|porrum|t=leek}}, {{cog|en|furze}}, and possibly {{cog|grc|πράσον|t=leek}}.<ref>{{R:MacBain|ros|}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{sga-noun|m|ruis|ruis}}

# A {{l|en|linseed}}.
#* {{RQ:sga-Corm|Y|1079}}
#*: {{lang|sga|'''ros''' līn}}
#*:: linseed
# A [[flax]] - or other small [[seed]].

