==French==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|fr|fro|pas}}, from {{inh|fr|la|passus}}.

Its use as an auxiliary negative adverb comes from an accusative use ({{cog|la|[[nec]]… [[passum]]}}) in negative constructions – literally “not… a step”, i.e. “not at all” – originally used with certain verbs of motion. In older French other nouns could also be used in this way, such as {{m|fr|ne… [[goutte]]||not… a drop}} and {{m|fr|ne… [[mie]]||not… a crumb}}, but in the modern language {{m|fr||pas}} has become {{w|Grammaticalization|grammaticalised}}.

