===Adverb===
{{fr-adv}}

# {{n-g|The most common adverb of negation in French, typically translating into English as [[not]], [[don't]], [[doesn't]], etc.}}
#: {{ux|fr|Je ne sais '''pas'''.|I don't know}}
#: {{ux|fr|Ma grande sœur n'habite '''pas''' avec nous.|My big sister '''doesn't''' live with us.}}
#: {{ux|fr|J’veux '''pas''' travailler.|I don't wanna work.|footer=(Je '''ne''' veux '''pas''' travailler)}}

====Usage notes====
* The adverb of negation '''{{m|fr||pas}}''' is normally used in conjunction with the particle {{m|fr|ne}}, as in the examples {{m|fr||Je '''ne''' sais '''pas'''}} and {{m|fr||Ma grande sœur '''n’'''habite '''pas''' avec nous}} above. In colloquial language, {{m|fr||ne}} can be dropped, as in the example {{m|fr||J'veux '''pas''' travailler}} above.
* Word order:<ref>{{R:fr:TLFi}}</ref>
** '''{{m|fr||Pas}}''' directly follows the inflected verb, which itself follows the particle {{m|fr|ne}};
**: {{uxi|fr|Il ne <u>mange</u> '''pas'''.|He's not eating.}}
**: {{uxi|fr|Ne le <u>touchez</u> '''pas'''.|Don't touch him.}}
** in compound verb structures it is placed between the inflected auxiliary and the participle.
**: {{uxi|fr|Il n'<u>a</u> '''pas''' <u>mangé</u>.|He didn't eat.}}
** When negating an infinitive verb, '''{{m|fr||pas}}''' normally follows {{m|fr|ne}} and precedes that verb in the construction {{m|fr||ne '''pas'''}} + infinitive (though the sequence {{m|fr|ne}} + infinitive + '''{{m|fr||pas}}''' was common in the Classical French of the 17th and 18th centuries).
**: {{uxi|fr|Il a reçu une leçon à <u>ne '''pas''' oublier</u>.|He received a lesson not to be forgotten.}}
** {{m|fr||pas}} can be placed before an adverb that modifies all or part of a verbal syntagma, but it directly follows an adverb that modifies the whole sentence.
**: {{uxi|fr|Je n'ai <u>'''pas''' vraiment</u> compris.|I didn't truly understand.}}
**: {{uxi|fr|Il n'est <u>probablement '''pas'''</u> arrivé.|He probably hasn't arrived.}}
** Certain adverbs (e.g. {{m|fr|même}}) can be used before or after '''{{m|fr||pas}}''' without affecting the meaning of the phrase. With other adverbs (e.g. {{m|fr|toujours}}), there may be considerable difference in meaning depending on whether '''{{m|fr||pas}}''' comes before or after.
**: {{uxi|fr|'''pas''' toujours|not always}}
**: {{uxi|fr|toujours '''pas'''|still not}}

====Synonyms====
