Borrowed from {{bor|id|nl|passend}}, {{m|nl|pas}}, from {{der|id|dum|pas}}, {{m|dum|passen}}, from {{der|id|fro|pas}}, from {{der|id|la|passus}}, {{m|la|pandere||to spread, unfold, stretch}}, from {{der|id|ine-pro|*patno-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*pete-||to spread, stretch out}}.
* Sense of "to [[pass]], to achieve a successful outcome from" is {{sl|id|ms|pas|nocap=1}} or {{sl|id|en|pass|notext=1}} which both are cognate of above.

====Noun====
{{id-noun|pl=pas-pas}}

# {{l|en|pass}}, permission or license to pass, or to go and come
# {{l|en|mountain pass}}

