==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Dunau|Tonau|Dhonau|Thonau|Donaw|Dunaw|Dhonaw|Tonaw|Tunaw|Thonaw|Thunaw||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Attested in this form at least since 1544. From earlier {{m|de|Donaw}} (since 1530s, ''D'' under Low German influence), from earlier {{m|de|Tonaw}} (since late 15th c., ''o'' possibly also under Low German influence), from {{der|de|gmh|Tuonawe}}, perhaps under Slavic influence from earlier {{m|gmh|Tuonowe}}, {{m|gmh|Tuonow}}, from {{der|de|goh|Tuonouwa}}, from something like {{der|de|gmw-pro||*Dōnauwju}} (cf. {{cog|gml|Dônouwe}}, {{m|gml|Dônouw}}), from {{der|de|gem-pro|*Dōnawjaz}} paretymologically attracted to {{m|gmw-pro|*auwju||floodplain, meadow}}, from {{der|de|cel-pro|*Dānowyos}}, an extended form of the river-name {{m|cel-pro|*Dānu}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*déh₂nu||river goddess}}, akin to {{m|ine-pro|*dʰenh₂-||to set in motion; to flow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|de|De-at-Donau.ogg|Audio (Austria)}}
* {{audio|de|De-Donau.ogg|Audio}}

