Page 1165 geography: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{wikiversity}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|frm|géographie}}, from {{uder|en|la|geōgraphia}}, from {{uder|en|grc|γεωγραφία||a [[description]] of the [[earth]]}}, from {{m|grc|γῆ||[[earth]]}} + {{m|grc|γράφω||[[write]]}}.

Use in reference to lavatories derives from the mid-20th century euphemism "show one the geography of the house" in reference to pointing out the toilets.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/dʒɪˈɒɡɹəfi/|/ˈdʒɒɡɹəfi/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/d͡ʒiˈɑɡɹəfi/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-geography.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ge|og|ra|phy}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒɡɹəfi|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[description]] of the [[earth]]: a [[treatise]] or [[textbook]] on geography
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|year=2021
|author=w:Mark Steyn
|title=Our Increasingly Unrecognizable Civilization
|journal=w:Imprimis
|publisher=w:Hillsdale College
|volume=50
|issue=4/5
|issn=0277-8432
|oclc=3890282
|page=3
|text=These days, instead of going off behind the bike shed during recess to learn about sex, kids need to sneak behind the bike shed to do a little bit of closeted '''geography''' or closeted Latin.}}
# {{label|en|archaic}} an [[atlas]] or [[gazetteer]].
# The [[study]] of the [[physical]] [[properties]] of the [[earth]], [[including]] [[how]] [[human]]s [[affect]] and are [[affect]]ed by [[them]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:geography}}
# [[terrain|Terrain]]: the [[physical]] [[properties]] of a [[region]] of the [[earth]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1973|author=Helen Miller Bailey; Abraham Phineas Nasatir|title=Latin America: the development of its civilization
|passage=The '''geography''' of the Andes approaches never made transportation easy; routes to Bogota, Quito, La Paz, and Cuzco were so precipitous as to slow down the development of those Spanish cities in the interior.}}
# [[any|Any]] [[subject]] [[consider]]ed in [[term]]s of its [[physical]] [[distribution]].
# {{label|en|astronomy}} [[similar|Similar]] [[book]]s, [[studies]], or [[region]]s [[concern]]ing [[other]] [[planet]]s.
# The [[physical]] [[arrangement]] of [[any]] [[place]], ''[[particularly]]'' {{label|en|UK|slang}} a [[house]].
# {{label|en|chiefly|_|upper-class|_|UK|euphemism}} The [[lavatory]]: a [[room]] [[use]]d for [[urination]] and [[defecation]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 21 1967|journal=The Listener|page=802
|passage=The Business Man Jocular: ‘I say, where's the [[geography]], old son?’}}
# {{label|en|figuratively}} The [[relative]] [[arrangement]] of the [[part]]s of [[anything]].
# {{label|en|chiefly|_|business|_|&|_|marketing}} A [[territory]]: a [[geographical]] [[area]] as a [[field]] of [[business]] or [[market]] [[sector]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|upper-class British slang for lavatory}} {{l|en|loo}}; ''see also'' '''[[Thesaurus:bathroom]]'''

