Page 1188 antimeridian: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Antimeridian}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|180th meridian}}
[[File:Earth_map_with_180th_meridian.jpg|thumb|Greenwich '''antimeridian''' at 180° longitude]]

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|anti|meridian}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|geography}} The [[reference]] [[line]] at 180° [[longitude]], on the opposite side of earth to the [[prime meridian]].
#: {{syn|en|Greenwich antimeridian}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Simon Guerrier; Dr. Marek Kukula|title=The Scientific Secrets of Doctor Who|publisher=Random House|isbn=9781448142972|text=On the opposite side of the Earth from Greenwich is the '''antimeridian''', a line of longitude that is 180° both east and west of the prime meridian. It cuts through parts of eastern Russia, the Fiji Islands and the middle of the Pacific Ocean.}}
# {{lb|en|geography}} A [[meridian]] of longitude opposite to any given meridian used as a point of reference.
#: {{ux|en|123° west is the '''antimeridian''' of the 57° east meridian.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=William Millar|title=The Amateur Astronomer's Introduction to the Celestial Sphere|publisher=Cambridge University Press|isbn=9780521671231|page=24|text=The '''antimeridian''' contains your nadir and the opposite celestial pole for your hemisphere. The local meridian and the '''antimeridian''' together form the great circle simply called the meridian.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Charles W. J. Withers|title=Zero Degrees: Geographies of the Prime Meridian|year=2017|publisher=Harvard University Press|page=183|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=_v1aDgAAQBAJ&lpg=PA211&dq=%22antimeridian%22&hl=es&pg=PA183#v=onepage&q&f=false|isbn=978-0-674-08881-8|passage=Other prime meridians were presented as candidates for the world's baseline: Jersualem; Ferro; Kamchatka; the mid-Atlantic; the Bering Strait; and Greenwich's '''antimeridian'''.}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|antipode}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|the reference line at 180° longitude, on the opposite side of earth to the prime meridian}}
* Catalan: {{t|ca|antimeridià|m}}
* French: {{t+|fr|antiméridien|m}}
* German: {{t|de|Antimeridian|m}}
