From {{uder|en|la|-}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἀντίποδες}}, from {{m|grc|ἀντί||opposite}} + {{m|grc|πόδες}}, plural of {{m|grc|πούς||foot}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ænˈtɪp.əˌdiz/}}<ref name="Dict.com">{{R:Dictionary.com}}</ref><!--{{R:MWO}}: {{IPAchar|/ænˈtɪ.pəˌdiz/|lang=en}}-->

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The [[place]] on the [[diametrically]] [[opposite]] [[side]] of the [[earth]] from a given point.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|V|1|text=We should hold day with the '''Antipodes''',<br>If you would walk in absence of the sun.}}
# The [[Southern Hemisphere]].
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|I|passage={{...}}a delighted shout from the children swung him toward the door again. His sister, Mrs. Gerard, stood there in carriage gown and sables, radiant with surprise. &para; "Phil!&nbsp; ''You!''&nbsp; Exactly like you, Philip, to come strolling in from the '''antipodes'''&mdash;dear fellow!" recovering from the fraternal embrace and holding both lapels of his coat in her gloved hands.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|now|rare}} [[Australia]] and [[New Zealand]].
# {{lb|en|figuratively|by extension}} The opposite of something.
#* {{RQ:Landon Romance|page=295|volume=III|passage=The sleepy yet shrewd judge was the '''antipodes''' to confidence, but to Don Manuel he felt no hesitation in frankly stating his actions and their motives, from his first arrival in Spain to the present time.}}
