===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{enPR|äm}}, {{IPA|en|/ɑːm/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|ärm}}, {{IPA|en|/ɑɹm/}}
* {{a|AU}} {{enPR|äm}}, {{IPA|en|/ɐːm/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-arm.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑː(ɹ)m|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂er-}}
From {{inh-lite|en|enm|arm}}, from {{inh-lite|en|ang|sc=Latnx|earm}}, from {{inh-lite|en|gmw-pro|sc=Latnx|*arm}}, from {{inh-lite|en|gem-pro|sc=Latnx|*armaz||arm}}, from {{inh-lite|en|ine-pro|sc=Latnx|*h₂r̥mós|*h₂(e)rmos|a fitting, joint; arm, forequarter}}, a suffixed form of {{m-lite|ine-pro|sc=Latnx|*h₂er-||to join, fit together}}.
{{rel-top|cognates}}
Akin to {{cog-lite|nl|arm}}, {{cog-lite|de|Arm}}, {{cog-lite|yi|sc=Hebr|אָרעם|tr=orem}}, {{cog-lite|da|-}}, {{cog-lite|no|-}} and {{cog-lite|sv|arm}}. Indo-European cognates include {{cog-lite|la|armus||the uppermost part of the arm, shoulder}}, {{cog-lite|hy|sc=Armn|արմունկ||tr=armunk|elbow}}, {{cog-lite|grc|sc=Polyt|ἁρμός||tr=harmós|joint, shoulder}} and {{m-lite|grc|sc=Polyt|ἅρμα||tr=hárma|wagon, chariot}}, {{cog-lite|ae|sc=Avst|𐬀𐬭𐬨𐬀|tr=arma}}, {{cog-lite|peo|tr=arma}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The portion of the upper human [[appendage]], from the [[shoulder]] to the [[wrist]] and sometimes including the [[hand]].
#: {{ux|en|She stood with her right '''arm''' extended and her [[palm]] forward to indicate “Stop!”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1963|author=w:Margery Allingham|title=w:The China Governess
|chapter=19|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL2004261W
|passage=When Timothy and Julia hurried up the staircase to the bedroom floor, where a considerable commotion was taking place, Tim took Barry Leach with him. He had him gripped firmly by the '''arm''', since he felt it was not safe to let him loose, and he had no immediate idea what to do with him.}}
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The extended portion of the upper [[limb]], from the [[shoulder]] to the [[elbow]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''arm''' and forearm are parts of the upper limb in the human body.}}
# A [[limb]], or [[locomotive#Adjective|locomotive]] or [[prehensile]] [[organ]], of an [[invertebrate]] animal.
#: {{ux|en|the '''arms''' of an octopus}}
# The part of a piece of clothing that covers the arm.
#: {{syn|en|sleeve}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|page=485|[https://archive.org/details/mobydickorwhale01melv/page/485/mode/1up?q=%22arm+of+this%22 Chapter 100]|text={{...}} one '''arm''' of this jacket streamed behind him like the [[broider]]ed '''arm''' of a [[hussar|huzzar]]’s [[surcoat]].}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1970|author=w:J. G. Farrell|title={{w|Troubles (novel)|Troubles}}|url=https://archive.org/details/troubles00jgfa/page/340/mode/1up?q=%22arm+of+her%22|page=340|publisher=Knopf|year_published=1971|location=New York
|passage={{...}} he noticed that a dark stain had appeared under the '''arm''' of her grey silk dress.}}
#* {{RQ:Smith White Teeth|chapter=5|page=82|passage=Samad made a grab for the boy and caught him by the '''arm''' of his shirt.}}
# A long, [[narrow]], more or less [[rigid]] part of an object [[extend]]ing from the main part or centre of the object, such as the arm of an [[armchair]], a [[crane]], a pair of [[spectacles]] or a [[pair of compasses]].
#: {{ux|en|The robot '''arm''' reached out and placed the part on the assembly line.}}
# {{lb|en|geography}} A [[bay]] or [[inlet]] off a main body of water.
#: {{ux|en|Shelburne Bay is an '''arm''' of Lake Champlain.}}
# A [[branch]] of an [[organization]].
#: {{ux|en|the cavalry '''arm''' of the military service}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2018-04-25|author=w:Ron Nixon|title=Scandals and Investigations, but Few Arrests, for Air Marshals Program|journal=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/25/us/politics/air-marshals-scandals-investigations.html|passage=Congress has asked the Government Accountability Office, its investigative '''arm''', to review the workplace complaints raised by air marshals, said Charles Young, a spokesman for the office.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Power; might; strength; support.
#: {{ux|en|the '''arm''' of the law}}
#: {{ux|en|the secular '''arm'''}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Isaiah|52|1|passage=To whom is the '''arm''' of the Lord revealed?}}
# {{lb|en|baseball|slang}} A [[pitcher]]
#: {{ux|en|The team needs to sign another '''arm''' in the offseason.}}
# {{lb|en|genetics}} One of the two parts of a [[chromosome]].
# A group of patients in a medical trial.

