==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA-lite|en|/bɑː/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{enPR|bär}}, {{IPA-lite|en|/bɑɹ/|[bɑɹ]|[bɑ˞]}}
* {{a|AU}} {{IPA-lite|en|/baː/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-bar.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-baa.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑː(ɹ)|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|baa|bah}} {{qualifier|in some pronunciations}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh-lite|en|enm|barre}}, from {{der-lite|en|fro|barre||beam, bar, gate, barrier}}, from {{der-lite|en|VL.|*barra}}, of uncertain origin. {{doublet|en|barre}}.

====Noun====
{{head-lite|en|nouns|{{glossary|countable}} and {{glossary|uncountable}}||plural|bars}} <!-- {{en-noun|~}} -->

[[File:Bar square steel.jpg|thumb|right|upright=1.25|Two steel bars]]
[[File:A_toll_bar_in_Roumania,_1877.jpg|thumb|right|upright=1.25|A toll bar in Romania]]

# A [[solid]], more or less [[rigid]] object of metal or wood with a uniform [[cross-section]] smaller than its [[length]].
#: {{ux-lite|en|The window was protected by steel '''bars'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable|metallurgy}} A solid metal object with uniform ([[round]], [[square]], [[hexagonal]], [[octagonal]] or [[rectangular]]) cross-section; in the US its smallest dimension is {{frac|1|4}} inch or greater, a piece of thinner material being called a [[strip]].
#: {{ux-lite|en|Ancient Sparta used iron '''bars''' instead of handy coins in more valuable alloy, to physically discourage the use of money.}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|We are expecting a carload of '''bar''' tomorrow.}}
# A [[cuboid]] piece of any solid [[commodity]].
#: {{ux-lite|en|'''bar''' of chocolate}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|'''bar''' of soap}}
# A broad [[shaft]], [[band]], or [[stripe]].
#: {{ux-lite|en|a '''bar''' of light}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|a '''bar''' of colour}}
# A long, narrow drawn or printed rectangle, cuboid or cylinder, especially as used in a [[bar code]] or a [[bar chart]].
# {{lb|en|typography}} Any of various [[line]]s used as [[punctuation]] or [[diacritic]]s, such as the [[pipe]] ⟨{{!}}⟩, [[fraction bar]] (as in <span style="display:inline-block; vertical-align:-0.5em; font-size:85%; text-align:center;"><span style="display:block; line-height:1em; margin:0 0.1em;">1</span><span style="display:block; line-height:1em; margin:0 0.1em; border-top:1px solid;">2</span></span>), and [[strikethrough]] (as in Ⱥ), [[formerly]] {{label|en|obsolete}} including [[oblique]] [[mark]]s such as the [[slash]].
#: {{hypo|en|pipe|strikethrough|macron}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} The [[sign]] indicating that the [[characteristic]] of a [[logarithm]] is [[negative]], conventionally placed above the digit(s) to show that it applies to the [[characteristic]] only and not to the [[mantissa]].
# {{lb|en|physics}} A similar sign indicating that the [[charge]] on a [[particle]] is the [[negative]] of its usual value (and that consequently the particle is in fact an [[antiparticle]]).
# {{senseid|en|pub}} A [[business]] selling [[alcoholic]] [[drink]]s for consumption on the premises, or the premises themselves; a [[public house]].
#: {{syn|en|barroom|ginshop|pub|q3=British|public house|tavern|Thesaurus:pub}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|The street was lined with all-night '''bars'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|counter}} The [[counter]] of such premises.
#: {{syn|en|wet bar}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|Step up to the '''bar''' and order a drink.}}
# A counter, or simply a [[cabinet]], from which alcoholic drinks are served in a private house or a hotel room.
# {{lb|en|by extension|in combinations such as {{m-lite|en|coffee bar}}, {{m-lite|en|juice bar}}, etc.}} Premises or a counter serving any type of beverage.
# An [[establishment]] where [[alcohol]] and sometimes other [[refreshments]] are [[serve]]d.
# An [[informal]] establishment selling [[food]] to be [[consume]]d on the premises.
#: {{ux-lite|en|a burger '''bar'''}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|a local fish '''bar'''}}
# An establishment offering [[cosmetic]] services.
#: {{ux-lite|en|a nail '''bar'''; a brow '''bar'''}}
# An [[official]] [[order]] or [[pronouncement]] that prohibits some activity.
#: {{syn|en|ban|prohibition}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|The club has lifted its '''bar''' on women members.}}
# Anything that [[obstruct]]s, [[hinder]]s, or [[prevent]]s; an [[obstruction]]; a [[barrier]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aureng-zebe|83|passage=Muſt I new '''bars''' to my own joy create?}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Terence Dillon|title=A Long Way Home|page=184
|passage=Mr Harding could look back on his initial judgement of Paul's talent with great satisfaction while Paul could reflect that to be Irish was not necessarily a '''bar''' to progress.}}
# {{senseid|en|metasyntactic variable}} {{lb|en|programming|derived from {{m-lite|en|fubar}}}} A [[metasyntactic variable]] [[represent]]ing an [[unspecified]] [[entity]], often the second in a series, following {{m-lite|en|foo}}.
#: {{ux-lite|en|Suppose we have four objects, [[foo]], '''bar''', [[baz]] and [[quux]].}}
# {{lb|en|UK|Parliament}} A dividing line (physical or notional) in the [[chamber]] of a [[legislature]] beyond which only [[member]]s and [[official]]s may pass.
# {{lb|en|UK|law}} The [[railing]] surrounding the part of a [[courtroom]] in which the [[judge]]s, [[lawyer]]s, [[defendant]]s and [[witness]]es stay.
# {{lb|en|US|Philippines|law|usually with '''the'''}} The [[bar exam]], the [[legal]] [[licensing]] [[exam]].
#: {{ux-lite|en|He's studying hard to pass '''the Bar''' this time; he's failed it twice before.}}
# {{lb|en|law|metonym|"the Bar"|"the bar"}} Collectively, [[lawyer]]s or the [[legal]] [[profession]]; specifically applied to [[barrister]]s in some countries, but including all lawyers in others.
#: {{ux-lite|en|He was called to '''the bar''', he became a [[barrister]].}}
# {{lb|en|telecommunications|electronics}} One of an array of bar-shaped [[symbol]]s that display the [[level]] of something, such as wireless signal strength or battery life remaining.
#: {{ux-lite|en|I don't have any '''bars''' in the middle of this desert.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} A vertical line across a musical [[staff]] dividing written [[music]] into sections, typically of equal durational value.
# {{lb|en|music}} One of those musical [[section]]s.
#: {{syn|en|measure}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[horizontal]] [[pole]] that must be crossed in the [[high jump]] and [[pole vault]].
# {{lb|en|metaphorical}} Any level of [[achievement]] regarded as a [[challenge]] to be [[overcome]].
# {{lb|en|football|most codes}} The [[crossbar]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 29, 2010
|author=Chris Whyatt
|title=Chelsea 1 - 0 Bolton
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9309542.stm
|page=
|passage=Composed play then saw Sam Ricketts nutmeg Ashley Cole before Taylor whipped a fine curling effort over Petr Cech's '''bar'''.}}
# {{lb|en|backgammon}} The [[central]] [[divider]] between the inner and outer [[table]] of a [[backgammon]] [[board]], where [[stone]]s are placed if they are [[hit]].
# An addition to a [[military]] [[medal]], on account of a subsequent act.
# A [[linear]] [[shoal]]ing [[landform]] feature within a [[body of water]].
# {{lb|en|geography|nautical|hydrology}} A [[ridge]] or [[succession]] of ridges of [[sand]] or other [[substance]], especially a [[formation]] extending across the [[mouth]] of a [[river]] or [[harbor]] or off a [[beach]], and which may [[obstruct]] [[navigation]]. (FM 55-501).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1868|chapter=Route 20: {{smallcaps|London to Tiflis}} {{...}}|title=Handbook for Travellers in Russia, Poland, and Finland|edition=2nd|location=London|publisher=John Murray|page=320|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/gri_33125009080421/page/n337/mode/2up?q=bar|passage=Travellers change at Batoum into a steamer which performs the service between that port and Poti, and which has a less draught of water to enable it to cross the '''bar''' of the river Rion.}}
# {{lb|en|heraldiccharge}} One of the [[ordinary|ordinaries]] in [[heraldry]]; a diminutive of a [[fess]].
#: {{cot|en|barrulet|closet}}
# A [[city]] [[gate]], in some British place names.
#:{{ux-lite|en|Temple '''Bar''', London}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} A [[drill]]ing or [[tamp]]ing [[rod]].
# {{lb|en|mining}} A [[vein]] or [[dike]] crossing a [[lode]].
# {{lb|en|architecture}} A [[gatehouse]] of a [[castle]] or fortified town.
# {{lb|en|farriery}} The part of the [[crust]] of a horse's [[hoof]] which is bent [[inwards]] towards the [[frog]] at the heel on each side, and extends into the centre of the [[sole]].
# {{lb|en|farriery|in the plural}} The space between the [[tusk]]s and [[grinder]]s in the upper [[jaw]] of a [[horse]], in which the [[bit]] is placed.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A measure of [[drug]]s, typically one [[ounce]].
