{{see translation subpage|Verb}}

====Preposition====
{{head-lite|en|prepositions}}

# [[except|Except]], [[other than]], [[besides]].
#: {{syn|en|apart from|barring|except for|excepting|excluding|other than|save|Thesaurus:except}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|He invited everyone to his wedding '''bar''' his ex-wife.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1936|author=w:F.J. Thwaites|title={{w|The Redemption (novel)|The Redemption}}|publisher=H. John Edwards|location=Sydney|chapter=I|page=5|text="I might be a fool," the younger man admitted quietly, "even an idiot, but there's not a person living, '''bar''' you, who possess the courage to call me a weakling, Sir."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2019|month=October|author=Philip Sherratt|title=Midland Main Line upgrade presses on|journal=Modern Railways|page=62|text=These see the overhead wires installed on all '''bar''' the slow lines between Bedford and Wellingborough by next May, with the remaining section completed by August, when the full programme is due to be completed.}}
# {{lb|en|horse racing}} {{non-gloss definition|Denotes the minimum odds offered on other horses not mentioned by name.}}
#: {{ux-lite|en|Leg At Each Corner is at 3/1, Lost My Shirt 5/1, and it's 10/1 '''bar'''.}}

