Page 1214 bay: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Bay|bây|bẫy|bảy|baþ|бау}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|bā}}, {{IPA|en|/beɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-bay.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪ|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|bae}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|baye}}, {{m|enm|baie}}, from {{inh|en|ang|beġ||berry}}, as in {{m|ang|beġbēam||berry-tree}}, conflated with {{der|en|fro|baie}}, from {{der|en|la|bāca||berry}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[berry]].
# ''{{ll|mul|Laurus nobilis}}'', a [[tree]] or [[shrub]] of the family [[Lauraceae]], having dark green leaves and berries.
# [[bay leaf|Bay leaf]], the [[leaf]] of this or certain other species of tree or shrub, used as a herb.
# {{lb|en|in the plural|now|_|rare}} The leaves of this shrub, woven into a [[garland]] used to reward a [[champion]] or [[victor]]; hence, [[fame]], [[victory]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|passage=both you here with many a cursed oth, / Sweare she is yours, and stirre vp bloudie frayes, / To win a willow bough, whilest other weares the '''bayes'''.|4|1}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1771|author=w:John Trumbull|title=On the Vanity of Youthful Expectations
|passage=The patriot's honours and the poet's '''bays'''.}}
# {{lb|en|US|dialect}} A [[tract]] covered with bay trees.
# A kind of [[mahogany]] obtained from {{w|Campeche}} in [[Mexico]].

