* Occitan: {{t|oc|abaiament|m}}, {{t|oc|abaiada|f}}
{{trans-bottom}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[howl]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Fables|Theodore and Honoria
|passage=The hounds at nearer distance hoarsely '''bay'd'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[bark]] at; hence, to follow with barking; to bring or drive to bay.
#: ''to '''bay''' the bear''
#* {{quote-book|en|year=a. 1611| author=w:William Shakespeare| title=w:Cymbeline| section=act 5, scene 5| lines=222–223| passage=Spit, and throw stones, cast mire upon me, set / The dogs o'th' street to '''bay''' me}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To pursue noisily, like a pack of hounds.

