==Turkish==

===Etymology===
From {{der|tr|ota|بای|tr=bay||rich}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*bāy||rich, noble; many, numerous}}.

The meaning “sir, gentleman” was coined during the [[w:Turkish language#Language reform and modern Turkish|language reforms]] to replace {{m|tr|bey}}.<ref>{{R:tr:Nishanyan|bay}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|tr|/ˈbɑj/}}

===Noun===
{{tr-noun|ı|lar}}

# {{lb|tr|countable}} [[gentleman]]
# {{lb|tr|title used for a man}} [[Mr.]]

====Usage notes====
Used as a title, the word is usually capitalized and followed by a person's name, often his [[surname]] or [[full name]] (as in “Bay Ahmet Şık”). This is unlike the more traditional title {{m|tr|bey}}, which is used after a person's name, most commonly just his [[given name]] (as in “Ahmet Bey”).

