Page 1224 Black Sea: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Crimea Laspi Sunset.jpg|thumb|Black Sea in the [[Crimea]]]]

===Etymology===
{{calque|en|ota|قره دكز|tr=Kara Deñiz|t=Black Sea}} (modern {{cog|tr|Karadeniz}}) (from {{m|tr|kara||black, dark; north}} + {{m|tr|deniz||sea}}). Compare {{cog|ru|Чёрное море}}. The Turkish word is derived from the languages of the Near East, which is ultimately from an {{der|en|ira-old}} name: the primary {{noncog|grc|-}} name {{m|grc|Πόντος Ἄξεινος}} (first attested in 462 BC) is a rendering of {{noncog|ira-old}} {{m|ira-pro|*axšáyHnah-|*axšaina-|dark-colored}}. The naming is according to the system in which color names indicated the cardinal points (black [or dark] for north, red for south, white for west, and green or light blue for east); compare {{m|en|Red Sea}}. It is supposedly named as such by the {{w|Achaemenids}}; see ''Iranica'' for details.<ref>http://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/black-sea</ref>

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=The [[black|Black]] [[sea|Sea]]}}

# {{place|inland sea|bound by [[Southeastern Europe]] in the west, [[Eastern Europe]] in the north and northeast, and [[Turkey]] in the south}}.

====Derived terms====
{{col4|en
|Black Sea bottlenose dolphin
}}

