Page 1225 Bohai Bay: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{commonscat}}

===Etymology===
{{partial calque|en|cmn|渤海灣}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper-noun|head=Bohai Bay}}

# {{place|en|One of the three major <<bays>> of the <<sea/Bohai Sea>>, part of the territorial waters of <<c/China>>}}.
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=September 7, 2010
|author=Manuela Zoninsein
|title=Chinese Offshore Development Blows Past U.S.
|journal=w:The New York Times
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220417220635/https://archive.nytimes.com/www.nytimes.com/cwire/2010/09/07/07climatewire-chinese-offshore-development-blows-past-us-47150.html?pagewanted=all
|issn=0362-4331
|oclc=1645522
|section=w:ClimateWire
|url2=https://archive.is/S1e5T
|text=As of March this year, pipelines accommodating 17 MW were already installed between Donghai and a pilot wind project in '''Bohai Bay''' near Tianjin.}}
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=July 27, 2015
|title=China accepts group’s case against ConocoPhillips, CNOOC
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220614215823/https://apnews.com/article/79e7db67ddbe4aa7b012bc2377a23989
|archivedate=14 June 2022
|work=w:AP News
|text=In 2012, ConocoPhillips and CNOOC reached a $160 million agreement with the Ministry of Agriculture to settle compensation claims related to the spill. ConocoPhillips also said it would help pay for social projects in '''Bohai Bay''' and reduce pollutants in the bay.}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|bay}}
* Chinese:
*: Mandarin: {{t+|cmn|渤海灣}}
* Japanese: {{t-needed|ja}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===See also===
* {{l|en|Bohai Sea}}

===Further reading===
* {{cite-book|en|year=2008|chapter=Bohai or Bohai Bay|editor={{w|Saul B. Cohen}}|title=The Columbia Gazetteer of the World|url=https://archive.org/details/columbiagazettee0000unse_l7h3/|edition=2nd|volume=1|location=[[New York]]|publisher={{w|Columbia University Press}}|isbn=978-0-231-14554-1|lccn=2008009181|oclc=212893637|page=466|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/columbiagazettee0000unse_l7h3/page/466/|column=1}}
-------- end text --------
Page 1226 Bohai Sea: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{commonscat}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Pohai Sea}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|cmn|渤海|tr=Bóhǎi}} + {{m|en|sea}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=Bohai [[sea|Sea]]}}

# {{place|marginal sea|on the east coast of|c/China}}.
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=JUNE 22, 2009
|title=Oil slicks poisoning China's Bohai Sea - official
|editor=Emma Graham-Harrison
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220514170118/https://www.reuters.com/article/china-environment-idINPEK4801920090622
|archivedate=14 May 2022
|work=w:Reuters
|section=Oil Report
|text='''Bohai Sea''' is on the northeastern coast of China, bounded by Liaodong and Shandong Peninsulas, so pollution there is slow to wash out to the ocean, exacerbating damage to local marine life.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=August 22, 2019
|author=w:Jane Perlez
|title=At Mao’s Beach, China’s Leaders Still Make History as Lifeguards Hide From the Sun
|journal=w:The New York Times
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190822091113/https://www.nytimes.com/2019/08/22/world/asia/china-beidaihe-beach-communist-party-mao.html
|issn=0362-4331
|oclc=1645522
|section=Asia Pacific
|url2=https://archive.is/Ks7mY
|text=Then there is the question of the water quality in the '''Bohai Sea''', a large basin that swirls into Beidaihe.<br>“The water quality is bad,” said Prof. Wang Yamin, of Shandong University Marine College. Runoffs from chemical fertilizer plants have spoiled the sea in the last 30 or so years as China’s economy has grown, he said.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{q|dated}} {{l|en|Gulf of Chihli}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|marginal sea}}
* Chinese:
*: Mandarin: {{t+|cmn|渤海|tr=Bó Hǎi}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===See also===
* {{l|en|Bohai Bay}}

