Page 1227 Bosphorus: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia|Bosporus}}
[[File:Istanbul and Bosporus big.jpg|thumb|upright=1.35|The Bosphorus from space.]]
[[File:Turkish Strait disambig.svg|thumb|The Turkish Straits.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Bosporus}}

===Etymology===
From medieval {{uder|en|la|Bosphorus}}, from {{uder|en|grc|Βόσπορος}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbɒs.fəɹ.əs/|/ˈbɒs.pəɹ.əs/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbɑs.fɚ.əs/|/ˈbɑs.pɚ.əs/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒspəɹəs}}
* {{hyph|en|Bos|pho|rus}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{sid|en|Q35958}}{{place|en|The [[narrow]] <<strait>> beside <<city/Istanbul>>, <<c/Turkey>> [[connecting]] the [[Black Sea]] to the [[Sea of Marmara]], the [[northern]] [[end]] of the [[Turkish Straits]] [[connect]]ing the [[Black Sea]] with the [[Aegean]] and [[Mediterranean]]}}.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1950|month=July|author=J. C. Mertens|title=By the "Taurus Express" to Baghdad|journal=Railway Magazine|page=435|text=The 20-min. crossing of the '''Bosphorus''' by ferry steamer from the Golden Horn, the busy river-fed harbour that divides old and new Istanbul on the European side of the '''Bosphorus''', was a pleasure in itself.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|Constantinople}} [[strait|Strait]]
* {{l|en|Istanbul}} [[strait|Strait]]

====Hypernyms====
* {{l|en|Turkish}} [[strait|Strait]](s)

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|Dardanelles}}

