Page 1230 British Isles: -------- begin text --------
==English==
[[File:Cloud-free Europe ESA17486464 (British Isles).jpeg|thumb|Satellite image showing the British Isles.]]

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|British|t=relating to [[Britons]], [[Britain]], or the [[Britains]]}} + {{m|en|isles|t=islands}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=272964|date=December 2021|nodot=1}}</ref> Compare {{der|en|grc|Βρεττανίδες νῆσοι}} and {{der|en|la|Britannicae insulae|t=British islands}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˌbɹɪ.tɪʃ ˈaɪlz/}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=the British Isles}} {{g|p}}

# {{sid|en|Q38272}}{{place|en|archipelago|r/Northern Europe|consisting of the islands of [[Great Britain]], [[Ireland]], [[Anglesey]], the [[Isle of Man]], the [[Isle of Wight]], the [[Hebrides]], the [[Shetland Islands]], the [[Orkney Islands]], the [[Isles of Scilly]], the [[Channel Islands]] and many smaller islands}}.<ref>{{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

====Usage notes====
* The name is usually applied in a geographical or territorial sense, rather than as a term for a political unit. In Ireland, some prefer not to use the term.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=272964|date=December 2021|nodot=1}}</ref> Use may exclude the [[Channel Islands]], which are closer to mainland Europe than to the other islands.

====Synonyms====
See [[Thesaurus:British Isles]].

