===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{abbreviation of|en|California|nodot=1}}, {{place|en|state|c/United States of America|continent/North America|a=a}}
# {{abbreviation of|en|Canada|nodot=1}}, a country in [[North America]]<!-- "place" template removed as no other abbreviations are included in Category:en:Countries and this template can't handle "nocat" -->
# {{lb|en|Canada|politics}} {{initialism of|en|{{w|Canadian Alliance}}|nodot=1}}, Conservative-Reform Alliance Party, Reform-Conservative Alliance Party
# {{lb|en|software|computing}} {{initialism of|en|{{w|Computer Associates}}|nodot=1}}, an American software company.
# {{lb|en|sports|cricket}} {{abbreviation of|en|{{w|lang=en|Cricket Australia}}|nodot=1}}, the governing body of cricket in Australia.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Canadian politics}} {{l|en|CRAP}}, {{l|en|RCAP}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|cellular automata}} {{initialism of|en|cellular automaton}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=1989-03-21|author=Mark Kramer|title=Fast LIFE (was: Re: summing 9-cell neighborhoods)|newsgroup=comp.theory.cell-automata|url=https://groups.google.com/g/comp.theory.cell-automata/c/zYT2xMNp9rc/m/vsFFSAJEMcMJ|text=BTW: Of course the rules were parametrised, so any totalistic 2-dimensional 9-neighbourhood '''CA''' could be run.}}
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=2012-07-03
|author=Mike James
|title=A New Computational Universe - Fredkin's SALT CA
|site=www.i-programmer.info
|url=http://www.i-programmer.info/news/112-theory/4445-a-new-computational-universe-fredkins-salt-ca.html
|accessdate=2012-10-25
|passage=The new '''CA''' is a modification of Fredkin's earlier SALT architecture in which every cell is identified as either even or odd - as in sodium and chlorine in a salt crystal hence the name. The state of each cell is either up or down and the development rule simple takes account of states of odd and even neighbours. The up-date at each time step simply takes the form of a swap of the states of diagonally related cells. SALT '''CAs''' are reversible and capable of universal computation and are conjectured to be capable of universal construction in the sense of Von Neumann.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=2013-10-31|author=Shawn LeGrand|title=Question about one-dimensional cellular automaton with a finite number of cells|newsgroup=comp.theory.cell-automata|url=https://groups.google.com/g/comp.theory.cell-automata/c/m0qb-_Dny5o/m/A74mP0JfAZEJ|text=I assume we are speaking of a single rule '''CA''' (one rule for every cell).}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} {{initialism of|en|certificate authority}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Kapil Raina|title=PKI Security Solutions for the Enterprise|page=30
|passage=Well-designed '''CAs''' will create a trust hierarchy, which consists of a root with a number of subroots, to further enhance protection of the private key.}}
# {{lb|en|US|nautical}} {{initialism of|en|armored cruiser|nodot=1}}, a type of warship
# {{lb|en|US|nautical}} {{initialism of|en|heavy cruiser|nodot=1}}, a variant of the [[cruiser]] type of warship
# {{lb|en|US|military}} {{initialism of|en|civil affairs|nodot=1}}, a military occupational specialty or branch
# {{lb|en|organic compound}} {{abbreviation of|en|cyanoacrylate}}
# {{lb|en|Scotland|Canada|AU|NZ|South Africa|accounting}} {{initialism of|en|chartered accountant}}
# {{lb|en|Japan}} {{initialism of|en|cabin attendant}}
# {{initialism of|en|[[central]] [[authority]]}}
# {{lb|en|UK|law}} {{init of|en|Companies Act}}
# {{lb|en|[[TTY]]/[[TDD]]}} {{initialism of|en|communications assistant}}
# {{init of|en|closed access|nodot=1}}, as opposed to [[w|open access]].

