Page 1234 canton: -------- begin text --------
{{also|cantón|Canton|Cantón}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology 1===
1530s, from {{bor|en|frm|canton}}, from {{der|en|fro|canton|t=corner}}; heraldic sense from the 1570s, geographic sense from c. 1600.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|kanton}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkæntn̩/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkæntɒn/}} ''(especially in the flag sense)''
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-canton.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q2311958}} A [[division]] of a political unit.
#* '''1912''', Joseph McCabe (translator), ''We Must Take Sides; or, The Principal of Action'' (originally by {{w|Voltaire}})
#*: These three millions live in a small '''canton''' of Egypt which cannot maintain twenty thousand people
#* '''20 May, 1686''', {{w|Gilbert Burnet}}, ''letter from Nimmengen''
#*: {{quote|en|There is another piece of Holbein's, {{...}} in which, in six several '''cantons''', the several parts of our Saviour's passion are represented.}}
## {{senseid|en|Q23058}} One of the [[state]]s comprising the [[Swiss Confederation]]. [[Category:en:Switzerland]]
## A [[subdivision]] of an ''[[arrondissement]]'' of [[France]]. [[Category:en:France]]
## A division of [[Luxembourg]], [[Federation of Bosnia and Herzegovina]], etc.
## {{lb|en|obsolete}} A subdivision of a [[county]], of [[Quebec]], [[Canada]]; equivalent to a [[township]]. [[Category:en:Quebec]]
# A small [[community]] or [[clan]].
# A subdivision of a [[flag]], the [[rectangular]] [[inset]] on the upper [[hoist]] (i.e., [[flagpole]]) side (e.g., the stars of the US national flag are in a canton).
# {{senseid|en|Q1559605}} {{lb|en|heraldiccharge}} A division of a [[shield]] occupying one third of the [[chief]], usually on the [[dexter]] side, formed by a [[perpendicular]] line from the top meeting a [[horizontal]] line from the side.
#* {{RQ:Evelyn Diary|21 August 1662}}
#*: {{quote|en|The king gave us the arms of England to be borne in a '''canton''' in our arms.}}

