Page 1237 Caprivi Strip: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Named after the German chancellor [[w:Leo von Caprivi|Leo von Caprivi]], who negotiated with the British about this strip of land as well as the island of [[Helgoland]] in exchange for [[Zanzibar]] in 1890.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=the [[Caprivi]] [[strip|Strip]]}}

# {{place|en|A narrow <<strip of land>> politically belonging to the country of <<c/Namibia>> and connecting the mainland with the [[Zambezi]] river}}.

