{{trans-bottom}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Pertaining to [[open#Adjective|open]] [[countryside]]; [[unforested]], [[flat#Adjective|flat]].
#* {{RQ:Montaigne Florio Essayes|book=I|chapter=Of the Caniballes|page=102|passage=They are ſeated alongſt the ſea-coaſt, encompaſſed toward the land with huge and ſteepie mountains, having betweene both, a hundred leagues or there abouts of open and '''champaine''' ground.}}
#* {{RQ:Smollett Peregrine Pickle|volume=II|71|text=A fine '''champagne''' country, well stored with corn.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Christopher Hill (historian)|Christopher Hill]]|title=The World Turned Upside Down|year=1972|publisher=Folio Society|year_published=2016|page=35|passage=In England mobility was taken for granted, at least outside the '''champaign''' agricultural areas.}}

====Synonyms====
