# {{lb|en|geography}} A [[dip]] on a [[mountain]] [[ridge]] between two [[peak]]s.
#: {{syn|en|nek|q1=South Africa}}
#: {{cot|en|bealach|mountain pass|pass|saddle|hause}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|title=Across Peaks & Passes in Kumaun Himalaya|author=Harish Kapadia|chapter=Ascents in the Panch Chuli Group|location=New Delhi|publisher=Indus Publishing Company|isbn=8173870969|page={{gbooks|nD95LUfpgzgC|136|col}}|passage=We spent half an hour on the summit before returning to our camp, where we stuffed the frozen tent and all the gear into our packs and started the long descent of the southwest ridge to rejoin Harish and others who were still encamped on the '''col''' at the foot of it.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2019|author=Alan Staniforth|title=Cleveland Way|page=74|passage=Turn left through a gate in the right angle of the wall and drop down to a '''col''' before climbing up the hill.}}
# {{lb|en|meteorology}} A [[pressure]] region between two [[anticyclone]]s and two [[low-pressure]] regions.
#: {{syn|en|saddle point}}

