Page 1269 cryptodepression: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{was wotd|2019|January|9}}

===Etymology===
[[File:037 Lago di Como.jpg|thumb|[[Lake Como]] in [[Lombardy]], [[Italy]], possesses a cryptodepression. One of the deepest lakes in [[Europe]], its [[bottom#Noun|bottom]] is more than 200 [[metres]] (660 [[foot#Noun|feet]]) below [[sea level]].]]

From {{prefix|en|crypto|t1=''prefix meaning ‘hidden’''|depression|t2=area lower in topography than its surroundings}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˌkɹɪptəʊdɪˈpɹɛʃən/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˌkɹiptoʊdəˈpɹɛʃ(ə)n/}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-cryptodepression.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|cryp|to|de|press|ion}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|geography|[[limnology]]}} The portion of a [[lake]] which lies below [[sea level]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:G. Evelyn Hutchinson|G[eorge] Evelyn Hutchinson]]|title=A Treatise on Limnology|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:John Wiley & Sons|year=1957|volume=I (Geography, Physics, and Chemistry)|page=165|oclc=475547083|passage=When the bottom of the lake lies below mean sea level, it is said to occupy a '''cryptodepression''', the depth of which is the depth below sea level of the deepest point of the basin.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Robert V. Thomann; Dominick M. DeToro; Richard P. Winfield; Donald J. O’Connor|chapter=Section IV: Lake Ontario – Background|title=Mathematical Modeling of Phytoplankton in Lake Ontario: 1. Model Development and Verification|series=Ecological Research Series|seriesvolume=EPA-660/3-75-005|location=Corvallis, Or.|publisher=National Environmental Research Center, Office of Research and Development, [[w:United States Environmental Protection Agency|U.S. Environmental Protection Agency]]|month=March|year=1975|page=8|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-3f3flUsfn0C&pg=PA8|oclc=890687357|passage=The lake's elevation above sea level is 74.01 meters (242.8 feet) which makes its depth of '''cryptodepression''' to be 170 meters (558 feet).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|chapter=Appendix A: Problem Identification|title=A Study to Determine the Feasibility of Providing Flood Control Improvements to the Susupe Chalan Kanoa Area, Island of Saipan, Commonwealth of the Northern Mariana Islands: Draft Detailed Report and Environmental Statement|location=Fort Shafter [Honolulu], Hi.|publisher=[[w:United States Army Corps of Engineers|U.S. Army Engineer District, Honolulu]]|month=June|year=1979|page=A-10|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=3TQ0AQAAMAAJ&pg=SL1-PA10|oclc=172922398|passage=The greater volume of the lake [Lake Susupe] occupies a '''cryptodepression''' (that portion which lies below sea level). Based upon a surface elevation of +2.5 ft determined on 20 December 1978 by Juan C. Tenorio and Associates' surveyors, the depth of the '''cryptodepression''' is -1.4m (4.7 ft) below sea level.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=R. B. Wood; J. F. Talling|chapter=Chemical and Algal Relationships in a Salinity Series of Ethiopian Inland Waters|title=[[w:Hydrobiologia|Hydrobiologia: The International Journal of Aquatic Sciences]]|location=Dordrecht|publisher=[[w:Springer Science+Business Media|Kluwer Academic Publishers]]|year=1988|volume=158|page=29|issn=0018-8158|oclc=757640392|newversion=reprinted in|editor2=J. M. Melack|title2=Saline Lakes: Proceedings of the Third International Symposium on Inland Saline Lakes, Held at Nairobi, Kenya, August 1985|series2=Developments in Hydrobiology|seriesvolume2=44|location2=Dordrecht|publisher2=Dr. W. Junk Publishers|year2=1988|section2=abstract|page2=29|pageurl2=https://books.google.com/books?id=asHtCAAAQBAJ&pg=PA29|doi2=10.1007/978-94-009-3095-7|isbn2=978-94-010-7891-7|passage=At present there are three major closed systems (Awash R.&nbsp;– Afar drainage, northern rift lakes, southern rift lakes), numerous crater lakes with seepage-in and -out, and two '''cryptodepressions''' with marine inputs.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=José Galizia Tundisi; Takako Matsumura-Tundisi|chapter=The Origin of Lakes|title=Limnology|location=Boca Raton, Fla.|publisher=w:CRC Press|year=2012|section=section 3.3.10 (Average Slope (α))|page=49|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-S3MBQAAQBAJ&pg=PA49|isbn=978-0-415-58835-5|passage=The maximum depth of some lakes is below current sea level. Such lakes are called '''cryptodepressions'''. Well-known cases of tectonic lakes include Lake Baikal and the Caspian Sea. Some glacial lakes in Norway, Scotland and England are also '''cryptodepressions'''.|footer={{small|Application of the word to the lake as a whole.}}|brackets=on}}

