===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# That which [[draw#Verb|draws]]: that which attracts e.g. a crowd.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 24, 2007|author=Joyce Hor-Chung Lau|title=Hong Kong Is Reshaped by Mainlanders|journal=w:The New York Times
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20150605101611/https://www.nytimes.com/2007/06/24/world/asia/24hongkong.html
|issn=0362-4331|oclc=1645522|section=Asia Pacific|url2=https://archive.is/hHRLc
|text=At the mountain’s base is the leafy suburb of Kowloon Tong. It has never been a big tourist '''draw''', but in the decade since territorial control returned to China, this quintessentially Hong Kong neighborhood has had many more visitors — and important changes.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Christoper Zara|title=Tortured Artists: From Picasso and Monroe to Warhol and Winehouse, the Twisted Secrets of the World's Most Creative Minds|section=part 1, chapter 1, {{gbooks|q=draws|id=HV4jKhjzMVYC|pg=27}}
|passage=After ''It'', Clara became one of the top box-office '''draws''' in Hollywood, but her popularity was short lived.}}
# The act of drawing:
## The act of [[#Verb|draw]]ing a gun from a holster, etc.
##: {{ux|en|the Wild West's quick-'''draw''' champion}}
## The [[procedure]] by which the [[result]] of a [[lottery]] is [[determine]]d.
##: {{ux|en|The '''draw''' is on Saturday.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=January 29, 2011|author=Chris Bevan|title=Torquay 0 - 1 Crawley Town
|work=BBC|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/fa_cup/9379079.stm|page=
|passage=Having spent more than £500,000 on players last summer, Crawley can hardly be classed as minnows but they have still punched way above their weight and this kind of performance means no-one will relish pulling them out of the hat in Sunday's '''draw'''.}}
## {{lb|en|archery}} The act of pulling back the strings in preparation of firing;<!--separate sense?--> the distance the strings are pulled back.
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2016-08-25|author=Mike Loades|title=The Composite Bow|publisher=Bloomsbury Publishing|isbn=9781472821614|page=21
|text=This configuration offered the capacity for an exceptionally long '''draw''' – Manchu archers drew all the way back to the point of the right shoulder{{nb...}}}}
# The result of drawing:
## The [[result]] of a [[contest]] that neither side [[win|has won]]; a [[tie]].
##: {{ux|en|The game ended in a '''draw'''.}}
## {{lb|en|cricket}} The [[result]] of a two-[[innings]] match in which at least one side did not complete all their innings before time ran out (as distinguished from a [[tie]]).
# That which is drawn (e.g. funds from an account).
#: ''They're going to take away our draw!'' {{q|referring to e.g. disability assistance}}
## In a commission-based job, an advance on future (potential) [[commission]]s given to an employee by the employer.
# [[draft|Draft]]: flow through a [[flue]] of gasses (smoke) resulting from a combustion process, possibly adjustable with a [[damper]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1981|author=Stephen King|title=Do the Dead Sing?
|passage=She looked in [to the stove] and a tight, dismayed gasp escaped her. She slammed the door shut and adjusted the '''draw''' with trembling fingers. For a moment—just a moment—she had seen her old friend Annabelle Frane in the coals.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} The [[spin]] or [[twist]] imparted to a [[ball]] etc. by a drawing stroke.
# {{lb|en|golf}} A [[golf]] shot that (for the right-handed player) curves intentionally to the left. See [[hook]], [[slice]], [[fade]].
# {{lb|en|curling}} A shot that is intended to land gently in the house (the circular target) without knocking out other stones; cf. ''[[takeout]]''.
# {{senseid|en|dry stream bed}} {{lb|en|geography}} A dry [[stream]] bed that drains surface water only during periods of heavy [[rain]] or [[flooding]].
#* '''1918''', {{w|Willa Cather}}, ''{{w|My Ántonia}}'', Mirado Modern Classics, paperback edition, page 15
#*: The garden, curiously enough, was a quarter of a mile from the house, and the way to it led up a shallow '''draw''' past the cattle corral.
# {{lb|en|slang|countable}} A [[bag]] of [[cannabis]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Yvonne Ellis|title=Daughter, Arise: A Journey from Devastation to Restoration|page=54
|passage=So my friends and I would all chip in money to get a bag of weed or a '''draw'''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|uncountable}} Cannabis.
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2003|artist=w:Goldie Looking Chain|album=The Manifesto|title=Soap Bar|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EtVZbQkvk_Q|passage=Selling '''draw''' to your mates but it's really Oxo cubes.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=Michael Coleman|title=Old Skool Rave|page=139
|passage=Mick spoke to Simon, who was more of a drinker. He said that people who smoked '''draw''' were boring.}}
# {{lb|en|poker}} A situation in which one or more players has four cards of the same suit or four out of five necessary cards for a [[straight]] and requires a further card to make their [[flush]] or straight.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Ryan Wiseman|page=82|title=Earn $30,000 Per Month Playing Online Poker: A Step-By-Step Guide to Single|passage=The player to your left immediately raises you the minimum by clicking the raise button. This action immediately suggests that he's on a '''draw'''}}
# {{lb|en|horse racing}} The [[stall]] from which a [[horse]] [[begin]]s the [[race]].

