Page 1295 ecosystem: -------- begin text --------
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|eco|system}}. {{coin|en|nobycat=1|Arthur Tansley|nat=English|occ=botanist|in=1935}} in a paper titled "The Use and Abuse of Vegetational Concepts" in the journal ''[[w:Ecology (journal)|Ecology]]''.<ref>
{{cite-journal
|lang=en
|journal=Ecology
|volume=16
|number=3
|title=The Use and Abuse of Vegetational Concepts
|year=1935
|month=July
|author=Arthur Tansley
|authorlink=Arthur Tansley
|url=http://www.ecology150anniversary.net/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/tansley-1935.pdf
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20161006125220/http://www.ecology150anniversary.net/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/tansley-1935.pdf
|archivedate=2016-10-06
|passage=Our natural prejudices force us to consider the organisms (in the sense of the biologist) as the most important parts of these systems, but certainly the inorganic “factors” are also parts – there could be no systems without them, and there is constant interchange of the most various kinds within each system, not only between the organisms but between the organic and the inorganic. These ''ecosystems'', as we may call them, are of the most various kinds and sizes.
}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈiːkəʊˌsɪstəm/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈikoʊˌsɪstəm/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|eco|sys|tem}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[system]] formed by an [[ecological]] [[community]] and its [[environment]] that [[function]]s as a [[unit]].
#* {{quote-journal
|1=en
|date=2012-01
|author=Donald Worster
|title=A Drier and Hotter Future
|volume=100
|issue=1
|page=70
|magazine=w:American Scientist
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/a-drier-and-hotter-future
|passage=Phoenix and Lubbock are both caught in severe drought, and it is going to get much worse. We may see many such [dust] storms in the decades ahead, along with species extinctions, radical disturbance of '''ecosystems''', and intensified social conflict over land and water. Welcome to the Anthropocene, the epoch when humans have become a major geological and climatic force.
|accessdate=12 May 2013
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120126223603/http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/a-drier-and-hotter-future
|archivedate=26 January 2012
}}
# The [[interconnectedness]] of [[organism]]s (plants, animals, microbes) with each other and their [[environment]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A network of interconnected people, organisations, products or services that resembles a natural ecosystem due to the complex interdependencies.
#: {{ux|en|The company’s '''ecosystem''' mainly comprises its supply chain, customers, end consumers and competitors.}}
#* {{quote-web|en
|date=2022-03-21
|author=Rahul Shivshankar
|work=Times of India
|title=The real reason why the Left eco-system has launched a scurrilous attack on the movie Kashmir Files
|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/blogs/beyond-the-headline/the-real-reason-why-the-left-eco-system-has-launched-a-scurrilous-attack-on-the-movie-kashmir-files/
|text=It &#91;[[w:The Kashmir Files|The Kashmir Files]]&#93; is being described by the leftist “liberal” '''ecosystem''' as a movie that peddles bigotry against Muslims.}}
#* {{quote-web|en
|date=2022-02-17
|author=Angshuman Choudhury; Suraj Gogoi
|work=Scroll.in
|title=Hijab ban: How some liberals are sleepwalking into the trap set by Hindutva nationalists
|url=https://scroll.in/article/1017559/hijab-ban-how-some-liberals-are-sleepwalking-into-the-trap-set-by-hindutva-nationalists
|text=There is a certain duality in how the Hindutva '''ecosystem''' is pushing the anti-hijab discourse into the mainstream.}}

====Hypernyms====
* {{l|en|system}}

====Derived terms====
* [[ecosystem engineer]]

