Page 1307 Fennoscandia: -------- begin text --------
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|la|Fennia||Finland}} + {{m|la|Scandia||Scandinavia}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{sid|en|Q604496}}{{place|en|pensinula|r/Northern Europe|comprising, besides the [[Scandinavian Peninsula]], also [[Finland]], the [[Kola Peninsula]] and [[Karelia]] (and sometimes also including [[Denmark]], although it is not part of the Scandinavian Peninsula)}}.
#:{{syn|en|Fennoscandinavia|Fenno-Scandinavia}}
# {{sid|en|Q580133}}{{lb|en|geology}} the [[Fennoscandian Shield]] underlying Norway, Sweden, Finland, and Northern Denmark; [[Baltic Shield]].
# {{lb|en|culture}} the culture group comprising the [[Finnic]], [[Sami]], and [[Scandinavian]] cultures.

====Usage notes====
Unlike the term ‘[[Nordic countries]]’, Fennoscandia does not include [[Iceland]], [[Greenland]] and other geographically disconnected overseas areas.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|Fennoscandian}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|geographic area}}
* Danish: {{t|da|Fennoskandinavien|c}}
