Page 1318 Gaul: -------- begin text --------
{{also|gaul}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|Gaule||Gaul}}, from {{der|en|frm|Gaule||Gaul}}, from {{der|en|fro|Gaule|}}, {{m|fro|Waulle||Gaul|pos=a term used to translate unrelated {{noncog|la|Gallia|t=Gaul}}}}, from {{der|en|frk|*Walhaland|*Walha(land)|Gaul, Land of the Romans, foreigners}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*walh||foreigner, Roman, Celt}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*walhaz||an outlander, foreigner, Celt}}, probably of {{der|en|cel}} origin, from the same source as {{cog|la|Volcae||pos=name of a Celtic tribe in South Germany, which later emigrated to Gaul}}. Akin to {{cog|goh|Walh}}, {{m|goh|Walah||a Celt, Roman, Gaul}}, {{cog|ang|Wealh}}, {{m|ang|Walh||a non-Germanic foreigner, Celt/Briton/Welshman}}, {{cog|non|Valir||Gauls, Frenchmen}}. More at {{l|en|Wales}}/{{l|en|Welsh}}, {{l|en|Cornwall}}, {{l|en|Walloon}}, and {{l|en|Vlach}}/{{l|en|Wallachia}}.

Despite their similar appearance, Latin {{m|la|Gallia}} is not the origin of French {{m|fr|Gaule}}. During the evolution from Latin to French, stressed initial /ˈɡa-/ yielded /dʒa/ > /ʒa/ (cf. Latin {{m|la|gamba}} > French {{m|fr|jambe}}), while unstressed final /-lia/ yielded /ʎə/ > /j/ (cf. Latin {{m|la|filia}} > French {{m|fr|fille}}). Thus, the regular outcome of {{cog|la|Gallia}} is /ʒaj/ ⟨Jaille⟩, which is attested in several French toponyms: ''La Jaille-Yvon, Saint-Mars-la-Jaille'', etc.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɡɔːl/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Gaul.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{q|[[cot-caught merger]]}} {{IPA|en|/ɡɑl/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːl|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|gall}}

===Proper noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|historic}} {{place|en|historical region|roughly corresponding to modern [[France]], [[Luxembourg]], [[Belgium]], most of [[Switzerland]], and parts of [[Northern Italy]] ([[Lombardy]]), the [[Netherlands]], and [[Germany]] west of the [[Rhine]]}}.
#: {{hyper|en|[[Celtic]] Gaul|[[Belgic]] Gaul|Aquitaine|Cisalpine Gaul|Transalpine Gaul|Gallia Narbonensis|q=historical}}

