===Etymology 3===
{{clipping|en|gorgeous|alt=gorge(ous)}}; originally British slang.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|en|gorg}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|more}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} [[gorgeous|Gorgeous]].
#: {{ux|en|Oh, look at him: isn’t he '''gorge'''?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Brittany [Lyn] Geragotelis|chapter=1|title=Life’s a Witch|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Simon & Schuster|Simon & Schuster BFYR]]|year=2013|page=19|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=H9n1BTJws5oC&pg=PA19|isbn=978-1-4424-6655-5|passage="Um, Hadley? Don't tell me that's ''another'' new outfit. It's totally '''gorge'''!” Sofia stopped me in the middle of the hallway to admire the clothes I'd meticulously picked out that morning.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=Katy Perry Reveals Her {{w|Prismatic World Tour}} Costumes Featuring [[w:Roberto Cavalli|Cavalli]], [[w:Valentino (fashion designer)|Valentino]], & MORE!|url=https://perezhilton.com/katy-perry-tour-costumes-roberto-cavalli-revealed-hot/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190328090427/https://perezhilton.com/katy-perry-tour-costumes-roberto-cavalli-revealed-hot/|archivedate=28 March 2019|work=[[w:Perez Hilton|PerezHilton.com]]|date=5 May 2014|passage=While she's &#91;{{w|Katy Perry}}'s&#93; been hard at work on her singing and choreography, designers have been hard at work coming up with the most '''gorge''', glam, and fabulous costumes for her to wear on stage.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:Carson Kressley|title=[[w:RuPaul's Drag Race (season 9)|RuPaul’s Drag Race]] Recap: ‘RuPaul Roast’|url=https://ew.com/recap/rupauls-drag-race-recap-season-9-episode-8/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190217190838/https://ew.com/recap/rupauls-drag-race-recap-season-9-episode-8/|archivedate=28 March 2019|magazine=w:Entertainment Weekly|date=12 May 2017|passage=Now here's a little inside scoop, I happen to adore [[w:Michelle Visage|Michelle [Visage]]] and she has never looked more '''gorge''' than in this episode!}}

