===Etymology===
{{cal|en|it|[[golfo|Golfo]] [[di]] [[Venetia]]}}, from consideration of the [[sea]] as a [[gulf]] of the [[Mediterranean]] and the previous importance of the {{w|Republic of Venice}} to its trade and major ports.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|archaic}} {{synonym of|en|Adriatic Sea}}.
#* '''1771''', [[:s:EB1|''Encyclopaedia Britannica'', 1st ed.]], Vol. II, p. 184:
#*: [[:s:Encyclopædia Britannica, First Edition/Chimæra|CHIMÆRA]], in geography, a port town of [[Turkey|Turky]] in Europe, [[situated|ſituated]] at the entrance of the '''gulph of Venice''', in the province of [[Epirus]], about thirty-two miles north of the city [[Corfu]], near which are the mountains of [[Chimaera#English|Chimæra]], which divide Epirus from [[Thessaly|Theſſaly]]...
# {{lb|en|informal}} {{place|en|A [[wide]] <<gulf>> at the [[north]] [[end]] of the <<sea/Adriatic Sea>>, [[bound]] on the [[south]] by the [[line]] between [[Maestra Point]] in the [[Po]] [[delta]] and [[Cape Kamenjak]] on the [[Istrian]] [[peninsula|Peninsula]]}}.

