Page 1355 hook: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Hook|hòòk}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hoke}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hōc}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hōk}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hōkaz}}, variant of {{m|gem-pro|*hakô|t=hook}}, probably ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kog-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*keg-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*keng-|t=peg, hook, claw}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates}}
Compare {{cog|fy|heak}}, {{cog|nl|haak|t=hook}}) (compare {{cog|fy|-}}/{{cog|nl|hoek|t=hook, angle, corner}}, {{cog|nds||Hook}}, {{m|nds||Huuk}}); also related to {{l|en|hake}}. {{rel-bottom}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ho͝ok}}, {{IPA|en|/hʊk/}}
* {{a|sometimes in Northern England, otherwise obsolete}} {{enPR|ho͞ok}} {{IPA|en|/huːk/}}<ref>{{R:Critical Pronouncing Dictionary|Hook|302|3|ppage=1}}</ref>
* {{audio|en|en-us-hook.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-hook.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʊk|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{multiple images
|direction = vertical
|image1 = Blue lifting hook.jpg
|caption1 = A hook ''(sense 1)'' on a construction crane
|image2 = RichardMasonRocca.JPG
|caption2 = A hook shot ''(sense 23.2)'' in basketball
|image3 = Kickboxing right hook landing.jpg
|caption3 = A right hook ''(sense 23.4)'' in boxing
}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[rod]] [[bend#Verb|bent]] into a [[curved#Adjective|curved]] [[shape#Noun|shape]], typically with one [[end#Noun|end]] [[free#Adjective|free]] and the other end [[secure#Verb|secured]] to a [[rope#Noun|rope]] or other [[attachment]].
# A [[barbed#Adjective|barbed]] [[metal]] hook used for [[fishing#Noun|fishing]]; a [[fishhook]].
# Any of various hook-shaped [[agricultural]] [[implement#Noun|implements]] such as a [[billhook]].
#* {{RQ:Pope Horace|like slashing Bentley with his desperate '''hook'''}}
#* {{RQ:Keats Lamia|poem=To Autumn|stanza=2|page=138|passage=Or on a half-reap'd furrow sound asleep, / Drowsed with the fume of poppies, while thy '''hook ''' / Spares the next swath and all its twinèd flowers: [...]}}
# The curved [[needle#Noun|needle]] used in the art of [[crochet]].
# The part of a [[hinge#Noun|hinge]] which is [[fix#Verb|fixed]] to a [[post#Noun|post]], and on which a [[door]] or [[gate]] [[hang#Verb|hangs]] and [[turn#Verb|turns]].
# A [[loop#Noun|loop]] shaped like a hook under certain [[written#Adjective|written]] [[letter#Noun|letters]], for example, ''g'' and ''j''.
# A [[tie-in]] to a [[current#Adjective|current]] [[event]] or [[trend#Noun|trend]] that makes a [[news]] [[story]] or [[editorial]] [[relevant]] and [[timely]].
# A [[snare#Noun|snare]]; a [[trap#Noun|trap]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Cymbeline|5|5|passage=A shop of all the qualities, that man<br>Loues woman for, besides that '''hooke''' of Wiuing,}}
# An [[advantageous]] [[hold]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2020|author=Joel W. Barrows|title=Deep Red Cover
|passage=“What makes you so sure that nobody knows you've got a '''hook''' into him?” Ward asked.}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} The projecting points of the [[thighbone]]s of [[cattle]]; called also [[hook bones]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[removal|Removal]] or [[expulsion]] from a group or activity.
#: {{ux|en|He is not handling this job, so we're giving him the '''hook'''.}}
# {{lb|en|agriculture}} A [[field]] [[sow]]n [[two]] [[year]]s in [[succession]].
# {{lb|en|authorship}} A [[brief]], [[punchy]] [[opening]] [[statement]] intended to get [[attention]] from an audience, reader, or viewer, and make them want to continue to listen to a speech, read a [[book]], or watch a [[play]].
# {{lb|en|narratology}} A [[gimmick]] or element of a creative work intended to be attention-grabbing for the audience; a compelling [[idea]] for a story that will be sure to attract people's attention.
#* {{quote-web|en|author=A. A. Dowd|title=''[[w:Good Boys (film)|Good Boys]]'' Puts a Tween Spin on the R-rated Teen Comedy, to Mostly Funny Effect|work=w:The A.V. Club|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210304011128/https://film.avclub.com/good-boys-puts-a-tween-spin-on-the-r-rated-teen-comedy-1837252319|archivedate=4 March 2021|date=14 August 2019|passage=The '''hook''' of ''Good Boys'', Hollywood's latest odyssey of comic adolescent mischief, is that the kids behaving badly are, for once, truly kids.}}
# {{lb|en|bridge|slang}} A [[finesse#Noun|finesse]].
# {{lb|en|card games|slang}} A [[jack#Noun|jack]] (the [[playing card]]).
# {{lb|en|geography}} A [[spit#Noun|spit]] or narrow [[cape]] of [[sand#Noun|sand]] or [[gravel]] turned [[landward]] at the outer end, such as Sandy Hook in [[New Jersey]].
# {{lb|en|music}} A [[catchy]] [[musical]] [[phrase]] which forms the basis of a [[popular]] [[song]].
#: {{ux|en|The song's '''hook''' snared me.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Annie Zaleski|title=AFI sounds refreshed and rejuvenated on its 10th album, ''AFI (The Blood Album)''|url=http://www.avclub.com/review/afi-sounds-refreshed-and-rejuvenated-its-10th-albu-248390|work=w:The A.V. Club|date=20 January 2017|passage=Guitarist Jade Puget and vocalist Davey Havok have distilled AFI’s strengths (a ferocious, post-hardcore rhythmic backbone; goth-tinctured, post-punky guitars; and Havok’s desperate, dramatic croon) into 14 taut, '''hook'''-driven songs.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|informal}} A ship's [[anchor]].
# {{lb|en|programming}} Part of a [[system]]'s [[operation]] that can be [[intercept]]ed to [[change#Verb|change]] or [[augment]] its [[behaviour]].
#: {{syn|en|endpoint}}
#: {{ux|en|We've added '''hooks''' to allow undefined message types to be handled with custom code.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2015|author=Rachel Alt-Simmons|title=Agile by Design|page=182
|passage=In lieu of those unneeded '''hooks''', write code to [[fail fast]] and prevent gaps from becoming a problem.}}
# {{lb|en|Scrabble}} An instance of playing a word [[perpendicular]] to a word already on the board, adding a letter to the start or the end of the word to form a new word.
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Setup plays can also be made when you do not have the needed letter but believe your opponent doesn't know the '''hook''' owing to its obscurity.| page=58| author=Andrew Fisher; David Webb| title=The Art of Scrabble| year=2003| isbn=0713488204| url=https://books.google.com/books?id=Y5WsuWIA9lIC&printsec=frontcover&dq=how+to+win+at+scrabble&source=bl&ots=RQ7XEaa7bm&sig=C1d1M3II9UpifvxAvoYytC61T8c&hl=en&sa=X&ei=5jo-UJrELOLK0QXsr4GQCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=hook&f=false}}
# {{lb|en|typography}} A [[diacritical mark]] shaped like the upper part of a [[question mark]], as in '''ỏ'''.
# {{lb|en|typography|rare}} A [[háček]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|title=Language Issues|section=XV-XVIII, [https://books.google.com/books?id=DHMqAQAAIAAJ&q=%22hook%22&dq=%22hook%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=o0s1T8uFA6PM0QWT7ZmjAg&ved=0CEkQ6AEwBDiqAQ page 36]
|passage=Common diacritics in Slavonic language are the '''hook''' ˇ (as in ha'''č'''ek – Czech for ‘hook’) and the stroke ´ (robi'''ć''' – Polish for ‘do/make’).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=David Adams|title=The Song and Duet Texts of [[w:Antonín Dvořák|Antonín Dvořák]]|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=XVsXAQAAIAAJ&q=%22hook%22&dq=%22hook%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=AjQ1T9_8KqHH0QWg3uyUAg&ved=0CDMQ6AEwADgy|page=168
|passage=In Czech, palatalization is normally indicated by the symbol ˇ, called ''haček'' or “'''hook'''.”}}
#* '''2004''', ''Keesing’s Record of World Events'' L:i–xii, <span class="plainlinks">[https://books.google.com/books?id=jS0MAQAAMAAJ&q=%22hook%22&dq=%22hook%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=eV01T--jFeG_0QWFnZ2SAg&ved=0CFgQ6AEwBziWAQ page unknown]</span>
#*: In detailing the proposed shortening of the Czech Republic to Česko…the '''hook''' (hacek) erroneously appeared over the letter “e” instead of the “C”.
# {{non-gloss definition|Senses relating to sports.}}
## {{lb|en|baseball}} A [[curveball]].
##: {{ux|en|He threw a '''hook''' in the dirt.}}
## {{lb|en|basketball}} a [[basketball]] shot in which the offensive player, usually turned perpendicular to the basket, gently throws the ball with a sweeping motion of his arm in an upward arc with a follow-through which ends over his head. Also called [[hook shot]].
## {{lb|en|bowling}} A ball that is rolled in a curved line.
##* {{quote-book|en|passage=However, for pins on the bowler's right, such as the 3, 6, 9, or 10, move more toward the center of the foul line if you bowl a straight ball or slightly to the left of the center of the foul line if you bowl a '''hook'''.| page=102| author=Harold Keith| title=Sports and Games| year=1969| url=https://books.google.com/books?id=D-6OR7p3tNwC&q=%22bowl+a+hook%22&dq=%22bowl+a+hook%22&hl=es&sa=X&ei=J9HIUJydO4KXhQfU84DYCw&redir_esc=y}}
## {{lb|en|boxing}} a type of [[punch]] delivered with the arm rigid and partially bent and the fist travelling nearly horizontally [[mesially]] along an [[arc]]
##: {{ux|en|The heavyweight delivered a few powerful '''hooks''' that staggered his opponent.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|author=Ben Dirs|title=Carl Froch outclassed by dazzling Andre Ward|url=http://news.bbc.com/sport2/hi/boxing/16234673.stm|work=w:BBC Sport|date=18 December 2011|passage=American Ward was too quick and too slick for his British rival, landing at will with razor sharp jabs and '''hooks''' and even bullying Froch at times.}}
## {{lb|en|cricket}} A type of [[shot#Noun|shot]] played by [[swing#Verb|swinging]] the [[bat#Noun|bat]] in a [[horizontal]] [[arc]], hitting the ball [[high]] in the air to the [[leg#Noun|leg]] side, often [[play#Verb|played]] to balls which [[bounce#Verb|bounce]] around [[head#Noun|head]] [[height]].
## {{lb|en|golf}} A [[golf]] shot that (for the right-handed player) curves [[unintentionally]] to the left. (See [[draw]], [[slice]], [[fade]].)
# {{lb|en|Canada|Australia|military}} Any of the [[chevron]]s denoting [[rank]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[prostitute]].
#: {{syn|en|hooker}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1983|author=G. W. Levi Kamel|title=Downtown Street Hustlers|page=160|passage=I was talkin' to a couple of the ''''hooks'''' (female prostitutes) I know.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|slang|obsolete}} A [[pickpocket]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1885|author=Michael Davitt|title=Leaves from a Prison Diary|page=18|passage=He preceded me to Dartmoor, where I found his fame even more loudly trumpeted than ever, especially by Manchester “'''hooks'''” (pickpockets), who boast of being the rivals of the “Cocks,” or Londoners, in the art of obtaining other people's property without paying for it.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=David W. Maurer|title=Whiz Mob: A Correlation of the Technical Argot of Pickpockets with Their Behavior Pattern|page=58|passage="Everybody's a tool over there. Everybody's a '''hook''', except them four guys on the points of the compass. They are eight or ten strong over there." But all professional pickpockets, however expert or however clumsy, operate on the basis of the situation just outlined.}}
# {{lb|en|surfing}} {{syn of|en|shoulder||the part of a wave that has not yet broken}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1963|author=Grant W. Kuhns|title=On Surfing|page=67|passage=This maneuver involves a sharp turn, back into the '''hook''' of the wave.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|chiefly|historical}} A [[knee]]-shaped [[wooden]] [[join]] connecting the [[keel]] to the [[stem]] (post forming the frontmost part of the [[bow]]) or the [[sternpost]] in [[cog]]-like [[vessel]]s or similar vessels.
#: {{hypo|en|heel knee}}

