Page 1357 horse latitudes: -------- begin text --------
{{also|horse-latitudes|Horse Latitudes}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|horse-latitudes}}
* {{l|en|Horse Latitudes}}

===Etymology===
Various theories; probably from a sailors' ritual of parading a straw-stuffed effigy of a horse around the deck before throwing it overboard.

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun|head=[[horse]] [[latitude]]s}}

# {{lb|en|informal|geography|meteorology}} The [[warm]], [[subtropical]] bands which encircle the globe between approximately 30 and 35 degrees both north and south of the [[Equator]], characterized by high [[atmospheric]] pressure and [[dry]] [[variable]] winds ranging from [[calm]] to [[light]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1866|translator=W. Moy Thomas|author=w:Victor Hugo|title=Toilers of the Sea|chapter=6
|passage=At the equator, an immense mist seems permanently to encircle the globe. It is known as the cloud-ring. The function of the cloud-ring is to temper the heat of the tropics. . . . These are what are called '''horse latitudes'''. It was here that navigators of bygone ages were accustomed to cast their horses into the sea to lighten the ship in stormy weather.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1945|month=May|title=What is Weather?|titleurl=http://books.google.ca/books?id=lJ5XVVDB3SMC&pg=PA31&dq=%22horse+latitudes%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0k-VUbvmN8a4qAHVpYCYAg&ved=0CGQQ6AEwCQ#v=onepage&q=%22horse%20latitudes%22&f=false|journal=Flying Magazine|volume=36|issue=5|page=31
|passage=The north boundary of Zone A is a belt of high barometric pressure known to many generations of seafaring men as the "'''Horse Latitudes'''." Here air currents are divergent and there is relatively low humidity.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=August 15 1999|author=w:Lance Morrow|title=Captains Courageous|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20010211125009/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,29478,00.html|journal=Time
|passage=The 27,000-mile course starts in November in the Bay of Biscay on the coast of France; points south through the '''horse latitudes''' and doldrums, past Africa to the bottom of the world; rounds Cape Horn; then turns north to home.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Dominic Smith|title=Bright and Distant Shores|page=125|isbn=9781439198889|url=http://books.google.ca/books?id=oMioOym3KZMC&pg=PA125&dq=%22horse+latitudes%22+subject:%22fiction%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=XE6VUe67JtSpqQHhlYGgBQ&ved=0CE0Q6AEwBTgU#v=onepage&q=%22horse%20latitudes%22%20subject%3A%22fiction%22&f=false|passage=The captain used the idle '''Horse Latitudes''' to train and prepare the remainder of the crew.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A condition of relative [[inactivity]], calm, or [[lethargy]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 15 1961|title=State of Business: Hardening the Soft Spots|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130508025741/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,827104,00.html|journal=Time
|passage=After months in the '''horse latitudes''', retail and auto sales are scudding along at a brisk pace.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=July 23 1991|author=Woody Hochswender|title=Patterns|titleurl=http://www.nytimes.com/1991/07/23/news/patterns-757491.html|journal=New York Times|accessdate=14 May 2013
|passage=These are the '''horse latitudes''' of fashion, when it's O.K. not to think about clothes, if only for 15 minutes.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=July 24 2000|author=w:Froma Harrop|title=When a tax-free Internet robs the states, guess who they will tax?|titleurl=http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=mTIzAAAAIBAJ&sjid=QwgGAAAAIBAJ&pg=4606,6209817&dq=horse-latitudes-of&hl=en|journal=Free Lance-Star|accessdate=16 May 2013|page=A9
|passage=The Senate version of the House measure now bobs quietly in the '''horse latitudes''' of legislative inaction.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=July 8 2006|author=Bob Ekstrom|title=One Amazin’ Debacle|titleurl=http://www.sports-central.org/sports/2006/07/08/one_amazin_debacle.php|journal=Sports Central|accessdate=16 May 2013
|passage=The Mets were once the clipper ship of baseball, but a demoralizing 4-8 run against the American League East has left them adrift in the '''horse latitudes'''.}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|warm, dry subtropical bands encircling the globe}}
