*: Roman: {{tt+|sh|preòstālī}}
* Spanish: {{tt+|es|sobrado|m}}, {{tt+|es|sobras|f}}
* Swahili: {{tt+|sw|kushoto}}
* Swedish: {{tt+|sv|kvar}}
* Tagalog: {{tt|tl|tira}}
* Telugu: {{tt+|te|మిగిలిన}}
{{trans-bottom}}
}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|levit}}, {{m|enm|ilevet}}, {{m|enm|y-levyd}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ġelȳfd}}, {{m|ang|ġelȳfed}}, past participle of {{der|en|ang|ġelȳfan}}, {{m|ang|lȳfan|t=to allow, permit}}, equivalent to {{af|en|leave|t1=to give leave to, allow, grant, permit|-ed}}.

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|leave||ed-form|t=permit}}.
#: {{ux|en|We were not '''left''' go to the beach after school except on a weekend.}}

===References===
* The Concise Dictionary of English Etymology, Walter W. Skeat.

