===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The fact or quality of having a [[position]] in [[space]].
#* {{RQ:Glanvill Scepsis Scientifica|passage=It is thought that the soul and angels are devoid of quantity and dimension, and that they have nothing to do with grosser '''locality'''.}}
# The [[feature]]s or [[surroundings]] of a particular [[place]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable|maths|computing}} The condition of being [[local]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Randall Hyde|title=Write Great Code, Volume 1: Understanding the Machine|page=154
|passage=This shows temporal '''locality''' of reference in action because the CPU accesses <code>i</code> at three points in a short time period. This program also exhibits spatial '''locality''' of reference.}}
# The [[situation]] or [[position]] of an [[object]].
# An [[area]] or [[district]] considered as the [[site]] of certain [[activity|activities]]; a [[neighbourhood]].
# Limitation to a county, district, or place.
#* {{RQ:Blackstone Commentaries|passage='''locality''' of trial}}
# {{lb|en|geography}} A [[built-up]] [[area]], i.e. a [[city]], [[town]] or [[village]]
# {{lb|en|dated|phrenology}} The [[perceptive]] [[faculty]] concerned with the ability to [[remember]] the [[relative]] positions of places.

