===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To wind or turn in a course or passage
#: {{syn|en|wind|worm}}
#: {{ux|en|The stream '''meandered''' through the valley.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1881|text=Instead of a rivulet '''meandering''' downwards, there was a foaming brown torrent racing over the ledge, carrying down great loose stones with it and falling with a loud roar far down into the unseen chasm below.|url=https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/On_the_Indian_Hills/OtgRAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22meandering+down%22&pg=PA172&printsec=frontcover|author=Edwin Lester Arnold|title=On the Indian Hills}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 November 18|author=Paul Bigland|title=New infrastructure and new rolling stock|journal=Rail|page=51|text=I'd forgotten how scenic parts of the line are - the railway crosses a host of streams while '''meandering''' through meadows or skirting woodland.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[intricate]].
#: {{ux|en|His speech '''meandered''' through various topics.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[wind]], [[turn]], or [[twist]]; to make [[flexuous]].
#* {{RQ:Drayton Poly-Olbion|passage=Her labyrinth-like ţurns, and mad '''meander'd''' trace{{...}}}}

