Page 1449 no man's land: -------- begin text --------
{{also|no-man's-land}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|noman's land}}
* {{l|en|no-man's land}}

===Etymology===
Originally from {{inh|en|enm|Nomanneslond}}.  Revived with new senses in a dispatch printed in the ''Times'' newspaper by Colonel {{w|Ernest Dunlop Swinton}} writing as "Eyewitness".

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈnoʊˌmænzˌlænd/|nocount=1}}
* {{hyphenation|en|no man's land}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|?|head=[[no]] [[man]][[-'s|'s]] [[land]]}}

# {{lb|en|military}} The ground between trenches where a soldier from either side would be easily targeted.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A space [[amidships]] used to keep [[block]]s, [[rope]]s, etc.; a space on a ship belonging to no one in particular to care for.
# Part of a [[prison]], [[hospital]] [[complex]], etc. where people are not normally allowed to go.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A place where no one can or should be.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=March 25 2006|author=Melissa Hoyos|title=‘'''No man’s land'''’ has no fire protection|journal=Tri City Herald
|passage=There’s a 137-square-mile chunk of Franklin County {{...}} referred to as "'''no man’s land'''" because it isn’t protected by any of the county’s four fire districts.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1867|author=T W Robertson|title=Caste|passage=Now, George, if you’re going to consider this question from the point of view of poetry, you’re off to '''No Man’s Land''', where I won’t follow you.}}
# {{lb|en|tennis}} The area between the backcourt and the space close to the net, from which it is difficult to return the ball.
# {{lb|en|politics|geography}} Territory, often disputed, that cannot be inhabited because of fear of conflict, especially:
## {{lb|en|historical}} Tracts of uninhabited territory close to the [[Iron Curtain]].
## The stretch of land between the border posts of two contiguous sovereign states, sometimes separated by great distance.
## Land not claimed by any recognized sovereign state; [[terra nullius]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} The fibrous sheath of the flexor tendons of the hand, specifically in the zone from the distal palmar crease to the proximal interphalangeal joint.

====Hypernyms====
* {{l|en|land}}

