Page 1459 oligotrophic: -------- begin text --------
==English==

===Etymology===
{{confix|en|oligo|trophic}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-oligotrophic.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|physiology|of a diet}} [[deficient]] in [[nutrition]] (providing little nourishment)
# {{lb|en|biology|of a body of water}} being poor in [[nutrient]]s and [[mineral]]s and therefore not having an excessive growth of [[algae]] and thus a no diminished [[oxygen]] content to other organisms.
#:{{antonyms|en|eutrophic}}
# {{lb|en|geography|of a wetland}} deficient in plant [[nutrient]]s, such as [[nitrogen]] or [[phosphorus]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1969|month=July|author=Fred W. Rabe; Robert C. Wissmar|title=Some Effects of Antimycin in an '''Oligotrophic''' Lake|journal=The Progressive Fish-Culturist|section=volume XXXI, № 3, page 163}}

