# {{lb|en|historical}} [[any|Any]] of [[various]] [[historical]] [[county palatine|counties palatinate]], [[particularly]]:
## The [[County Palatinate of the Rhine]] or [[Electoral Palatinate]] of the [[Holy Roman Empire]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1759|author=George Sale; et al|chapter=The Modern Part of an Universal History|volume=XXIX|title=History of the German Empire|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=dFtjAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA2|page=2
|passage=Since the reign of ''[[Charlemagne]]'', this country is divided into ''[[High Germany|High]]'' and ''[[Low Germany]]'': the [[first|firſt]], towards the [[south|ſouth]], comprehending the '''''[[Palatinate]]''''' of the ''[[Rhine]]'', ''[[Franconia]]'', ''Suabia'', ''[[Bavaria]]'', ''[[Bohemia]]'', ''[[Moravia]]'', ''[[Austria|Auſtria]]'', ''[[Carinthia]]'', ''[[Carniola]]'', ''[[Stiria]]'', ''[[Tyrol]]'', the ''[[Swiss|Swiſs]]'', and the ''[[Grisons|Griſons]]''...}}
# {{lb|en|geography}} The [[area]] of the [[former]] [[German]] [[County Palatinate of the Rhine|County Palatinate]] as a [[region]] of [[modern]] [[Germany]].

