====Verb====
[[File:Alaska Gold in pan.jpg|thumb|'''panned''' gold]]
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To wash in a pan (of earth, sand etc. when searching for gold).
#: {{cot|en|sluice}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1875|author=w:William Tecumseh Sherman|title=Memoirs
|passage=We {{...}} witnessed the process of cleaning up and '''panning''' out, which is the last process of separating the pure gold from the fine dirt and black sand.}}
# {{senseid|en|criticize}}{{lb|en|transitive}} To [[disparage]]; to [[belittle]]; to [[put down]]; to harshly [[criticize]], especially a work (book, movie, etc.)
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:criticize}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Tiffany Hsu|title=All Those Celebrities Pushing Crypto Are Not So Vocal Now|work=The New York Times|date=2022-05-17|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/17/business/media/crypto-gwyneth-paltrow-matt-damon-reese-witherspoon.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Matt Damon, who compared the advent of virtual money to the development of aviation and spaceflight in a critically '''panned''' but widely seen Crypto.com ad last year, did not respond to requests to weigh in.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|with [[out]], to [[pan out]]}} To turn out well; to be successful.
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal|of a contest}} To [[beat]] one's opposition [[convincingly]].

=====Translations=====
