==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɑrki/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɑːki/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑː(ɹ)ki|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{suffix|en|park|y}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# Of, from, or [[related]] to a [[park]] or [[parks]] [[generally]], [[especially]] [[parklike]].
#: {{ux|en|We went to a beautiful '''parky''' place over by the river.}}
# [[having|Having]] [[park]]s or [[parklike]] [[area]]s.
#: {{ux|en|[[Yellowstone]] has always been '''parky''' country.}}

=====Hyponyms=====
* {{l|en|parkish}}, {{l|en|parklike}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{alternative spelling of|en|parkie}}: a [[parkkeeper]].

===Etymology 2===
{{uncertain|en}}, but probably from [[#Etymology 1|''parky'']] above or from dialectical pronunciation of {{m|en|perky}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|British|informal}} {{synonym of|en|chilly}}: [[somewhat]] [[cold]] but not [[extremely]] so.
#* {{quote-text|en|date=March 6 2007|author=w:Julie Rutterford|title=[[:w:Life_on_Mars_(British_TV_series)|Life on Mars]]|section=[[:w:List_of_Life_on_Mars_(British_TV_series)_episodes|Season 2, Episode 3]]
|passage=''Gene Hunt:'' [''seeing a woman in a [[sari]]''] A bit '''parky''' to be out in just her [[nighty]].}}

