====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|nautical}} To raise the point of (a [[gaff]]) closer to [[perpendicular]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}}
## To reach a [[highest]] [[degree]] or maximum.
##: {{ux|en|Historians argue about when the Roman Empire began to '''peak''' and ultimately decay.}}
## To rise or extend into a peak or point; to form, or appear as, a peak.
##* {{RQ:Livy Holland Romane Historie|passage=There '''peaketh''' up a mightie high mounte.}}
# {{senseid|en|gcfem}}{{lb|en|[[gender-critical feminism|gender-critical]]}} To cause to adopt [[gender-critical]] or [[trans-exclusionary]] views ([[ellipsis]] of {{m|en|peak trans}}).
#*{{quote-web|en|date=4 August 2019|passage=I came to this via sport but the thing that really '''peaked''' me was this.|author=Alison Weir (@WeirAlison)|site=w:Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/WeirAlison/status/1158259318875152384|archivedate=|archiveurl=}}
#*{{quote-web|en|date=31 August 2019|passage=My friend '''peaked''' me last year, at the GRA [Gender Recognition Act] consultation.|author=MrsMiggins (@MrsMiggins13)|site=w:Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/MrsMiggins13/status/1167932262836404224|archivedate=|archiveurl=}}
#*{{quote-web|en|date=22 November 2021|passage=Solidarity from Spain, @jk_rowling. Thank you for '''peaking''' so many people all over the world.|author=DefendingMySisters (@DefendingMy)|site=w:Twitter|url=https://twitter.com/DefendingMy/status/1462874946380746753|archivedate=|archiveurl=}}
#* {{seemoreCites|en}}

