==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kʷel-}}
From {{der|en|LL.|polāris}} , equivalent to {{l|en|pole}} + {{l|en|-ar}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpəʊ̯lə(ɹ)/|[ˈpʰəʊ̯lə(ɹ)]}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpoʊ̯lɚ/|[ˈpʰoʊ̯lɚ]}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-polar.wav|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊlə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of or having a [[pole]] or [[polarity]], as:
## {{lb|en|geography}} Of, relating to, measured from, or referred to a [[geographic]] [[pole]] (the [[North Pole]] or [[South Pole]]); within the [[Arctic Circle|Arctic]] or [[Antarctic Circle|Antarctic]] circles.
## {{lb|en|space sciences}} Of an [[orbit]] that passes over, or near, one of these poles.
## {{lb|en|chemistry}} Having a [[dipole]]; [[ionic]].
## {{lb|en|mathematics}} Of a [[coordinate]] [[system]], specifying the [[location]] of a [[point]] in a [[plane]] by using a [[radius]] and an [[angle]].
## {{lb|en|linguistics|of a [[question]]}} Having but [[two]] possible [[answer]]s, ''[[yes]]'' and ''[[no]]''.
## {{lb|en|conceptual analysis}} Of or relating to a pole (extreme) on any spectrum or field, such as an ideologically pure [[dogmatic]] position as opposed to any [[syncretic]] integration or balancing of competing principles.
##: {{collocation|en|'''polar''' viewpoints}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|en|polar bear|polar body|polarity|polarise|polarize|polarisation|polarization|non-polar|polar antonym|polar area diagram|polar bear dip|polar bear plunge|polar bear swim|polar cap|polar circle|polar cod|polar cone|polar coordinates|polar covalent bond|polar dog|polar equation|polar fox|polar ice|polar lights|polar moment of inertia|polar night|polar question|polar star|polar stratospheric cloud|polar vortex|polar wander|polar willow|polar wolf|space polar coordinate|polar motion|polar nucleus|polar opposite}}

