Page 1506 pycnophylactic: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia|Dasymetric map}}

===Etymology===
{{prefix|en|pycno|phylactic}}. Coined by [[w:Waldo Tobler|Waldo Tobler]] in his 1979 paper "Smooth Pycnophylactic Interpolation for Geographical Regions", ''Journal of the American Statistical Association'', volume 74, number 367, pages 519-536.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|geography}} Relating to a kind of areal [[interpolation]] that preserves [[density]] within defined regions.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988| title=Traffic Zones Reconsidered|author=Peter Stanley Lindquist | page=66| passage=If intrazonal homogeneity cannot be maintained in cases where similar land uses lie in adjacent zones and dissimilar land uses lie within the same zone, then the '''pycnophylactic''' method may be favored.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005| title=Thematic Cartography and Geographic Visualization |author=Terry A. Slocum; Robert B. McMaster; Fritz C. Kessler | page=286| passage=Although the '''pycnophylactic''' method is arguably more appropriate for isopleth mapping than point-based interpolation methods, it must be emphasized that the method should only be used with continuous phenomenon.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 23, 2019|work=PLOS One|title=A geographically weighted random forest approach for evaluate forest change drivers in the Northern Ecuadorian Amazon|author=Fabián Santos; Valerie Graw; Santiago Bonilla|volume=|number=|passage=We iterated the algorithm with 20 census variables (see Section 1.3.3) to obtain population density surfaces. In all cases, the '''pycnophylactic''' property [85] was verified by adding population density surface pixels and comparing them with their original values.}}
-------- end text --------
