# Of, from, or [[concerning]] [[Ravenna]], a [[major]] [[city]] in [[Italy]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1958|author=Pieter Singelenberg|chapter=The Iconography of the Etschmiadzin Diptych and the Healing of the Blind Man at Siloe|title=Art Bulletin
|passage=He held at first that this work had originated from a '''Ravennate''' workshop.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|Ravennese}}, {{l|en|Ravennan}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|rare}} One of the [[Ravennese]]: a [[native]] or [[inhabitant]] of [[Ravenna]] in [[Italy]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1980|title=Dragmalogia of Giovanni da Ravenna on the Preferable Way of Life|volume=7
|passage=...shortly after he arrived in his adopted city the signore Guido II da Polenta appointed Giovanni as one of the '''Ravennates''' who served as foreign notaries at the podesla's court in Florence.}}

