Page 1516 Red Sea: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Red See}}, {{m|enm|Reede See}}, {{m|enm|Rede See}}, {{m|enm|reade sea}}, from {{inh|en|ang|Rēad Sǣ}}, a calque of {{der|en|la|Mare Rubrum}}, itself a calque of {{der|en|grc|Ἐρυθρᾱ̀ θάλασσα}}; equivalent to {{af|en|red|sea}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[red|Red]] [[sea|Sea]]}}

# {{place|en|A long, narrow <<sea>> between [[Africa]] and the [[Arabian Peninsula]]; links the [[Suez Canal]] with the [[Arabian Sea]]}}.
# {{lb|en|US politics}} The [[state]]s of the [[western]] and [[southern]] [[United States]] which consistently [[vote]] [[Republican]] in [[presidential]] [[election]]s.

====Usage notes====
* One common [[simile]] is to ''part (something) like the Red Sea'', referring to the Biblical tale of the {{w|Parting of the Red Sea}}.

