===Etymology===
{{calque|en|fr|Montagnes de Roche}} first recorded in 1752 by Jacques Legardeur de Saint-Pierre, believed to itself be a calque from an indigenous language, possibly a {{calque|en|crk|ᐊᓯᓃᐘᒋᕀ|tr=[[asinîwaciy]]|nocap=1|nocat=1}}, a compound which includes {{m|crk|ᐊᓯᓂᕀ|tr=[[asiniy]]||rock}} + {{m|crk|ᐘᒋᕀ|tr=[[waciy]]||mountain}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-plural proper noun|head=the [[rocky|Rocky]] [[mountain|Mountains]]|sg=Rocky Mountain}}

# {{place|en|A range of <<mountains>> running from Northern [[New Mexico]] to [[Alaska]]}}.
