<!--Regarding synonyms: Although the {{w|Battle of the Bulge}} was named for a salient as termed a "bulge", the noun "[[bulge#Noun|bulge]]" is not generally otherwise a synonym of "salient" in military usage.-->
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1919|title=Americans Defending Democracy: Our Soldiers' Own Stories|publisher=World's War Stories, Inc.|chapter=General Pershing's Story|page=9|passage=On April 26 the First Division had gone into the line in the Montdidier '''salient''' on the Picardy battlefront.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1978|author=w:Jan Morris|title=Farewell the Trumpets|location=New York|publisher=Harcourt Brace Jovanovich|chapter=9|page=193|url=https://archive.org/details/farewelltrumpets00janm|passage=The battlefronts were often no more than a few hundred yards wide, and the '''salients''' never more than a few miles deep.}}
