Page 1545 sector principle: -------- begin text --------
==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# A principle in [[international law]] where international boundaries are extended over sea areas in the [[Arctic]] towards the [[North Pole]] following [[meridian]]s (lines of longitude). The same principle is used over land in the Antarctic to the South Pole.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Law of the Sea and Polar Maritime Delimitation and Jurisdiction|editor=Alex G. Oude Elferink|year=2001|passage=The Canadian authorities have also relied upon the '''sector principle''' for the purposes of the Inuvialuet Land Claim and the Nunavut boundary.}}

