{{la-ndecl|sinus<4>}}

=====Quotations=====
''Aeneid'' (Pūblius Vergilius Marō) lines 1.160&ndash;161:
Latin: ''quibus omnis ab altō // frangitus inque sinūs scindit sēsē&#x361; unda reductōs.''
English: on which all the waves from the deep are broken and it splits itself into receeding ripples.

