==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{confix|en|socio|tope}}; compare {{cog|de|Soziotop}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsəʊʃiə(ʊ)ˌtəʊp/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsoʊʃiəˌtoʊp/|/ˈsoʊʃioʊˌtoʊp/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[geographical]] [[area]] that has a uniform [[social]] [[environment]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Johan Galtung|chapter=Development Theory|page=202|url=https://www.google.co.nz/books/edition/Wisdom_in_the_Open_Air/lijSesXIxz0C|title=Wisdom in the Open Air:The Norwegian Roots of Deep Ecology|editors= David Rothenberg; Peter Reed|year=1993|passage=Let us further assume a Chinese boxes logic again: the world space is an extremely rich '''sociotope''', in interaction so far with no other '''sociotope''', and all the others are nested within.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Alexander Ståhle|page=63|url=http://arkitekturforskning.net/na/article/viewFile/134/105|title=Sociotope mapping – exploring public open space and its multiple use values in urban and landscape planning practice|work=Nordic Journal of Architectural Research|volume=19|issue=4|year=2006|passage=The Leisure and Nature Administration at the municipality initiated a '''sociotope''' mapping project to collect knowledge in the open space use values.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author= Patrick Beuth; et al.|page=63|url=https://www.spiegel.de/international/world/the-most-dangerous-cult-of-our-times-qanon-s-inexorable-spread-beyond-the-u-s-a-e2b13c80-246a-43e5-945b-80ad7767a170|title=QAnon's Inexorable Spread Beyond the U.S.|work=Spiegel International|date=24 September 2020|passage=Diaz is an avowed fan of Donald Trump and emerged from the large '''sociotope''' of right-wing radio hosts in the U.S.}}

====Related terms====
* [[biotope]]

