====Adverb====
{{en-adv}}

# Soundly.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|canto=I|book=I|stanza=42|passage=So '''{{long s}}ound''' he {{long s}}lept, that nought [[mought]] him awake.}}

====Interjection====
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|British|Ireland|slang}} [[yes|Yes]]; {{n-g|used to show agreement or understanding, generally without much [[enthusiasm]].}}
#: {{ux|en|I found my jacket. — '''Sound'''.}}

===Etymology 2===
* Noun: from {{inh|en|enm|sownde}}, alteration of {{m|enm|soun}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|sun}}, {{m|xno|soun}}, {{der|en|fro|son}}, from accusative of {{der|en|la|sonus}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*swenh₂-||to sound, resound}}.
* Verb: from {{inh|en|enm|sownden}}, {{m|enm|sounen}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|suner}}, {{m|fro|sounder}}, {{der|en|fro|soner}} (modern {{m|fr|sonner}}), from {{der|en|la|sonō}}.
* The hypercorrect '''-d''' appears in the fifteenth century. (Compare dialectal {{m|en|drownd|drown'''d'''}}, {{m|en|gownd|gown'''d'''}} for the same development.)
Displaced native {{ncog|enm|swei}}, from {{ncog|ang|swēġ}}, from {{ncog|gem-pro|*swōgiz}}.
{{wikipedia}}

[[File:Thoth08BigasDrumEvansChalmette.jpg|thumb|right|upright|A [[drum]] produces '''sound''' via a vibrating membrane.]]
[[File:Sound Effect - Door Bell.ogg|thumb|'''Sound''' of a [[doorbell]].]]

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[sensation]] [[perceived]] by the [[ear]] caused by the [[vibration]] of [[air]] or some other [[medium]].
#: {{ux|en|He turned when he heard the '''sound''' of footsteps {{nowrap|behind him}}.&emsp; {{nowrap|Nobody made a '''sound'''.}}}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|I|passage=The warlike '''sound''' <br> Of trumpets loud and clarions.}}
# A [[vibration]] capable of causing such sensations.
#* {{quote-book|en|page=501|title={{w|Encyclopædia Britannica|Encyclopaedia Britannica; Or A Dictionary of Arts, Sciences, and Miscellaneous Literature}}| year=1820| volume=20| publisher=Archibald Constable and Company| location=Edinburgh| edition=6th| url=https://books.google.co.nz/books?id=LOQnAAAAMAAJ| passage= In trumpets for assisting the hearing, all reverbation of the trumpet must be avoided. It must be made thick, of the least elastic materials, and covered with cloth externally. For all reverbation lasts for a short time, and produces new '''sounds''' which mix with those which are coming in.}}
#* {{RQ:Weyman Chippinge Borough|I|01|passage=It was April 22, 1831, and a young man was walking down Whitehall in the direction of Parliament Street.{{nb...}}. He halted opposite the Privy Gardens, and, with his face turned skywards, listened until the '''sound''' of the Tower guns smote again on the ear and dispelled his doubts.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} A [[distinctive]] [[style]] and [[sonority]] of a [[particular]] [[musician]], [[orchestra]] etc.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1954|author=Valentine Davies; et al|title=w:The Glenn Miller Story
|passage=He looks like he's got it, maybe. Listen to those kids!<br>There's no maybe about it. That's it, that's the '''sound'''.}}
# Noise without meaning; empty noise.
#* {{RQ:Locke Human Understanding|Of Power|section=18|23|For let us conſider this Prepoſition as to its meaning, (for it is the ſence, and not '''ſound''', that is and muſt be the Principle or common Notion) {{...}}}}
# {{l|en|earshot|Earshot}}, distance within which a certain noise may be heard.
#: {{ux|en|Stay within the '''sound''' of my voice.}}
# {{lb|en|phonetics}} A [[segment]] as a part of spoken language, the smallest unit of spoken language, a [[speech sound]].

