===Etymology===
From {{inh|enm|ang|stæpe}}, {{m|enm|stepe}}, from {{inh|enm|gmw-pro|*stapi}}. The (historical) geminate is due to the influence of {{m|enm|steppen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|enm|/ˈstɛp(ə)/|/ˈstɛːp(ə)/|/ˈstap(ə)/|/ˈstaːp(ə)/}}

===Noun===
{{enm-noun|steppes}}

# A {{l|en|step}}, [[pace]] {{gloss|movement of the foot}}
# A step or stair; an individual landing of a set of stairs.
# An imprint or sign of something; that which something leaves as evidence:
## The imprint left by a step; a footprint or track.
## The imprint left by a thing, person or phenomenon (extant or former)
## {{lb|enm|figurative}} The remains left by an injury or disease.
# The bottom region of the foot; the [[sole]].
# A phase, step or tier as part of a scale or process.
# {{lb|enm|figurative}} A move, action or direction (towards an objective).
# {{lb|enm|rare}} The length covered by a step (as a unit of length, ~2.5 feet)
# {{lb|enm|rare}} The ground; a foothold or stepping-place.
# {{lb|enm|rare}} A group or a thing that is part of it.

