#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=May 7, 1996
|author=w:John Noble Wilford
|title=Mummies, Textiles Offer Evidence Of Europeans in Far East
|journal=w:The New York Times
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20090807140644/https://www.nytimes.com/1996/05/07/science/mummies-textiles-offer-evidence-of-europeans-in-far-east.html
|issn=0362-4331
|oclc=1645522
|section=SCIENCE
|url2=https://archive.li/TsaHe
|text=More surprises were in store. In the last two decades, Chinese archeologists digging in the same region, the '''Tarim Basin''' in Xinjiang Province, have uncovered more than 100 naturally mummified corpses of people who lived there 4,000 to 2,400 years ago.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1999
|author=w:Elizabeth Wayland Barber
|title=The Mummies of Ürümchi
|url=https://archive.org/details/mummiesofurumchi00barb/
|publisher=w:W. W. Norton & Company
|ISBN=0-393-04521-8
|LCCN=98-18958
|OCLC=468515927
|page=43
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/mummiesofurumchi00barb/page/43/
|text=At Cherchen, the only town of any size in the entire southeastern quadrant of the '''Tarim Basin''' (itself an oval 400 by 800 miles in diameter, mostly desert), they learned that locals had discovered an extensive antique cemetery on a plateau above the nearby hamlet of Zaghunluq.}}
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=OCTOBER 4, 2019
|author=Aizhu in Singapore Chen; Sun Yilei in Shanghai
|title=PetroChina unit strikes high oil, gas flows in deep Tarim well
|editor=Kenneth Maxwell
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20191005081811/https://www.reuters.com/article/us-china-petrochina-discovery-tarim-idUSKBN1WJ0PN
|archivedate=05 October 2019
|work=w:Reuters
|section=Commodities
|text=The '''Tarim basin''' currently has an annual production capacity of over 2 million tonnes of condensate and 10 bcm of natural gas.}}
#* {{seemoreCites|en}}

