#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Dec 11 1880|title=The Fortune Bay Outrage: Lord Granville's Letter to Minister Lowell|titleurl=http://query.nytimes.com/mem/archive-free/pdf?res=FB0A1EFD395B1B7A93C3A81789D95F448884F9|journal=New York Times|accessdate=22 June 2012
|passage=Her Majesty's Government do not interpret these expressions in any sense derogatory to the sovereign authority of Great Britain in the '''territorial waters''' of Newfoundland.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1909|author=w:Bram Stoker|title=The Lady of the Shroud|section=Book 7
|passage=You are not merely within '''territorial waters''', but you have invaded a national port.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Nov 10 2009|author=Bill Powell|title=Before Obama's Visit, a New Clash Between Koreas|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120606010301/http://www.time.com/time/world/article/0,8599,1937150,00.html|journal=Time
|passage=According to the South Korean joint chiefs of staff, a North Korean gunboat ventured about a mile into what Seoul claims is its '''territorial waters'''.}}

