==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:World map indicating tropics and subtropics.png|thumb|The '''tropics'''.]]

===Noun===
{{head|en|noun form}}

# {{plural of|en|tropic}}

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun}}

# {{lb|en|geography}} The region of the [[Earth]] centred on the [[equator]] and lying between the [[Tropic of Cancer]] and the [[Tropic of Capricorn]] and characterized by a hot [[climate]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=165|passage=The day was ending; night comes on very quickly in the '''tropics''', and as yet there was no moon visible.}}
#* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|page=201|passage=‘In the '''tropics''' one must before everything keep calm.’...He lifted a warning forefinger...‘''Du calme, du calme''.’}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|tropical zone}}
* {{l|en|torrid zone}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|tropical}}

