Page 1601 underground: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Underground}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|undergrounde|pos=adv}}, equivalent to {{compound|en|under|ground}}. Compare {{cog|nl|ondergrond}}, {{m|nl|ondergronds}}, {{cog|de|Untergrund}}, {{cog|da|undergrunds}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˌʌndəˈɡɹaʊnd/|/ˈʌndəɡɹaʊnd/|qual2=especially for the noun}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-underground.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˌʌndɚˈɡɹaʊnd/|/ˈʌndɚɡɹaʊnd/|qual2=especially for the noun}}
* {{rhymes|en|aʊnd|s=3}}
* {{hyphenation|en|un|der|ground}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|not comparable}} Below the ground; below the surface of the Earth.
#: {{syn|en|subterranean|hypogean}}
#: {{ux|en|There is an '''underground''' tunnel that takes you across the river.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2014-06-14|volume=411|issue=8891|magazine=w:The Economist|title=It's a gas|url=http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21604091-it-possible-sniff-out-problems-sewer-pipes-they-happen-its-gas|passage=One of the hidden glories of Victorian engineering is proper drains. Isolating a city’s effluent and shipping it away in '''underground''' sewers has probably saved more lives than any medical procedure except vaccination.}}
# {{anchor|hidden}} {{lb|en|figurative}} [[hidden|Hidden]], [[furtive]], [[secretive]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:hidden|Thesaurus:covert}}
#: {{ux|en|These criminals operate through an '''underground''' network.}}
# {{lb|en|of|_|music|art|_|etc.}} [[outside|Outside]] the [[mainstream]], [[especially]] [[unofficial]] and [[hidden]] from the [[authorities]].
#: {{syn|en|unconventional|alternative}}
#: {{ant|en|mainstream}}
#: {{ux|en|'''underground''' music}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=w:Stephen Fry|title=The Liar| page=27|passage=‘{{...}}he wrote to me last week telling me about an incredible bitch of a row blazing there on account of someone having been and gone and produced an unofficial magazine called ''Raddled'', full of obscene libellous Oz-like filth. And what I though, what Sammy and I thought, was—why not?’ ‘Why not what?’ said Tom. ‘Why not do the same thing here?’ ‘You mean an '''underground''' magazine?’ ‘Yup.’}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=Barry Miles: 'I think of the 60s as a supermarket of ideas. We were looking for new ways to live'|date=2010-03-20|author=James Campbell|work=The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/books/2010/mar/20/barry-miles-sixties-indica-interview|passage="In many ways, it showed there was no longer an '''underground''', as such. This proved that there was no longer one society with everyone agreeing how to live . . . The '''underground''' had officially come above ground, and consequently no longer existed."}}

