===See also===
* [[:Category:en:Countries]]
* [[Appendix:Countries and territories of the world]]
* [[Appendix:English nationality prefixes]]
* {{section link|Appendix:Roget_MICRA_thesaurus/Class_V#737a._Government}}

===Notes===
* This entry is designed to cover two co-occurring entities: an organization and a territory. The organization has e.g. state organs as its parts, whereas the territory has locations as its parts. This duality extends to administrative divisions. By contrast, WordNet has these two entities neatly separated. From a linguistic thesaurus perspective, having these two merged seems justifiable, and corresponds to how e.g. [[France]] is defined using a single sense and not two separate senses, one for the organization and another one for the territory. Wikidata seems overengineered.
* Only sovereign countries are included, not constituent countries such as [[England]].

===Further reading===
* {{R:Moby II}}
* {{R:WordNet 2006|country}} < political unit < organization < social group
* {{R:WordNet 2006|country}} (territory) < administrative district < district < region < location
* {{R:NCIT|C25464|Country}} < Geographic Area < Conceptual Entity
* [[Wikidata:Q6256]]: country < political territorial entity < administrative territorial entity < human-geographic territorial entity < territory < geographic region < geographical feature < geographic location < location
* [[Wikidata:Q3624078]]: sovereign state < country, state
* [[Wikidata:Q7275]]: state (a sovereign state, constituent state, or federated state) < organization, political territorial entity, administrative territorial entity
* [https://pesd.princeton.edu/node/676 State/Nation-State], princeton.edu
* [https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/sovereignty/ Sovereignty], plato.stanford.edu
* [https://www.worlddata.info/definition-country.php What is a country?], worlddata.info

