==Erzya==

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|myv|*mastə̑r}}. At least the first component is cognate to Finnish [[maa]] (from {{inh|myv|urj-pro|*mëxe}}). Proper names (toponyms like [[Арзамас]] ({{m|myv|Eŕźamas}}<ref>https://www.mv.helsinki.fi/home/rueter/Paasonen/ORIGINALS/mw_styles_e_.shtml</ref>) and personal names [[Инемас]], [[Келемас]]) point on existing of the shortened form [[-мас]].

===Noun===
{{head|myv|noun}}

# [[land]]
# [[country]], [[state]]
# [[countryside]]

