==Galician==

===Etymology 1===
From contraction of preposition {{m-lite|gl|a||to, towards}} + feminine definite article {{m-lite|gl|a||the}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|gl|[aː]}}

====Contraction====
{{head|gl|contraction|g=f|masculine|ao|masculine plural|aos|feminine plural|ás}}

# [[to]] [[the]], [[towards]] the

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh-lite|gl|roa-opt|aa}} (13th century, ''{{w|Cantigas de Santa Maria}}''), from {{inh-lite|gl|la|ala}}. Compare {{cog-lite|pt|á}}. {{doublet|gl|ala}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|gl|[ˈa]}}

====Noun====
{{gl-noun|f}}

# [[wing]]
#* '''c1350''', K. M. Parker (ed.), ''Historia Troyana''. Santiago: Instituto "Padre Sarmiento", page 30:
#*: {{quote|gl|''et '''as''' de leychuza''
|translation=and '''wings''' of an owl}}
#* {{quote-text|gl|year=1697|author=Juan Antonio Torrado|title=Fala o corvo
|passage=''Fala o corbo, escoyten todos:''<br>''Eu veño con '''asas''' negras''<br>''Cortando os ventos de longe''<br>''Para chegar à estas festas.''
|translation=The raven speaks, listen everyone:<br>"I come with black '''wings'''<br>Cutting the winds from afar<br>To arrive to these feasts"}}
#: {{syn|gl|ala}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l-lite|gl|axar}}

===References===
* {{R:gl:DDGM|aa}}
* {{R:gl:DDLG}}
* {{R:gl:TILG}}
* {{R:TLPGP}}

