===Etymology 1===
From {{m-lite|ga|dhá}}, lenited variant of {{m-lite|ga|dá}}.

====Pronoun====
{{ga-pron|type=personal|desc=triggers {{ga-mut-link|l}} in the masculine singular, {{ga-mut-link|h}} in the feminine singular, and {{ga-mut-link|e}} in the plural}}

# [[him]], [[her]], [[it]], [[them]] {{qualifier|used before the verbal noun in the progressive to indicate a third person direct object}}
#: {{ux|ga|Táim '''á''' bhualadh.|inline=1|I am hitting him.}}
#: {{ux|ga|Táim '''á''' ól.|I am drinking it {{qualifier|referring to a masculine noun, e.g. {{m-lite|ga|bainne||milk}}}}.}}
#: {{ux|ga|Táim '''á''' bualadh.|inline=1|I am hitting her.}}
#: {{ux|ga|Táim '''á''' hól.|I am drinking it {{qualifier|referring to a feminine noun, e.g. {{m-lite|ga|bláthach||buttermilk}}}}.}}
#: {{ux|ga|Táim '''á''' mbualadh.|inline=1|I am hitting them.}}
#: {{ux|ga|Táim '''á''' n-ól.|inline=1|I am drinking them.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|used as a quasi-reflexive pronoun in a sentence with passive semantics}}
#: {{ux|ga|Tá an buachaill '''á''' bhualadh.|The boy is being hit {{qualifier|literally ‘The boy is at his hitting’}}.}}
#: {{ux|ga|Tá an chloch '''á''' tógáil ag Séamas.|The stone is being lifted by Séamas {{qualifier|literally ‘The stone is at its lifting by Séamas’}}.}}

