==Latvian==
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=lv}}
[[File:Horse with swishy tail.jpg|250px|thumb|Zirgs un zirga aste (1)]]
[[File:Swiss International Air Lines (SWISS) Airplane Tail - Feb 2013.jpg|thumb|250px|Lidmašīnas '''aste''' (2)]]

===Etymology===
Originally an ''e''-stem variant of an earlier ''i''/''n''-stem {{m|lv|*astis}}, from {{der|lv|bat-pro|-}} {{m|ine-bsl-pro|*asti-}} < {{m|ine-bsl-pro|*aš-sti-}}. Further, two possible {{der|lv|ine-pro|-}} sources have been proposed: (a) {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-sti-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-}} “sharp, pointy, edgy; stone” (whence also {{m|lv|ass}} “sharp”, [[q.v.]]), with the meaning changes being “sharp, pointy (object)” > “stinger” > “tail”; and (b) {{m|ine-pro|*h₃ésth₁|*h₃ésth₁-|bone}}, in which case the semantic evolution would have been “bone” > “tail bone” > “tail” ([[cf.]] {{noncog|is|rōfa||dog's, cat's tail}} from {{noncog|non|rófa||bony part of a horse's tail}}). In the (a) case, cognates would include {{cog|lt|akstìs||skewer, fish bone}} {{m|lt|akštìs||skewer, fish bone, awn}}, {{cog|cu|осътъ||thorny water plant}}, {{m|cu|остъ||awn, stinger, fish bone}}, {{cog|ru|ость}}, {{cog|cs|osť}}, {{cog|pl|ość}}, {{cog|ru|осот||thorny plant}}, {{cog|bg|о́сът}}, {{cog|cs|-}}, {{cog|pl|oset}}. In the (b) case, cognates would include {{cog|hit|*ḫaštai}}, {{cog|sa|अस्थि}}, {{cog|grc|ὀστέον}}, {{cog|sq|asht}}, {{cog|txb|āsta}}, {{cog|la|os}} (and maybe also {{m|la|costa||rib}}), and perhaps also all the (a) cognates, which some authors also derive from {{m|ine-pro|*h₃ésth₁|*h₃ésth₁-}}.<ref>{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{lv-IPA|astɛ}}
{{audio|lv|lv-riga-aste.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{lv-noun|f|5th}}

# {{lb|lv|anatomy}} ([[long]]) [[tail]]
#: {{ux|lv|zirga '''aste'''|horse '''tail'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|suņa '''aste'''|dog '''tail'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|vilka '''aste'''|wolf '''tail'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|gaiļa '''aste'''|rooster '''tail'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|pāva '''aste'''|peacock '''tail'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|kaķis pa to laiku bija izlavījies no pagalma un, izlējis '''asti''', lēni gāja prom|the cat, meanwhile, had gotten out of the yard and, straightening (his) '''tail''', slowly went away|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|kas sunim '''asti''' cels, ja pats necels|who is going to raise a dog's '''tail''' if not for the dog himself|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|of [[object]]s}} [[tail]] {{gloss|[[extended]] [[part]] at the [[end]]}}
#: {{ux|lv|lidmašīnas '''aste'''|airplane '''tail'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|kleitas '''aste'''|dress '''tail'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|komētas '''aste'''|comet's '''tail'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|garas rindas stāvēja pie kasēm... paša '''astē''' iestājās arī tēvs|there were long lines at the cashiers... father joined at the very '''tail''' ({{=}} end) (of one of the lines)|inline=1}}

====Usage notes====
Basically, {{m|lv|aste}} refers to long tails like a horse's, while {{m|lv|ļipa}} refers to short tails like a rabbit's.

====Declension====
{{lv-decl-noun|as|e|5th||t|t|extrawidth=-60}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|lv|ļipa}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|lv|astains}}

