Page 1907 kluuvi: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Kluuvi}}
==Finnish==
{{wikipedia|lang=fi}}

===Etymology===
< {{der|fi|sv|glo}}

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# {{lb|fi|geography}} A shallow body of fresh or slightly [[brackish]] water typical for some coastal regions of the [[Baltic Sea]]; a former sea bay which has been separated from the sea in the process of [[postglacial rebound]]. Typically it has no [[catchment basin]] of any significance, and it gets new water only through direct precipitation or occasionally from the sea when the sea water level is high.

====Usage notes====
* [[slough]] and [[bayou]] are somewhat similar to {{m|fi||kluuvi}}, but not quite the same
* The term "gloe" is sometimes used as English translation for {{m|fi||kluuvi}}. The term is not found in English dictionaries, however, and before using it one should make sure that the audience understands the word.

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-risti|kluuv|||a}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|fi|kluuviflada}}

====See also====
* {{l|fi|flada}} {{qualifier|intermediate step in formation of a "kluuvi"}}
* {{l|fi|marskimaa}} {{qualifier|salt marsh}}
