==Norwegian Bokmål==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|nb|de|Aber||objection}}, a substantivization of {{der|nb|de|aber||but, however, though}} (as in "no buts and no ifs"), from {{der|nb|gmh|aber}}, {{m|gmh|aver}}, from {{der|nb|goh|aber}}, {{m|goh|abur}}, {{m|goh|aver}}, {{m|goh|avur}}, {{m|goh|afur||however, but}}, '''either''' from {{der|nb|gem-pro|*afar}}, {{m|gem-pro|*abar}}, {{m|gem-pro|*abur||after, following}}, from {{der|nb|ine-pro|*apo-||away, from}}, '''or''' from {{der|nb|gem-pro|*aferą||behind}}, from pre-Germanic ''*h₂ép-erom'', accusative/allative to an adjective ''*h₂ép-eros''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nb|/ˈɑːbər/}}
* {{audio|nb|NB - Pronunciation of Norwegian Bokmål «aber».ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|nb|ɑːbər}}
* {{hyphenation|nb|ab|er}}

===Noun===
{{head|nb|noun|g=n|definite singular|aberet|indefinite plural|aber|or|abere|definite plural|abera|or|aberne}}

# a [[problem]], an [[obstacle]], a [[difficulty]]
#: {{ux|nb|Det er et '''aber''' med det.|There is a '''problem''' with it.}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1908|author={{w|Sven Elvestad|Kristian F. Biller}}|title=Lys og Skygge|passage=– Nei, virkelig, har De ikke spist. Det var et aber: vi kunde jo ha stukket indom en restaurant|t=- No, really, you have not eaten. It was a difficulty: we could have stopped by a restaurant}}
#* {{quote-journal|nb|year=1927|work=Tidens Tegn|text=det er bare den aber at staten eier den|t=it is only the catch that the state owns it}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1921|author={{w|Jonas Lie (writer)|Jonas Lie}}|title=Samlede Digterverker VII|page=87|passage=[det] kunde være enkelte abere at notere|t=[it] could be individual difficulties to note}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1907|author=w:Alexander L. Kielland|title=Samlede værker I (Mindeutgave)|page=78|passage=[hun hadde] været forlovet – riktignok bare ni uger – men det var dog et lidet aber|t=[she had] been engaged - admittedly only nine weeks - but it was still a suffering difficulty}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1879-1895|author=w:Knut Hamsun|title=Knut Hamsuns brev I|page=238|passage=det har vel sine aber det ogsaa|t=it probably has its difficulties too}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=2010|author=w:Lars Saabye Christensen|title=Bernhard Hvals forsnakkelser|passage=det eneste som måtte være et aber er at når jeg biter kjevene sammen og knusper, kjenner jeg bare de bløte gommene gli mot hverandre|t=the only thing that may be a difficulty is that when I bite my jaws together and crush, I only feel the soft palates slide against each other}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|nb|hake||catch}}, {{l|nb|ulempe||disadvantage}}, {{l|nb|vanskelighet||difficulty}}, {{l|nb|men||damage, injury}}

