==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{sense|a lie or exaggeration}} {{alter|en|🧢}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kæp/|[kʰæp]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-cap.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-cap.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|cap}}
* {{rhymes|en|æp|s=1}}
<!-- 1 syllable words !-->

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|cappe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cæppe}}, from {{der|en|LL.|cappa}}. {{doublet|en|cape|chape|cope}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A close-fitting [[hat]], either [[brimless]] or [[peak]]ed.
#: {{hypo|en|Thesaurus:headwear}}
#: {{ux|en|The children were all wearing '''caps''' to protect them from the sun.}}
# A special hat to [[indicate]] [[rank]], [[occupation]], etc.
# An [[academic]] [[mortarboard]].
# A [[protective]] [[cover]] or [[seal]].
#: {{ux|en|He took the '''cap''' off the bottle and splashed himself with some cologne.}}
# A [[crown]] for covering a [[tooth]].
#: {{ux|en|He had golden '''caps''' on his teeth.}}
# The [[summit]] of a [[mountain]], etc.
#: {{ux|en|There was snow on the '''cap''' of the mountain.}}
# An [[artificial]] [[upper]] [[limit]] or [[ceiling]].
#: {{ant|en|floor}}
#: {{ux|en|We should put a '''cap''' on the salaries, to keep them under control.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022-09-02|author=Alex Lawson|title=G7 countries agree plan to impose price '''cap''' on Russian oil|journal=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/sep/02/g7-poised-to-agree-plan-to-impose-price-cap-on-russian-oil|passage=The G7 countries have agreed to impose a price '''cap''' on Russian oil in an attempt to stem the flow of funds into the Kremlin’s war coffers. {{...}} The level of the '''cap''' is still being discussed.}}
# The top part of a [[mushroom]].
# {{lb|en|toy}} A small amount of [[percussive]] [[explosive]] in a [[paper]] [[strip]] or plastic [[cup]] for use in a [[toy]] [[gun]].
#: {{ux|en|Billy spent all morning firing '''caps''' with his friends, re-enacting storming the beach at Normandy.}}
# A small [[explosive]] device used to [[detonate]] a larger [[charge]] of explosives.
#: {{ux|en|He wired the '''cap''' to the bundle of dynamite, then detonated it remotely.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[bullet]] used to [[shoot]] someone.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2001|author=Charles Jade|url=http://arstechnica.com/wankerdesk/01q1/metreon/metreon-3.html|title=Jade goes to Metreon
|passage=Did he think they were going to put a '''cap''' in his ass right in the middle of Metreon?}}
# {{lb|en|slang|originally|AAVE}} A [[lie]] or [[exaggeration]].
#: {{ux|en|[[no cap|no '''cap''']]}}
#: {{ux|en|that's '''cap'''}}
# {{lb|en|sport}} A place on a national team; an [[international]] [[appearance]].
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Rio Ferdinand}} won his 50th '''cap''' for England in a game against Sweden.}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Lost World|passage="By the way, are you by any chance the Malone who is expected to get his Rugby '''cap''' for Ireland?" "A reserve, perhaps."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Daniel Taylor| title=Youthful England earn draw with Germany but Lingard rues late miss| work={{w|The Guardian}} (London)| date=10 November 2017| url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2017/nov/10/england-germany-friendly-match-report| passage=Overall, though, England’s injury-diminished side coped well on the night when Ruben Loftus-Cheek, Jordan Pickford and Tammy Abraham all won their first '''caps'''.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The top, or uppermost part; the chief.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Timon of Athens|IV|3|93|2|Thou art the '''Cap'''&nbsp;/ Of all the Fooles aliue.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A respectful uncovering of the head.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1655|author=w:Thomas Fuller|title=The Church History of Britain, from the Birth of Jesus Christ until the Year MDCXLVIII|location=London|publisher=Thomas Tegg and Son|year_published=1837|volume=1|page=9|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/churchhistoryofb01full/page/8|passage=He that will give a '''cap''' and make a leg, in thanks for a favour he never received, deserveth rather to be blamed for want of wit, than to be praised for store of manners.}}
# {{lb|en|zoology}} The whole top of the [[head]] of a [[bird]] from the base of the [[bill]] to the [[nape]] of the [[neck]].
# {{lb|en|architecture}} The uppermost of any assemblage of parts.
#: {{ux|en|the '''cap''' of column, door, etc.; a capital, coping, cornice, lintel, or plate}}
# Something covering the top or end of a thing for protection or ornament.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A collar of iron or wood used in joining spars, as the mast and the topmast, the bowsprit and the jib boom; also, a covering of tarred canvas at the end of a rope.
# {{lb|en|geometry}} A portion of a [[spherical]] or other [[convex]] surface.
# A large size of writing paper.
#: {{ux|en|flat '''cap'''; fools'''cap'''; legal '''cap'''}}

