Page 1974 Danube: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wp}}
{{swp|Danube (disambiguation)}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Danub||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Attested since at least 1598 (also note {{cog|enm|Danby||Danube}} att. in 15th c. ''Mandeville's Travels'').

Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|Danube}}, from {{der|en|fro|Danube}}, from {{der|en|la|Dānubius}}, from {{der|en|cel-pro|*Dānowyos}} (compare Welsh river name {{m|cy|Donwy}}), an extended form of the river-name {{m|cel-pro|*Dānu}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*déh₂nu||river, river goddess}}, akin to {{m|ine-pro|*dʰenh₂-||to set in motion; to flow}}.

Cognate with {{cog|la|fōns||spring}}, {{cog|fa|دنیدن||to hasten, run|tr=danidan}}, {{cog|os|дон||water, river}}, {{cog|sa|धन्वति|tr=dhánvati||it flows, runs}}. More at [[w:Danube#Etymology|Danube]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdænjuːb/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Danube.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-prop}}

# {{sid|en|Q1653}}{{place|en|river|continent/Europe|;|flowing 2850 km from the confluence of the {{w|Breg (river)|Breg}} and {{w|Brigach}} at [[Donaueschingen]], [[Germany]], into the [[Black Sea]] in [[Romania]]}}.
# {{place|en|locale|c/US|named for the river}}.
## {{place|en|town|s/New York}}.
## {{place|en|city|s/Minnesota}}.

