# {{l|en|polo}} {{gloss|sport}}
# [[polo shirt]]
#* {{quote-text|tl|year=1981|author=Clodualdo Del Mundo|title=Writing for Film
|passage=Maraming reklamo si Arni tungkol sa initiation; sisisihin pa nito si Sid dahil ito ang pumilit sa kanyang sumali sa frat. Magsusuot ng '''polo''' si Arni. Halos hindi niya maigalaw ang kanyang braso.
|translation=Arni have a lot of complaints about the initiation; he even blamed Sid for forcing him to join the frat. Arni would wear a polo shirt. He could almost not move his arms.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|tl|polo barong}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|tl|es|polo||corvée}}, which came from either:

* From {{m|tl|pulo}}, {{m|tl|ikapulo||tenth}} or {{l|en|tithe}} ({{m|es|diezmo|diezmos}} {{m|es|predial|prediales}}), for a tenth (10%) of the harvest is given to the Church.<ref name="Potet1"/><ref name="Potet2"/> Related to etymology 4.
* From corruption of ''polong'',<ref name="Agoncillo"/> Hispanicized spelling of {{der|tl|tl|pulong}}, meaning "community work". <ref name="Vocabulario"/>

====Pronunciation====
* {{hyph|tl|po|lo}}
* {{tl-IPA}}

====Noun====
{{tl-noun|b={{tl-bay sc}}}}

# [[unpaid]] [[compulsory]] [[work]]; [[corvée]]
#: {{syn|tl|atag}}
# [[tax]] [[levy|levied]] on the [[native]]s and paid as [[labor]], [[goods]], and/or [[money]]
#: {{syn|tl|buwis|tributo|alkabala|amilyar|impuwesto}}

