===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} {{l|en|Valium}}.
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=1997-05-29|author=Kate Sholl|title=Re: MED: Pain relief in Neck?|url=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!original/alt.med.fibromyalgia/nnusd23Vohg/lDTh_11UowQJ|newsgroup=alt.med.fibromyalgia|passage=and i must be on that list of people that need to get knocked over with a hammer 'cause vicodin and '''val''' don't knock me out.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=1998-12-29|author=rob [username]|title=Re: Depression and MS(leg/feet burning pain)|url=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!original/alt.support.mult-sclerosis/gaPKhTHD39I/pP3ce1LiP1oJ|newsgroup=alt.support.mult-sclerosis|passage=I would think though that whatever the reason for a panic attack valium would be great. I know that if my house was on fire and I was on 15mg of '''val''' It{{sic}} would take a lot more energy than I had, to panic. ;^)}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=2002-06-28|author=FllSpdAhd1 [username]|title=Re: Valium?|url=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!original/rec.pets.cats.health+behav/03ZMpEg7OBg/0djskNXu8y4J|newsgroup=rec.pets.cats.health+behav|passage=I'm a medic and phenobarb is the primary drug for true seizures, but the OP states the cat presents seizure like behavior at the sound of her voice. I don't know where any of you are from, but we don't treat seizures with '''val'''.}}

