===Etymology===
{{root|de|ine-pro|*h₂er-}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|arm}}, from {{inh|de|goh|arm}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*arm}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*armaz}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro|*h₂ermos}}, {{m|ine-pro||*h₂ŕ̥mos}}, an extension of {{m|ine-pro|*h₂er-||to fit together, to link, to join}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|arm}}, {{cog|en|arm}}, {{cog|sv|arm}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|la|armus}} and {{m|la|arma}}.

