Page 2065 Bindestrichland: -------- begin text --------
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|de|Bindestrich-Land}}

===Etymology===
From {{com|de|Bindestrich|t1=hyphen|Land|t2=state}}. Originally used of [[North Rhine-Westphalia]], which was created by the Allied occupation authorities by dividing the [[Prussian]] {{w|Rhine Province}} and joining its northern half to the province of [[Westphalia]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|de|De-Bindestrichland.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n,s:es,^er}}

# a [[state]] or political [[territory]] whose name contains a [[hyphen]], with the implication that it has been arbitrarily created from merging two [[region]]s that share few historical and cultural ties

====Usage notes====
* Used especially of the German state of {{m|en|North Rhine-Westphalia}} and to a lesser degree of {{m|en|Baden-Württemberg}}, {{m|en|Mecklenburg-Vorpommern}}, and {{m|en|Sachsen-Anhalt}}.

====Declension====
{{de-ndecl|n,s:es,^er}}

