Page 2107 Wall: -------- begin text --------
{{also|wall|wall-}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
Of various origins, principally from {{inh|en|ang|wælisc}} etc. ("[[non-]][[Germanic]] [[speaker]], [[stranger]]") from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*walhaz||foreigner, stranger}}, the source of numerous other surnames such as {{m|en|Walsh}} and {{m|en|Wales}} and from {{inh|en|enm|wall}}, from {{inh|en|ang|weall||wall, dike, rampart}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wallaz}} or {{m|gem-pro|*wallą||wall, rampart}}, from {{der|en|la|vallum||wall, rampart, palisade}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wel-||to turn, wind, roll}}. Also from transcribed foreign surnames such as German {{m|en|Wahl}} and Swedish {{m|en|Wahlberg}}.

====Proper noun====
{{swp|Wall (surname)}}
{{swp|Wall (disambiguation)#Places|Wall (places)}}
{{en-proper noun|~}}

# {{surname|en}}.
# A [[placename]]
## {{place|en|village|par/Gwinear-Gwithian|south-west|co/Cornwall|cc/England|c/UK}} {{q|[[OS]] grid ref SW6036}}. <ref>[https://getoutside.ordnancesurvey.co.uk/local/wall-cornwall OS: Cornwall]</ref>
## {{place|en|village/and/civil parish|in south|co/Northumberland|cc/England|c/UK}} {{q|OS grid ref NY9169}}; part of {{l|en|Hadrian's Wall}} is in the parish.
## {{place|en|village/and/civil parish|in the City of|dist/Lichfield|co/Staffordshire|cc/England|c/UK}} {{q|OS grid ref SK0906}}.
## {{place|en|borough|in|co/Allegheny County|s/Pennsylvania|c/USA}}.
## {{place|en|town|co/Pennington County|s/South Dakota|c/USA}}.
## {{place|en|unincorporated community|co/Tom Green County|s/Texas|c/USA}}.

===Etymology 2===
See {{m|en|wall}}.

====Proper noun====
{{en-proper noun|head=the Wall}}

# {{lb|en|history|slang}} the [[Berlin Wall]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} the [[:wikipedia:Trump Wall|Trump Wall]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} the [[Great Wall of China]].

===Etymology 3===
{{wikipedia|Encampment (Chinese constellation)}}
{{calque|en|cmn|壁宿|tr=Bìxiù}}.

====Proper noun====
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|astronomy}} A [[Chinese]] [[constellation]] [[located]] near [[Pegasus]] and [[Andromeda]], [[one]] of the 28 [[lunar]] [[mansion]]s and [[part]] of the [[larger]] [[Black Turtle]].

===Statistics===
* According to the 2010 United States Census, ''Wall'' is the 631<sup>st</sup> most common surname in the United States, belonging to 53,794 individuals. ''Wall'' is most common among White (86.10%) individuals.

