Page 2133 βουνό: -------- begin text --------
==Greek==

===Etymology===
Inherited from the mediaeval {{inh|el|gkm|βουνό|βουνό, βουνόν}}, a {{glossary|metaplasm}} to neuter of the {{inh|el|grc|βουνός|pos=masculine|t=hill}} of uncertain etymology, probably in accordance to the masculine {{m|grc|ὄρος|t=mountain}}.<ref>{{R:DSMG}}</ref> A connection to {{m|grc|βουβών}} is very unlikely.<ref>{{R:Babiniotis 2010}}</ref>

Compare {{cog|grk-mar|вуно́}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|el|/vuˈno/}}
* {{hyphenation|el|βου|νό}}

===Noun===
{{el-noun|n|βουνά}}

# [[mountain]]
#: {{ux|el|Το όρος Έβερεστ είναι το ψηλότερο '''βουνό''' της οροσειράς των Ιμαλαΐων.|Mount Everest is the highest '''mountain''' in the Himalayan massif.}}
# [[mountainous]] [[countryside]]
# {{lb|el|figuratively}} [[heavy]] [[workload]], [[mountain]] of [[work]]

====Usage notes====
* {{m-self|el|βουνό}} is more typically used as a general term for a mountain, than in its name when its synonym {{m|el|όρος}} might be used.

====Declension====
{{el-nN-ο-α-1|βουν}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|el|όρος|g=n}}

