==Greek==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|el|grc|Μᾰκεδονῐ́ᾱ}}.

===Proper noun===
{{el-noun-proper|f}}

# {{place|el|an <<ancient>> [[Greek]] <<kingdom>> in the north of the [[Greek]] peninsula, in the contemporary [[Balkan]]s|t=Macedon|t2=Macedonia}}
# {{place|el|t=Macedonia|adr|c/Greece}}
# {{place|el|t=Macedonia|a broader <<region>> of the <<pen:suf/Balkan>>, consisting of the administrative region of [[Macedonia]] in <<c/Greece>>, the country of <<c/North Macedonia>> and a bit of <<c/Bulgaria>>}}
# {{lb|el|rare|outside|longer phrases}} {{place|el|t=North Macedonia|the country to the north of Greece: [[Βόρεια Μακεδονία]] ([[North Macedonia]]) formerly known as the [[Socialist Republic of Macedonia]] of [[Yugoslavia]]}} {{qualifier|see Usage notes}}
#* '''1979''', Giannēs Iōannidēs, Alekos Papapanagiōtou, "Αναμνήσεις" (''Anamnēseis: provlēmata tēs politikēs tou KKE stēn ethnikē antistasē, 1940-1945'') (Mémoires: problems of the Greek Communist Party policy during national Resistance 1940-1945), [https://books.google.gr/books?id=S35-AAAAIAAJ&q=%CE%93%CE%B5%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CE%BF%E1%BF%A6+%CE%A3%CF%84%CF%81%CE%B1%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%B3%CE%B5%CE%AF%CE%BF%CF%85+%CF%84%CE%BF%E1%BF%A6+%CE%9B%CE%91%CE%A3%CE%93&dq=%CE%93%CE%B5%CE%BD%CE%B9%CE%BA%CE%BF%E1%BF%A6+%CE%A3%CF%84%CF%81%CE%B1%CF%84%CE%B7%CE%B3%CE%B5%CE%AF%CE%BF%CF%85+%CF%84%CE%BF%E1%BF%A6+%CE%9B%CE%91%CE%A3%CE%93&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwj6kPXEmN3nAhUkSRUIHf30DIEQ6AEILjAA page 519 @books.google]. ([[polytonic#English|polytonic]] script):
#*: {{quote|el|{{...}} ἔφυγε ἀπό την ἕδρα τοῦ Γενικοῦ Στρατηγείου τοῦ ΛΑΣΓ στά τέλη τοῦ Όκτώβρη 1942 καί ἔφτασε στή '''Μακεδονία''' (Σκόπια) κατά τό Μάρτη τοῦ 1943.
|translation={{...}} (he) left from the headquarters of LASG [People's Liberating Army of Yugoslavia] in the end of October 1942 and arrived at '''Macedonia''' (Skopje) approximately in March of 1943.}}
#* {{seeCites|el}}

====Usage notes====
* For the country "Republic of Macedonia" see [[w:Macedonia naming dispute|"Macedonia naming dispute" ''on Wikipedia'']].) Expressions for the country in the 20th century included: {{m|el|[[ομόσπονδος|Ομόσπονδη]] [[δημοκρατία|Δημοκρατία]] [[της]] Μακεδονίας|t=Federal Republic of Macedonia}}, {{m|el|[[λαϊκός|Λαϊκή]] Δημοκρατία της Μακεδονίας|t=People's Republic of Macedonia}}, {{m|el|[[σοσιαλιστικός|Σοσιαλιστική]] Δημοκρατία της Μακεδονίας|t=Socialist Republic of Macedonia}}, post-Yugoslav bare {{m|el|Δημοκρατία της Μακεδονίας|t=Republic of Macedonia}}, and {{m|el|πρώην Γιουγκοσλαβική Δημοκρατία της Μακεδονίας|t=[[FYROM]] (Former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia)}}.

