Page 2177 χώρα: -------- begin text --------
==Ancient Greek==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|grc|χώρη||ion}}

===Etymology===
{{unk|grc}}; possibly loaned from a {{bor|grc|qsb-grc}} substrate or other regional language. Has been tentatively and inconclusively compared with {{m|grc|χᾰ́ος||empty space, abyss, chasm}} as well as {{m|grc|χατέω||to lack, miss, need, desire}}; Beekes dismisses these connections as unfounded. No apparent cognates outside of Greek.

Beekes however compares {{m|grc|χήρα||widow}}, assuming common derivation from the {{nc|ine-pro|-}} root {{m|ine-pro|*ǵʰeh₁-||to leave behind}}, which would not make it related to {{m|grc|χατέω}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{grc-IPA|χώρᾱ}}

===Noun===
{{grc-noun|χώρᾱ|χώρᾱς|f|first}}

# [[location]], [[place]], [[spot]] (see Latin [[locus]])
# the proper place
# one's place in life
# piece of land: [[tract]], [[land]], [[field]]
# [[country]] (opposite town), [[countryside]]
# [[country]], [[nation]]

