Page 2334 arid: -------- begin text --------
{{also|àrid|árið}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂eHs-}}
From {{der|en|fr|aride}} or directly from {{der|en|la|āridus||dry, arid, parched}},<ref>{{R:Lexico}}</ref> compare its synonymous contracted form {{m|la|ardus}}. Originally from the verb {{m|la|āreo||I am dry, I am parched}}, akin to {{m|la|ārdeō||I am on fire, I burn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈæɹ.ɪd/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈæɹ.ɪd/}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-ne-arid.ogg|Audio (US)}} {{a|non-Mary-marry-merry}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɛɚ.ɪd/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-arid.ogg|Audio (US)}} {{a|Mary-marry-merry}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# Very [[dry]].
#: {{ant|en|wet|drenched|damp|moist}}
#: {{ux|en|The cake was '''arid'''.}}
# Describing a very dry [[climate]]. Typically defined as less than 25 cm or 10 inches of rainfall annually.
#: {{syn|en|xeric}}
#: {{ant|en|rainforest|humid}}
#: {{hypo|en|semi-arid|semiarid}}
#: {{ux|en|Deserts are known for being '''arid'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2012|author=Chinle Miller|title=In Mesozoic Lands: The Mesozoic Geology of Arches and Canyonlands National Parks|chapter=|url=|page=|text=And because this part of Utah is '''arid''', the geologic landscape is fully revealed with very little vegetation to hide it, faults and all.|edition=Kindle}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} [[devoid|Devoid]] of [[value]].
#: {{ant|en|valuable|costly|precious}}
#: {{ux|en|The millionaire viewed his gift as '''arid'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1956|author=w:Arthur C. Clarke|title=The City and the Stars|page=37|passage=Such occupations might have seemed '''arid''' to those who did not possess the intellect to appreciate their subtleties.}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|aridity}}

