===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|gd|sga|crúach|t=stack of corn; rick; heap, conical pile; mountain, hill}}, from {{inh|gd|cel-pro|*krowko-|t=heap}}, probably from {{der|gd|ine-pro|*krā(u)-|t=to heap up}}, shared with {{cog|gem-pro|*hraukaz|t=heap}}, {{cog|lt|krûvà|t=heap}}.<ref>{{R:cel:EDPC|head=krowko|pages=226-27}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:IEW|1513}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{gd-noun|g=f|gen=cruaiche|pl=cruachan}}

# [[pile]], [[heap]], [[stack]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|gd|cho seasgair ri luchag ann an cruach|t=snug as a bug in a rug|lit=snug as a mouse in a haystack}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|gd|sga|crúachaid|t=heaps, piles}}, from {{m|sga|crúach|t=heap, pile}}.

====Verb====
{{gd-verb|past=chruach|fut=cruachaidh|vn=cruachadh|pp=cruachte}}

# [[pile]] or [[heap]] up
# make into a [[stack]]

===Mutation===
{{gd-mut-cons|c|ruach}}

===References===
<references/>
-------- end text --------
