Probably from {{der|it|gem-pro|*ansijō|t=loop, handle}} mixed with ''*asa'', inherited from {{der|it|la|ānsa|t=handle}}, perhaps also formally influenced by the Latin in the literary language. Cf. {{cog|de|Öse||eyelet}}, {{cog|rm|ansa|ansa, onsa|eyelet}}; contrast the inherited {{cog|sc|asa|t=handle}}, {{cog|lmo|asa||handle}} and {{m|lmo|aseta||loop}}, Verona {{cog|vec|asa|t=soffit}}, Abruzzo {{cog|nap|asa|t=door hinge}}, Calabria {{cog|scn|asa|t=handle}}, {{cog|pt|asa|t=wing; handle}}, {{cog|gl|asa|t=handle}}, {{cog|es|asa|t=handle}}.

====Noun====
{{it-noun|f}}

# [[handle]]
#: {{syn|it|manico|maniglia|presa}}
# {{lb|it|rare}} [[excuse]], [[pretext]]
#: {{syn|it|appiglio|pretesto|scusa}}
# {{lb|it|geography}} [[curve]] or [[bend]] (in a river)
#: {{syn|it|curva|meandro}}
# {{lb|it|geography}} a small [[bight]], [[bay]], [[cove]]
#: {{syn|it|insenatura}}
# [[loop]], [[coil]]
# {{n-g|as name of various chirurgical or laboratory instruments}}

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{head|it|verb form}}

# {{inflection of|it|ansare||3|s|pres|indc|;|2|s|impr}}

