#* {{quote-text|gl|year=1370|editor=R. Lorenzo|title=Crónica troiana.|page=378|publisher=Fundación Barrié|location=A Coruña
|passage=''Et os hũus tãgíã '''cornos''' et os outros pipas, et os que estauã perlos muros da vila, algũus deles deostauã et dezíã moyto mal aos de fora.''
|translation=And some were playing '''horns''' and others pipes, and of the ones that were by the walls of the town, some insulted and told many mean things to the ones outside}}
#* {{quote-text|gl|year=1813|author=Manuel Pardo de Andrade|title=Rogos de un escolar gallego
|passage=''Sobre un tapiz dua mesa''<br>''mais louro do que é o carbon''<br>''hay procesos, e un tinteiro''<br>''feito de '''corno''' de boy.''
|translation=Over the cloth of a table,<br>blacker than coal,<br>there are lawsuits and an inkwell<br>made with ox '''horn'''}}
# [[horn]] {{gloss|[[wind]] [[instrument]]}}
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=1390|editor=J. L. Pensado Tomé|title=Os Miragres de Santiago. Versión gallega del Códice latino del siglo XII atribuido al papa Calisto I|location=Madrid|publisher=C.S.I.C.|page=136
|passage=''Et moy rregeo tãgeo o '''corno''' que pero que era de marfil que o fendeu cõ o bafo, et al quebrantouselle as veas do pescoço et os nerueos''
|translation=And very strongly he blew the '''horn''', but since it was made of ivory he broke it with the puff, and also he broke the veins of the neck and the nerves}}
# [[cuckoopint]] {{gloss|{{taxlink|Arum italicum|species}}}}
# {{vern|European rhinoceros beetle}} {{gloss|{{taxlink|Oryctes nasicornis|species}}}}

