====Pronunciation====
{{ko-IPA|l=y}}

====Noun====
{{ko-noun|hanja=故障}}

# [[breakdown]] {{gl|mechanical}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[우리]][[-는]] [[길가]] [[쪽]][[-에]] 고장[[나다|난]] [[차]][[-가]] [[있다|있는]] [[것]][[-을]] [[목격하다|목격하였다]].|We saw a breakdown by the side of the road.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{ko-l|고장이 나다||to break down}}

===Etymology 2===
This term is not attested in pre-twentieth century documents.

The Pyongan dialect form {{m|ko|고당}} implies original {{lang|ko|*고댱}}, given the regular eighteenth- and nineteenth-century sound shift of {{IPAfont|/tj/ > /t/}} in Pyongan and {{IPAfont|/tj/ > /t͡ɕ/}} elsewhere. Hence perhaps a {{ko-etym-nativised|nocap=y|고장|[[古]][[場]]|old place; hometown|nodot=y}}, whose original Sino-Korean reading was indeed {{lang|ko|고댱}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ko-IPA}}

====Noun====
{{ko-noun}}

# a populated district; a [[town]]
# a [[center]] of production for a particular commodity

===References===
* {{cite-book|chapter={{lang|ko|고장}}|title={{lang|ko|{{ruby|[國](국)[語](어)[語](어)[源](원)[辭](사)[典](전)}}}}|pages=63-64|author=Seo Jeong-beom {{lang|ko|(서정범)}}|publisher=Bogosa Books|location=Seoul|year=2000}}

{{c|ko|Geography}}
