==Korean==

===Etymology===
[[File:Chgjgns02.jpg|thumb|{{ko-usex|[[갈아타다|갈아타는]] 곳|'''place''' to transfer}}]]
[[File:AREX-DMC Stn-gate.jpg|thumb|{{ko-usex|[[나가다|나가는]] 곳|'''place''' to exit}}]]
{{ko-etym-native|yb|곧|kwot}} Perhaps from the same root as {{ko-l|골|village}}, as well as {{ko-l|거리|street}}. Possibly cognate with the {{cog|mnc|ᡤᡠᡵᡠᠨ||country}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{ko-ipa}}

===Noun===
{{ko-noun}}

# [[place]]
#: {{syn|ko|장소(場所)}}

====Usage notes====
* In South Korea, there is an ongoing government-pushed movement to phase out established Sino-Korean words like {{ko-l|출구|出口|exit}} or {{ko-l|환승|換乘|transfer}} in public signage with collocations using {{m-self|ko|곳}} such as {{m|ko|[[나가다|나가는]] 곳|lit=leaving place}} or {{m|ko|[[갈아타다|갈아타는]] 곳|lit=vehicle-switching place}}, motivated by a nationalist ideology of {{w|linguistic purism}}. However, this has not caught on very much.

====Derived terms====
{{col2|ko
|곳곳
|곳곳이
}}

===References===
* {{cite-web|url=http://krdic.naver.com/detail.nhn?docid=3164200|work={{lang|ko|표준국어대사전}}|author=National Institute of the Korean Language (Naver.com mirror)|title={{lang|ko|곳}}|accessdate=2007-01-04}}
* {{cite-book|title={{lang|ko|새국어사전}}|year=2005|publisher=Isangsa|location=Seoul|author=Choe, Jong-du {{lang|ko|(최종두)}}, ed.|chapter={{lang|ko|곳}}|page=62}}
* {{cite-book|title={{lang|ko|한국어 발음사전}}|trans-title=Korean Pronouncing Dictionary|last=Lee|first=Ju Haeng {{lang|ko|(이주행)}}|coauthors=Lee Kyu Hang {{lang|ko|(이규항)}}, Kim Sang Jun {{lang|ko|(김상준)}}|year=2004|isbn=89-7006-165-7|publisher=Jigu Publishing|location=Seoul|chapter={{lang|ko|곳}}|page=85}}
* {{cite-book|chapter={{lang|ko|곳}}|title={{lang|ko|{{ruby|[國](국)[語](어)[語](어)[源](원)[辭](사)[典](전)}}}}|page=71|author=Seo Jeong-beom {{lang|ko|(서정범)}}|publisher=Bogosa Books|location=Seoul|year=2000}}

