==Middle Korean==

===Etymology===
Probably imitative. Compare {{cog|en|oi}}, {{cog|ja|-}} {{ja-r|おい}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|okm|/ǔj/}}

===Interjection===
{{head|okm|interjection|{{w|Idu script}}|爲|or|偉|tr=wǔy}}

# {{n-g|An interjection which appears in certain poems.}}
#* {{quote-book|ko|author=ko:안축/安軸<t:An Chuk>|title=ko:關東別曲/관동별곡<tr:Gwandong byeolgok>|trans-title=Song of the Lands East of the Pass|year=1330|text={{ruby|'''[爲](위〯)''' [四](ᄉᆞ〯)[海](ᄒᆡ〯) [天](텬)[下](하〯) [無](업〯)[豆](두〮)[舍叱](샷)[多](다〮)}}|tr='''WǓY''' SǑ.HǑY THYÈN.HǍ ĚP.TWÚ.SYÀS.TÁ|t='''O''', it does not exist [anywhere else] between the four seas under Heaven!}}
#* {{quote-book|okm|origyear=14th century?|chapter=ko:[思母曲/사모곡]<tr:Jeongseok-ga>|title=ko:樂章歌詞/악장가사<tr:Akjang gasa>|text=아바님도 어이어신 마ᄅᆞᄂᆞᆫ<br>'''위''' 덩더둥셩<br>어마님 ᄀᆞ티 괴시리 업세라|t=My father is my parent, too<br>'''''wuy''' tengtetwungsyeng''<br>But there is none to love me like my mother does.|tr=apa-nim-two ei-Gesin malonon<br>'''wuy''' tengtetwungsyeng<br>ema-nim kothi kwoysil_i epseyla|year=16th century}}
