Page 2752 Augusta: -------- begin text --------
{{also|augusta|augustā|Augustą}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|Augusta}}, feminine of {{m|la|Augustus}}. The places are mostly named for British royalty.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əɡʌstə/}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{given name|en|female|from=Latin}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|author=w:Margaret Atwood|title=Robber Bride|page=48|publisher=Virago Press|year_published=2013|isbn=9781853817229
|passage=''August'', Charis named her, because that's when she was born. Warm breezes, baby powder, languorous heat, the smell of mown hay. Such a soft name. Too soft for her daughter, who has added an ''a''. '''Augusta''', she is now — a very different resonance. Marble statues, Roman noses, tight-lipped commanding mouths.}}
# {{place|en|number of places|c/USA}}:
## {{place|en|city/county seat|co/Woodruff County|s/Arkansas}}.
## {{place|en|city/county seat|co/Richmond County|in east-central|s/Georgia}}; also see [[Disgusta]].
## {{place|en|village|s/Illinois}}.
## {{place|en|city|s/Kansas}}.
## {{place|en|city|s/Kentucky}}.
## {{place|en|The <<capital city>> of <<s/Maine>>, <<c/USA>> and the <<county seat>> of <<co/Kennebec County>>}}.
## {{place|en|village|s/Michigan}}.
## {{place|en|unincorporated community|co/Carver County|s/Minnesota}}.
## {{place|en|city|s/Missouri}}.
## {{place|en|census-designated place|s/Montana}}.
## {{place|en|unincorporated community|co/Sussex County|s/New Jersey}}.
## {{place|en|town|s/New York}}.
## {{place|en|unincorporated community|co/Hampshire County|s/West Virginia}}.
## {{place|en|city|s/Wisconsin}}.
## {{place|en|A number of <<townships>> in the <<c/USA>>, listed under {{w|Augusta Township}}}}.
# {{place|en|township|in the|co/United Counties of Leeds and Grenville|eastern|p/Ontario|c/Canada}}.
# {{place|en|town|r/Sicily|c/Italy}}.
