Page 2753 Babylon: -------- begin text --------
{{also|babylon|Babylón}}
==English==
{{wp}}
{{swp|Babylon (disambiguation)}}

===Etymology===
Partially inherited from {{der|en|ang|Babilon}}/{{m|ang|Babȳlōn}}, partially from {{der|en|la|Babylōn}}, from {{der|en|grc|Βαβυλών}}, from {{der|en|akk|Bābilim|𒆍𒀭𒊏𒆠|tr=Bābilim|lit=Gate of God}}; the name of the ancient Chaldean capital and Biblical city of the Apocalypse. {{doublet|en|Babel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbæb.ɪ.lɒn/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Babylon.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbæb.ɪ.lɑn/}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{sid|en|Q5684}}{{lb|en|historical}} {{place|en|ancient city|r/Mesopotamia|built on the banks of the [[Euphrates]], which was the capital of [[Babylonia]]}}.
# Any city of great wealth, luxury and vice.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=w:Ben Travers|title=w:A Cuckoo in the Nest
|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1521052W
|passage=Mother{{...}}considered that the exclusiveness of Peter's circle was due not to its distinction, but to the fact that it was an inner '''Babylon''' of prodigality and whoredom, from which every Kensingtonian held aloof, except on the conventional tip-and-run excursions in pursuit of shopping, tea and theatres.}}
# {{lb|en|rasta}} [[Western]] [[civilization]], seen as [[corrupt]] and [[materialistic]], and contrasted with [[Zion]].
# {{lb|en|Jamaica|MLE}} The [[police]].
#* {{quote-journal|en
|date=2017-09-24
|author={{w|Emma Jones (journalist)|Emma Jones}}
|title=Crime, sexism and a near death experience - former police officer lifts the lid on the hidden secrets of the force
|journal=w:Daily Mirror
|url=http://www.mirror.co.uk/news/real-life-stories/crime-sexism-near-death-experience-11202239
|passage=When I was the first officer on the scene at a nightclub brawl, I was picked up by the throat and strangled by a huge Rastafarian who was trying to kill me. I was losing consciousness when Marlon told him to let me go.<br>I remember him saying, ‘She’s alright for '''Babylon'''. Put her down.’ He dropped me and I ran to the station with massive bruises around my neck.
}}
# {{place|en|unincorporated community|co/Fulton County|s/Illinois|c/USA}}.
# {{place|en|town/and/village|therein, in|co/Suffolk County|isl/Long Island|s/New York|c/USA}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|police}} {{seeSynonyms|en|police|sense=1}}

