Page 2756 Boihaemum: -------- begin text --------
==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|Boiohaemum|Boihemum|Boiemum|Boehemum|Boiohemum}}

===Etymology===
Directly or via {{bor|la|grc|Βουίαιμον}}, rendering {{bor|la|gem-pro|*baiaz||one of the [[w:Boii|Boii]]}} + {{m|gem-pro|*haimaz||home}}, designating the area abandoned by the [[Boii]] c. 60 BCE and settled by the Germanic [[w:Marcomanni|Marcomanni]] shortly thereafter, now {{cog|de|Böhmen}}.<ref>Dietz, Karlheinz (Würzburg). “Boiohaemum.” ''Brill’s New Pauly'', 2012. Reference. 14 March 2012 [http://referenceworks.brillonline.com/entries/brill-s-new-pauly/boiohaemum-e218860]</ref> The tribal name, {{cog|la|Boiī|Bo(i)ī}}, is probably {{der|la|cel-gau||*bouios|cattle owner}}, a relative adjective from {{der|la|cel-pro|*bāus||ox, cow}}, which continues {{der|la|ine-pro|*gʷṓws||cattle}}, or less likely {{m|ine-pro|*bʰeyh₂-||to strike, hit}}. Related to {{m|la|Bavaria}}.

First attested in [[w:Velleius Paterculus|Velleius]] (19 BC – c. AD 31).

===Pronunciation===
* Uncertain:
** {{la-IPA|Boihaemum|eccl=0}}
** {{la-IPA|Boiaemum|eccl=0}}
* {{la-IPA|Boiaemum|cl=0}}

===Proper noun===
{{la-proper noun|Boihaemum<2>}}

# roughly the present {{place|la|region|c/Czech Republic|t1=Bohemia}}

====Declension====
{{la-ndecl|Boihaemum<2>}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|la|Bohēmī|Bo(h)ēmī}}, {{l|la|Boihaemī}}
* {{l|la|Bohēmia|Bo(h)ēmia}}, {{l|la|Boihaemia}}

