Page 2798 frons: -------- begin text --------
{{also|fröns}}
==English==
[[File:Grasshopper-head.jpg|thumb|Grasshopper-head: '''a''': antenna; '''b''': ocelli; '''c''': vertex; '''d''': compound eye; '''e''': occiput; '''f''': gena; '''g''': pleurostoma; '''h''': mandible; '''i''': labial palp; '''j''': maxillary palps; '''k''': maxilla; '''l''': labrum; '''m''': clypeus; '''n''': '''frons''']]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|frōns||the forehead, brow, front}}. {{doublet|en|front}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/fɹɒnz/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/fɹɑnz/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒnz|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|frontes}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} In [[vertebrate]]s, especially [[mammal]]s, the [[forehead]]; the part of the [[cranium]] between the [[orbit]]s and the [[vertex]].
# {{lb|en|entomology}} The front part of the [[epicranium]] or head [[capsule]] of many [[insect]]s; generally speaking, the area below or between the [[antenna]]e and above the [[clypeus]]. Typically it lies between the [[genal]] or "cheek" areas on either side of the head.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1981|author=J. F. McAlpine|title=Manual of Nearctic Diptera|page=14|volume=1|isbn=0-660-10731-7|passage=In a generalized insect the '''frons''' extends from the vertex to the frontoclypeal (epistomal) suture, between the two anterior tentorial pits.}}
# {{lb|en|entomology}} {{q|of [[Diptera]]}} The [[postfrons]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1985|author=D. M. Wood|title=A taxonomic conspectus of the Blondeliini of North and Central America and the West Indies (Diptera: Tachinidae)|journal=Memoirs of the Entomological Society of Canada|doi=10.4039/entm117132fv|volume=117|page=9|passage=In most blondeliines (and in most Tachinidae in general), males have a narrower '''frons''' than conspecific females {{...}}}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|forehead}}

===References===
* {{R:Lexico}}
* {{R:MWO}}

==Dutch==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|nl|frm|fronce}}, from {{der|nl|fro|fronce}}, from {{der|nl|frk|*hrunkja||wrinkle}} from {{der|nl|gem-pro|*hrunkijō}}, {{m|gem-pro|*hrunkitō||fold, wrinkle}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*sker-||to turn, bend}}. The semantic narrowing to frowns on the forehead may be influenced by unrelated {{noncog|la|frōns}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/frɔns/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-frons.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|frons}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɔns}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|f|-en|fronsje}}

# A [[frown]], a [[furrow]] of one's [[eyebrow]]s or [[forehead]].
#:{{ux|nl|inline=1|Ze keek met een diepe '''frons''' naar het document.|She looked at the document with a deep '''frown'''.}}
#:{{ux|nl|inline=1|Zijn '''frons''' gaf zijn verwarring aan.|His '''frown''' indicated his confusion.}}
#:{{ux|nl|inline=1|Ik zag een kleine '''fronsje''' op haar voorhoofd.|I saw a tiny '''furrow''' on her forehead.}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|nl|fronsen}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|af|frons}}

==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
[[File:Forhead 01 ies.jpg|thumb|'''Frōns''' (forehead) virī.]]
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*fronts}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*bʰrónts}} (compare {{cog|ga|braine||prow, edge}}, {{cog|non|brandr||sword blade}}), from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰren-||to project; edge}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|frōns}}

====Noun====
{{la-noun|frōns<3.I>|g=f}}

# {{lb|la|literally}}:
## {{lb|la|anatomy}} the [[forehead]], [[brow]], [[front]]
##: {{syn|la|ōs|vultus}}
## the [[brow]] or [[countenance]] as an [[indicator]] of the [[feeling]]s
##: {{syn|la|vultus|faciēs}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}}:
## as the mirror of a [[person]]'s [[character]] or [[feeling]]s
## {{lb|la|in particular}} as expressing [[shame]]
##: {{ux|la|'''frontem''' perfricāre|to assume a bold air|lit=to wipe the blush of one's '''brow'''}}
### {{lb|la|transferred sense}} a [[sense]] of [[modesty]]; [[decorum]], [[decency]]
###* {{Q|la|Persius|5|104|quote=exclāmet Melicerta perīsse '''frontem''' dē rēbus}}
## {{lb|la|Late Latin}} as expressing [[impudence]], [[boldness]]
##: {{syn|la|ōs}}
# {{lb|la|transferred sense}}:
## the [[outward]] [[appearance]], [[external]] [[quality]], [[look]] {{gl|as distinct from inward nature}}
##: {{syn|la|faciēs|speciēs|forma|habitus}}
##: {{uxi|la|prīmā fronte|at first sight}}
## the [[forepart]] of anything; the [[front]], [[facade]] {{gl|as opposed to back and sides}}
##: {{ant|la|tergum|latus}}
##: {{uxi|la|ā fronte, in fronte, in prīmā fronte, in frontem|in front, to the fore}}
## {{lb|la|military}} the front of an [[army]] or [[fleet]] in battle [[array]]
## {{lb|la|surveying|geography}} [[frontage]] {{gl|the part facing the [[road]], [[river]], [[coastline]]}}, usually in ref. to its [[length]]
### the [[coastline]]; a [[projecting]] piece of [[coast]]
## the outer [[extremity]] or [[face]], the outer or inner [[surface]] {{gl|eg. of a wall}}, the top or bottom [[end]] {{gl|of a trench}}, the [[broad]] side {{gl|of a rectangle}}
### either of the flat [[end]]s of a [[papyrus]] [[scroll]]
## the [[exposed]] surface, outer side of anything

