Page 2870 supernus: -------- begin text --------
==Latin==

===Etymology===
Most likely a {{back-formation|la|supernē|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|supernus}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj|supernus|adv=superne}}

# [[upper]], that is located [[above]]
#* {{Q|la|Pliny the Elder|Naturalis Historia|9|12|37|quote=Dentēs nōn sunt testūdinī, set rōstrī marginēs acūtī '''supernā''' parte, interiōrem claudente pyxidum modō tantā ōris dūritiā ut lapidēs comminuant.|trans=The turtle has no teeth, but the edges of the beak are sharp on the side '''above''', which closes the lower jaw in the manner of boxes with such hardness that they can crush stones.}}
# [[celestial]], [[supernal]], [[lofty]]
# {{lb|la|geography|figuratively|rare}} [[northern]]
#* '''5th C. {{CE|nodots=yes}}''', [[w:Priscian|Priscian]] (translator), ''Periegesis'' 29–33, original author: [[w:Dionysius Periegetes|Dionysius Periegetes]], in ''[[w:Poetae Latini Minores|Poetae Latini Minores]]'' (volume V), [[w:Emil Baehrens|Emil Baehrens]] (editor), ''[[w:Bibliotheca Teubneriana|Bibliotheca Teubneriana]]'', [[w:Leipzig|Leipzig]] 1879, [https://archive.org/stream/poetaelatinimin05baeh#page/276/mode/2up page 276]:
#*: {{quote|la|Fīnibus est Asiae latus artum lingua '''supernīs''',<br>Caspia quam mediam faciunt atque aequora pontī<br>Euxīnī: locus hic discrīmen dīcitur esse<br>Eurōpae atque Asiae disiungēns rūribus arva.
|translation=The '''northern''' limits of Asia Minor have a narrow flank, a tongue,<br>which the Caspian Sea and the waters of the Black Sea create<br>in the middle: this place is said to be the separation<br>of Europe and Asia, distinguising the country from the fields.}}

====Declension====
{{la-adecl|supernus}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|supernas}}
* {{l|la|supernē}}
* {{l|la|supernitās}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|la|super}}
* {{l|la|superāns}}
* {{l|la|superō}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|en|supernal}}
* {{desc|fr|supernel}}
* {{desc|it|superno}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|supernus<2>}}

