Page 2905 brasls: -------- begin text --------
==Latvian==
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=lv}}
[[File:BrodPřesEketėPodHrázíLaukžemiųTv01.jpg|thumb|250px|Brasls]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{qualifier|dialectal forms}} {{l|lv|brads}}, {{l|lv|brasts}}

===Etymology===
From the same source as the verb {{m|lv|brist}} ([[q.v.]]), with change of the final consonant and an extra element ''lo'', apparently originally an adjective meaning probably “shallow.” The {{cog|lt|-}} and {{cog|prg|-}} forms correspond to a variant {{m|lv|brasts}} found in [[Courland]] dialects and in some placenames ({{m|lv|Brastvalks}}) and family names ({{m|lv|Brastiņš}}); the Slavic forms correspond to a dialectal variant {{m|lv|brads}}, also found in placenames ({{m|lv|Bradas}}, {{m|lv|Bradaiži}}). Cognates include {{cog|lt|brastà}}, dialectal {{m|lt|brasvà}}, {{m|lv|brastvà}} “ford; miry path, swampy meadow,” {{cog|prg|*brast-}} “ford” (in placenames, e.g., {{m|prg|Balkombrastun}}), {{cog|sla-pro|*brodъ}} ({{cog|ru|-}}, {{cog|be|-}} {{m|ru|брод}}, {{cog|uk|брід}}, {{cog|bg|брод}}, {{cog|cs|brod}}, {{cog|pl|bród}}), <ref>{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{lv-IPA|bɾasls}}
{{audio|lv|lv-riga-brasls.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{lv-noun|m|1st}}

# [[ford]] {{gloss|[[shallow]] [[place]] in a [[river]] or [[stream]] where one can [[cross]] it}}
#: {{ux|lv|pāriet upi '''braslā'''|to cross the river at the '''ford'''|inline=1}}
