Page 2910 jūra: -------- begin text --------
{{also|jura|Jura|jurá|jūrā|jūrą}}

==Latvian==
{{was fwotd|lv|2013|December|8}}
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=lv}}
[[File:Fiesa, warm summer day, end of June 2012 02.jpg|250px|thumb|Jūra]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|lv|bat-pro|-}} {{m|ine-bsl-pro|[[*jáuˀrāˀ]] ~ [[*jū́ˀrāˀ]]}}, from {{inh|lv|ine-pro|[[*h₂wer-]], [[*ūr-]]}} with an added initial ''y'', from {{m|ine-pro|[[*aw-]], [[*awe-]]||to wet, to moisten, to flow}} with a suffix ''-r''. The initial ''*y'' may result from [[metathesis]] in {{m|lv|*awer-}} (> {{m|ine-pro|*h₂wer-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*eur-}}), or from the influence of some other [[Proto-Indo-European]] root like {{m|ine-pro|*(e)rey-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(e)rew-||to flow}} ([[metathesis|metathesized]] into {{m|ine-pro|*ewr-}}). The original meaning was thus “wet, swampy place” ([[cf]]. {{cog|lt|jáuris||swamp}} < {{cog|bat-pro|*jaur-}}), whence “lake” (still attested in old folk tales, and also in borrowings into {{cog|urj-fin}}: {{cog|liv|jõra}}, {{cog|et|järv}}, {{cog|fi|järvi}}, {{cog|smi}} {{m|und|jaura}}, {{m|und|jawre}}, {{m|se|jávri}}) and finally “sea.” Cognates include {{cog|lt|jū́ra}}, dialectal {{m|lt|jūrė}}, plural {{m|lt|jū́ros}}, {{m|lt|jū́rios}}, {{m|lt|jū́rės}} (cf. Latvian dialectal {{m|lv|jūre}}, {{m|lv|jūris}}, plural {{m|lv|jūres}}), {{cog|prg|iūrin}}, {{m|prg|*jūren}}, {{m|prg|*jūrʲai}}, {{cog|hy|ջուր||water}}, {{cog|sq|hurdë||deep place; pond; swamp}}; without the initial ''*y'', also {{cog|non|úr||drizzle}}, {{m|non|ȳra||to drizzle}}, {{cog|la|ūrīnō||to dive, to plunge into water}}, {{m|la|ūrīna||urine}}.<ref>{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{lv-IPA|jūːɾa|level}}
{{audio|lv|Lv-jūra.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{lv-noun|f|4th}}

# {{lb|lv|geography}} [[sea]] {{gloss|large body of salty water}}
#: {{ux|lv|Baltijas '''jūra'''|Baltic Sea|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|Melnā '''jūra'''|Black Sea|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''jūras''' krasts, ūdens, vējš|'''sea''' coast, water, wind|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|peldēt '''jūrā'''|to swim in the '''sea'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''jūras''' slimība|'''sea''' sickness|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|iziet '''jūrā'''|to go on '''sea''', to sail, to set off|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|virs, zem '''jūrās''' līmeņa|above, below '''sea''' level|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|astronomy}} [[sea]] {{gloss|dark areas on the [[surface]] of the [[Moon]] or other [[natural]] [[satellites]]}}
#: {{ux|lv|mēness '''jūra'''|moon '''mare'''|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|figuratively}} very large [[quantity]] or [[amount]] (of something)
#: {{ux|lv|ziedu '''jūra'''|'''sea''' of flowers|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|liesmu '''jūra'''|'''sea''' of flames|inline=1}}

====Declension====
{{lv-decl-noun|jūr|a|4th|extrawidth=-60}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|lv|jūras lauva}}
* {{l|lv|jūrnieks}}, {{l|lv|jūrniece}}

====See also====
* {{l|lv|ezers}}
* {{l|lv|okeāns}}

