===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|lv|de|Karte}}, like {{m|lv|kārts}} “playing cards” (the latter apparently having suffered the influence of {{m|lv|kārts}} “pole” on its form), first attested as {{m|lv|zemes}} {{m|lv|kārte}} (with a long ''ā'') in the 1850s, and later on (by the end of the 19th century) simply as {{m|lv|karte}} (with a short ''e'').<ref>{{R:lv:LEV|kārts<sup>b</sup>}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{audio|lv|lv-riga-karte.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{lv-noun|f|5th}}

# {{lb|lv|geography}} [[map]], [[chart]]
#: {{ux|lv|'''kartes''' mērogs|'''map''' scale|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|lasīt '''karti'''|to read a '''map'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|ģeogrāfiska '''karte'''|geographic '''map'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|topogrāfiska '''karte'''|topographic '''map'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|ģeoloģiska '''karte'''|geologic '''map'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|zvaigžņu '''karte'''|star '''chart'''|inline=1}}
# [[document]]; [[identification]]; [[card]]
#: {{ux|lv|bibliotēkas lasītāja '''karte'''|library reader '''card'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|slimnieka individuālā '''karte'''|individual patient '''card'''|inline=1}}
# [[sheet]] of [[paper]], [[card]], etc. with special [[information]]
#: {{ux|lv|tramvaja, trolejbusa '''karte'''|a (one-month) tram, trolley '''pass'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|ielūguma '''karte'''|invitation '''card'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|ēdienu '''karte''', ēdien'''karte'''|food '''menu'''|inline=1}}

====Declension====
