Page 2915 leja: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Leja|lejā|leją|Leją}}
==Latvian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{qualifier|dated, 19th-century form}} {{l|lv|leija}}

===Etymology===
From earlier (19th-century) {{m|lv|leija}}, from {{der|lv|bat-pro|*ley-ya-}}, from {{m|ine-bsl-pro|*ley-ā}}, from {{der|lv|ine-pro|*l̥-ey}}, from the [[w:Indo-European ablaut|zero grade]] of {{m|ine-pro|*el-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*Heh₃l-|t=to bend, to incline}} (whence also {{m|lv|elkonis|t=elbow}}, [[q.v.]]) with a suffix ''-ey''. The meaning probably evolved as follows: “bent inward” > “inwardly bent earth”, “valley” > “lower area.” Cognates include {{cog|got|𐌿𐌽𐌳𐌰𐍂𐌻𐌴𐌹𐌾𐌰|t=lower, smaller}}, {{cog|grc|λειμών|t=humid, grassy place, humid meadow}} (lower places are often humid).<ref>{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{audio|lv|lv-riga-leja.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{lv-noun|f|4th}}

# [[low]] [[area]], [[low]] [[place]], [[below]] {{gloss|[[place]] [[locate]]d [[below]], [[with respect to]] [[something]] [[else]]}}
#: {{ux|lv|pa '''leju''' mājai garām šaujas motociklets|a motorcycle ran by in the '''low area''' along the house|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|Lība palika stāvam un ostīja gaisu: kaut kur no '''lejas''' uzvēdīja svešāada smarša|Lība remained standing and sniffed the air: somewhere from '''below''' a strange smell was spreading|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|in [[genitive]], [[use]]d [[adjective|adjectivally]]}} [[lower]] [[side]], [[lower]] [[part]], [[bottom]] (of something)
#: {{ux|lv|'''lejas''' stāvs|the lower (i.e., first) floor|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|te bija '''lejas''' aula baznīca ar zaļo skārda jumtu|here was the '''lower''' village church with a green tin roof|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|tumšajā '''lejas''' gaitenī klusēdami izklīst skolēnu pulciņi|the small groups of studnets silently dispersed in the dark '''lower''' corridor|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|in [[locative]], [[use]]d [[adverbially]]}} [[down]], [[below]], at the [[bottom]], in a [[lower]] [[area]] (of some place)
#: {{ux|lv|'''lejā''' pagalmā spēlējās bērni|'''down''' in the yard the children were playing|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|izgāju pat uz balkona; dzīli '''lejā''' zem manis slīdēja automašīnas un trolejbusi|I went out on the balcony; deep down under me cars and trolleys slid by|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|un tad tepat '''lejā''' pie Varžupīte tie karkli|and then right here (they are), down by the Varžupīte (river), these willows|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|tieši zem nišas bija divi galdiņi; nišā varēja dzirdēt katru vārdu, ko tie tur '''lejā''' runāja|right under the niche there were two little tables; in the niche it was possible to hear every word which they said '''down''' there|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|geography}} [[valley]]
#: {{ux|lv|upes, strauta '''leja'''|river, creek '''valley'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|dziļa '''leja'''|deep '''valley'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|krūmiem aizaugusi leja|a '''valley''' overgrown with bushes|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''lejas''' nogāze|'''valley''' slope|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|starp diviem kalniem vēsā lejā / svēts, vientuļš klosteris glabājās|in a cool '''valley''' between two mountains / a holy, lonely monastery kept itself|inline=1}}
# [[depression]] in an [[area]] or [[terrain]]
#: {{ux|lv|miklajā ganību '''lejā''' nāca melnakšņu un kārklu krūmi|in the humid pasture '''depression''' there were (lit. came) alder and willow bushes|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|of rivers; usually with {{m|lv|uz}}, {{m|lv|no}}}} [[mouth]], [[estuary]]
#: {{ux|lv|no '''lejas''' brauc tvaikonis|from the '''river mouth''' came a steamboat|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|straume laivu nesa uz '''leju'''|the stream took the boat '''downstream''', to(ward) the '''estuary'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|jo tālāk ejam mēs uz leju, jo vairāk straume izšķir mūs|the further we go '''downstream''', the more the stream separated us|inline=1}}
# {{lb|lv|with {{m|lv|uz}}}} [[down]], [[downward]], [[toward]] the [[earth]] {{gloss|also [[metaphorical]]ly}}
