Page 2944 laukas: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Laukas}}
==Lithuanian==

===Etymology===
{{root|lt|ine-pro|*lewk-}}
Cognate with {{cog|lv|lauks}} and {{cog|prg|laukinikis|gloss=landowner}}, from {{cog|ine-pro|*lowkós||bright place, clearing}}; compare {{cog|gem-pro|*lauhaz||meadow, grove}} ({{cog|ang|lēah||clearing}}, English {{m|en|lea}}), {{cog|la|lūcus||sacred grove}} and {{cog|sa|लोक|tr=loká-||free space, world}}. Apparently from {{der|lt|ine-pro|*lewk-||bright}}; compare {{cog|prg|luckis}}, {{cog|sla-pro|*lučь|*lúčь|ray of light}} and {{cog|la|lūx||light}}.

A similar [[semantic]] progression can be observed in {{m|lt|aiškus||clear, bright}} > {{m|lt|aikštė||clearing, open space}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lt|/ˈlɒʊ.kɐs/}}

===Noun===
{{lt-noun|head=laũkas|m|laukaĩ|4}}

