Page 3019 puke: -------- begin text --------
{{also|pūkè|puķe|puķē|пуке}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|pyo͞ok}}, {{IPA|en|/pjuːk/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-puke.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːk|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably {{onomatopoeic|en|title=imitative}}; or, alternatively from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*pukaną||to spit, puff}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bew-||to blow, swell}}. If so, then cognate with {{cog|de|pfauchen}}, {{m|de|fauchen||to hiss, spit}}. Compare also {{cog|nl|spugen||to spit, spit up}}, {{cog|de|spucken||to spit, puke, throw up}}, {{cog|ang|spīwan||to vomit, spit}}. More at {{l|en|spew}}.

Attested as early as 1581, first mention is the derivative {{m|en|pukishness||the tendency to be sick frequently}}. In 1600, "to spit up, regurgitate", recorded in the ''Seven Ages of Man'' speech in Shakespeare's ''As You Like It''.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial|uncountable}} [[vomit]].
#* '''2007''', ''[[w:The Guardian|The Guardian]]'', [http://www.guardian.co.uk/science/blog/2007/aug/07/thelatestinthewaronterro The Guardian Science blog], "The latest in the war on terror: the '''puke''' saber"
#*: the '''puke''' saber [...] pulses light over rapidly changing wavelengths, apparently inducing "disorientation, nausea and even vomiting"
# {{lb|en|colloquial|countable}} A [[drug]] that [[induce]]s vomiting.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1776|author=Physician Lewis Beebe|url=https://wwnorton.com/college/history/archive/resources/documents/ch06_02.htm|title=Diary of a Revolutionary Army Physician
|passage="at 8 a.m. took a puke of vinum antimoniale; which operated very kindly; was very weak the remainder of the day."}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|countable}} A [[worthless]], [[despicable]] person.
# {{lb|en|US|slang|derogatory|countable}} A person from [[Missouri]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Clive Scott Chisholm|title=Following the Wrong God Home: Footloose in an American Dream|passage="'''Pukes'''" and "suckers" had badly mauled the Saints, the first pummeling them from Missouri and the second from Illinois.}}

=====Synonyms=====
* See [[Thesaurus:vomit]]
* (person) [[rotter]]

