===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|fr|VL.|*grava}} (attested in Mediaeval Latin), of pre-Latin origin, possibly {{der|fr|cel-gau|*grawa}}, from {{der|fr|cel-pro|*grāwā}}.

====Noun====
{{fr-noun|f}}

# [[bank]] {{q|of a river}}; [[shore]], [[strand]]
#: {{syn|fr|rive}}

===Etymology 2===
Named after {{w|Place de Grève}} on the banks of the Seine in Paris (now {{w|Place de l'Hôtel de Ville}}), where unemployed workers would gather. ''Place de Grève'' means “flat area covered with gravel or sand” (see Etymology 1 above).

====Noun====
{{fr-noun|f}}

# [[strike]] (cessation of work)
#: {{ux|fr|En raison de la '''grève''', il nous faudra prendre le train.|t=Because of the '''strike''', we will need to take the train. }}

