==Latin==
{{wikipedia|lang=la}}
[[Image:Glass of Milk (33657535532).jpg|thumb|[[poculum#Latin|Poculum]] lactis.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|lact|lacte}}

===Etymology===
Earlier {{m|la|lact}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*ǵlákt|g=n}} (gen. {{m|ine-pro|*ǵlaktós}}). Compare {{cog|sq|dhallë|t=buttermilk}}, {{cog|xcl|կաթն}}, {{cog|grc|γάλα|t=milk}}, {{cog|hit|𒂵𒆷𒀝𒋻|tr=galaktar|t=balm, resin}}, {{cog|wbk|zōr|t=milk}} and the irregular {{cog|ro|zară}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|lac}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|lac/lact<3.N.sg>}}

# [[milk]]
#: {{ux|la|Cum '''lacte''' nutricis.|inline=1|With the nurse's '''milk'''.}}
# for something [[sweet]], [[pleasant]]
#: {{ux|la|In melle sunt linguae sitae vostrae atque orationes, '''lacteque'''; corda felle sunt lita, atque acerbo aceto.|In honey your tongues and speeches are dipped, '''and in milk'''; your hearts are smeared with gall and with bitter vinegar. (Plautus)}}
#: {{ux|la|Ut mentes ... satiari velut quodam jucundioris disciplinae '''lacte''' patiantur.|That minds may endure being satisfied as by the '''milk''' of a more pleasant discipline. (Quintilian)}}
# [[milky]] [[juice]]
#: {{ux|la|'''Lac''' herbae.|inline=1|'''Milk''' of a plant.}}
#: {{ux|la|cum '''lacte''' veneni.|inline=1|with poisonous '''milk'''.}}
#*  '''c. 1st century BCE''', ''Anonymous'' (formerly misattributed to Ovid), ''Nux''
#*: {{quote|la|Lamina mollis adhuc tenero dum '''lacte''', quod intro est,<br>nec mala sunt ulli nostra futura bono.
|translation=As their nutshell still remains soft with something tenderly milky inside,<br>my future fruits are not good to anyone.}}
# {{lb|la|poetic}} [[milk-white]] color
#* {{Q|la|Publius Ovidius Naso|Ars Amatoria|I.290|year=2 CE|quote=Forte sub umbrosis nemorosae vallibus Idae<br>candidus, armenti gloria, taurus erat,<br>signatus tenui media inter cornua nigro;<br>una fuit labes, cetera '''lactis''' erant.|trans=As fortune had it, in the shadowy valleys of forested Ida,<br>there was a white bull, the glory of its herd,<br>marked by slightly black colour between its horns;<br>the blemish was (only) one, the rest were milk-white.}}

