From {{inh|da|gmq-oda|lændhe}}, from {{inh|da|non|lenda||to land}}, {{inh|da|gem-pro|*landijaną}}, cognate with {{cog|nn|lenda}}, {{cog|sv|landa}} (older {{m|sv|lända}}), {{cog|en|land}}, {{cog|de|landen}} (older {{m|de|länden}}). Derived from the noun {{m|gem-pro|*landą||land}}. The verb has taken over the vowel from the noun in Danish.

====Verb====
{{head|da|verb|past tense|landede|past participle|landet}}

# {{lb|da|intransitive}} to {{l|en|land}} {{q|get down to the ground or into the water after a flight or a jump}}
# {{lb|da|intransitive}} to {{l|en|land}} {{q|come to land with a ship}}
# {{lb|da|intransitive|figuratively}} to {{l|en|land}}, {{l|en|end up}} {{q|in a new state or at a new place, often unwillingly}}
# {{lb|da|transitive}} to {{l|en|land}}, {{l|en|bring down}} {{q|an aircraft or a spaceship}}
# {{lb|da|transitive}} to {{l|en|land}} {{q|bring to land, e.g. fish}}
# {{lb|da|transitive|figuratively}} to {{l|en|land}} {{q|bring home, e.g. an agreement}}

