===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sed-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|se}}, {{m|enm|see}}, from {{der|en|fro|sie||seat, throne; town, capital; episcopal see}}, from {{der|en|la|sedes||seat}}, referring to the bishop's [[throne]] or chair (compare ''seat of power'') in the [[cathedral]]; related to the Latin verb {{m|la|sedere||to sit}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{C|en|Christianity}} a [[diocese]], [[archdiocese]]; a region of a church, generally headed by a [[bishop]], ''especially'' an [[archbishop]].
# The [[office]] of a bishop or archbishop; [[bishopric]] or [[archbishopric]]
# A seat; a site; a place where sovereign power is exercised.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|year=1590|book=III|canto=VI|stanza=2|page=478|passage=Ioue laught on Venus from his ſouerayne '''ſee'''}}

