===Etymology 3===

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{alternative form of|en|cee}}; {{Latn-def|en|name|C|c|nocap=1}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=J. B. Rundell|title=The Irregularities of English Spelling: what they Cost and what they are Worth|journal=The Spelling Reformer, and Journal of the English Spelling Reform Association|volume=I|issue=10|location=London|month=April|year=1881|page=147|passage='''''see''''', ''ar'', ''eye'', ''ee'', ''ess'', cries}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Eva Holmquist|title=No Certain Time|publisher=Libra Publishers|year=1984|page=17|isbn=9780872121829|passage=They were still shocked if you said “eff you '''see''' kay” out loud, though it didn’t stop any of them from doing it.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:Sycamore Review|volume=8|year=1996|page=116|passage=eff you '''see''' kay why oh you.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Eric Barnes (writer)|Eric Barnes]]|title=[[w:Shimmer (novel)|Shimmer]]|location=Denver, Colo.|publisher=Unbridled Books|year=2009|page=91|isbn=978-1-93607-159-3|passage=I hear you. But hear me out, all right? Because I mean what I’m about to say. Eff-you-'''see'''-kay-why-oh-you. Fuck you.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Paul Richardson|title=Taylah’s Got Talent|year=2020|isbn=978-1-716-92650-1|passage=Her mother said, “Maybe you can have ‘Muck Donnas’, or we could have fish and chips.” Krissy shook her head, “Nah. We no have fwishenchit. We have Kay Eff '''See''' nuggers?”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Callum McSorley|chapter=15|title=Squeaky Clean|publisher=w:Pushkin Press|year=2023|isbn=9781782278375|passage=Same old answer: the ''eff-you-'''see'''-kay-you-pee''.}}

