# {{IATA|Albacete Airport||Albacete||Castilla–La Mancha||Spain}}

==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|abece}}, {{m|enm|ABC}}, from the first three letters of the Latin alphabet, standing for the whole alphabet.

====Alternative forms====
* {{sense|noun}} {{l|en|absey}} {{qual|in certain senses only}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA letters|en|A|B|C}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ABC.ogg|Audio (US, California)}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~|s|ABC's}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable|usually plural in|_|North America}} The English [[alphabet]]. {{defdate|First attested from around (1150 to 1350).}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=3}}</ref>
#: ''Do you know your '''ABC'''?'' (US: ''Do you know your '''ABC'''s?'')
#: {{syn|en|absey|q1=obsolete|alphabet}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|poetry}} A type of [[poem]] in which the [[line]]s start with the letters of the alphabet in order. {{defdate|Attested from around (1350 to 1470) until the mid-17th century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[primer]] for teaching the [[Latin alphabet]] and first elements of reading. {{defdate|Attested from around (1350 to 1470) until the mid-17th century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
# The [[fundamental]]s of any subject. {{defdate|First attested in the mid-16th century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
#: ''the '''ABC''' of finance''
#: {{syn|en|basics|fundamentals}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1866|author=D. P. Conyngham|title=The Irish Brigade and Its Campaigns: With Some Account of the Corcoran Legion, and Sketches of the Principal Officers|location=Glasgow|publisher=Cameron & Ferguson|page={{gbooks|Iag6AAAAcAAJ|28|its|A|B|C}}|passage=This was the ''Alma Mater'' of the Brigade, where it learned its '''A B C''' of military tactics.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020-04-21|author=Marina Harss|title=Twist, Bend, Reach, Step: A Merce Cunningham Solo Anyone Can Try|journal=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/04/21/arts/dance/DIY-merce-cunningham.html|passage=With her expert guidance, even a novice like me can have a taste of the focused, structured world of a Cunningham dance. The solo is possibly his plainest, almost an '''ABC''' of his meticulous approach to subdividing the body in motion — twist, bend, reach, step.}}
# {{lb|en|poker}} A [[straightforward]], [[uniform]] playing [[style]], often focusing on betting for [[value]], [[fold]]ing weak hands, and avoiding [[bluffing]].
# {{lb|en|UK|rail transport}} A British [[alphabetize]]d [[guidebook]] listing [[train]]s and their [[station]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1934|title=w:A Handful of Dust|author=w:Evelyn Waugh|publisher=Chapman & Hall|passage=For this reason his heart sank when, emerging from his study into the great hall at quarter to eleven, he met Beaver already dressed and prepared to be entertained; it was only a momentary vexation, however, for while he wished him good morning he noticed that his guest had an '''A.B.C.''' in his hands and was clearly looking out a train.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|en|ABC book}}<!-- a primer. Shakespeare, ''King John, I-i'', as an "absey" book-->
* {{l|en|ABC guide}}
* {{l|en|easy as ABC}}

