Page 3164 գօտի: -------- begin text --------
==Old Armenian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|xcl|գաւտի}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|xcl}}. The original spelling is {{m|xcl|գաւտի}}. Olsen derives from {{bor|xcl|ira}} {{m|und||*gaβtia}}, from {{der|xcl|ine-pro|*gʰeh₁bʰ-|t=to hold}}, connecting also with the ending of {{m|xcl|պարեգօտ|պարեգաւտ|t=coat, tunic}},<ref>{{R:xcl:Olsen|page=874}}</ref><ref>{{R:Textile Terminologies|page=196}}</ref> but this root is not attested in Iranian. J̌ahukyan compares to {{cog|oge|ღუედი}}.<ref>{{R:Jahukyan:1967|pages=97, 188}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{xcl-noun}}

# [[girdle]], [[belt]]
#: {{ux|xcl|գօտի ածել, գօտի ընդ մէջ ածել|t=to gird, to tie or to draw close round the body; to be prompt|inline=1}}
# {{lb|xcl|astrology}} [[belt]] of the sky
# {{lb|xcl|geography}} [[zone]]
#: {{ux|xcl|այրեցած գօտի|t=torrid zone|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|xcl|բարեխառն գօտի|t=temperate zone|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|xcl|սառուցեալ գօտի|t=glacial zone|inline=1}}
# {{lb|xcl|figuratively}} [[rainbow]]; [[mountain]] [[ridge]]; a [[corridor]] in a palace
#: {{ux|xcl|գօտի լերանց|t=chain of mountains|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|xcl|գօտի աստուածական, տէրունեան, Արամազդայ|t=rainbow|inline=1}}

====Usage notes====
The word has five combining forms: {{m|xcl||գօտի-}}, {{m|xcl||գօտե-}}, {{m|xcl||գօտէ-}}, {{m|xcl||գօտեւ-}} and {{m|xcl||գօտել-}}

