==Portuguese==
{{wikipedia|lang=pt}}
[[File:Taula del menjador de la casa Benlliure de València.JPG|thumb|250px|mesa]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|mesa||table}}, from {{inh|pt|VL.|mēsa}}, from {{inh|pt|la|mēnsa||table}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|gl|mesa}}, {{cog|es|mesa}}, {{cog|fr|moise}}, {{cog|it|mensa}} and {{cog|ro|masă}}.

Not related to {{noncog|fa|میز|tr=mêz|t=table}}. As both it and {{m+|pt||mesa}} have been borrowed into different languages of southern Asia, they are sometimes confused by etymologists.

===Pronunciation===
{{pt-IPA|mêsa}}
* {{a|Northeast Brazil}} {{IPA|pt|/ˈme.za/}}
* {{hyphenation|pt|me|sa}}

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|f}}

# [[table]] {{gloss|item of furniture}}
#: {{ux|pt|José, põe a '''mesa''', por favor.|translation=José, please set the '''table'''.}}
#* {{quote-book
|pt
|year=2015
|author=Neil Gaiman
|title=Os filhos de Anansi
|pageurl=http://books.google.com.br/books?id=FEJ3BwAAQBAJ&pg=PT6#v=onepage&q&f=false
|isbn=9788580577006
|page=6
|publisher=Editora Intrinseca
|passage=Cumprimentou-as tocando a aba do chapéu — pois ele usava chapéu, um fedora verde imaculado, além de luvas cor de lima —, e em seguida caminhou até a '''mesa''' onde estavam as mulheres, que deram risada.
|translation=He greeted them by touching the brim of his hat – for he wore a hat, an immaculate green fedora, and lime-colored gloves – and then walked to the table where the women were, who gave a laugh.}}
# [[meal]], [[food]]
#: {{ux|pt|Portugal tem boa '''mesa''' e bom vinho.|translation=Portugal has good '''food''' and good wine.}}
# {{lb|pt|geography}} {{l|en|mesa}}
# [[board]] {{gloss|committee}}

