==Proto-Germanic==

===Etymology===
Derived from {{m|gem-pro|*sīhwaną||to percolate, filter}}, from earlier {{m|gem-pro||*saigwiz}}, Pre-Germanic {{m|ine-pro|*seykʷ-|*soykʷís}}.<ref>{{R:gem:EDPG}}</ref>

Alternatively, from {{der|gem-pro|ine-pro|*sh₂ey-|*sh₂ey-wo-|to be fierce, afflict}} (compare {{cog|la|saevus||wild, fierce}}, Tocharian {{m|txb|saiwe||itch}}, Latvian {{m|lt|sievs}}, {{m|lt|sīvs||sharp, biting}}).<ref>Vladimir Orel, ''A Handbook of Germanic Etymology'', s.v. "saiwiz" (Leiden, Netherlands: Brill, 2003), 314.</ref> Compare {{m|gem-pro|*sairaz||sore, painful}}.

===Pronunciation===
