#: {{syn|gl|cume|curuto}}
# {{lb|gl|by extension}} a hill or mountain that ends in a peak
#: {{syn|gl|coto|outeiro}}
# sharp [[tip]] of anything
#* '''c1350''', Kelvin M. Parker (ed.), ''Historia Troyana''. Santiago: Instituto "Padre Sarmiento", page 30:
#*: {{quote|gl|''Et colleu ella de aquelas mellores et mays nobles et virtuosas eruas hũa partida cõ suas rrayzes, arrãcãdoas cõ hũ '''pico''' de hũa fouçe.''
|translation=And she gathered from the best, more noble and virtuous herbs, a quantity, together with its roots, uprooting them with the help of the '''tip''' of a sickle}}
#: {{syn|gl|bico|punta}}
# [[thorn]]
#: {{syn|gl|espiña}}
# [[pickaxe]]
#* {{quote-text|gl|year=1295|editor=Ramón Lorenzo|title=La traducción gallega de la Crónica General y de la Crónica de Castilla|page=873|location=Ourense|publisher=I.E.O.P.F.
|passage=''Et escaleyras nõ tĩjnã y nẽ '''picos'''''
|translation=They didn't had there ladders or '''pickaxes'''}}
#: {{syn|gl|picaraña}}

