==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{der|sv|la|gradus}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|sv|Sv-grad.ogg|audio}}
* {{rhymes|sv|ɑːd|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|c}}

# [[degree]] (extent)
#: {{ux|sv|I vilken '''grad''' bör man fokusera på kebabsåsens krämighet?|To what '''degree''' should you focus on the creaminess of the kebab sauce?}}
#: {{ux|sv|tredje '''gradens''' brännskador|third '''degree''' burns}}
#: {{ux|sv|närkontakt av tredje '''graden'''|close encounters of the third '''degree''' (idiomatic as opposed to "kind")}}
# {{lb|sv|physics}} [[degree]] (unit of temperature, in Celsius, Fahrenheit, Kelvin, etc.)
#: {{ux|sv|– Hur många '''grader''' är det ute? – 240 '''grader''' Kelvin.|– How many '''degrees''' is it outside? – 240 '''degrees''' Kelvin.}}
#* {{quote-song|sv|author=Ebba Grön|year=1981|album=Kärlek & uppror|trans-album=Love & rebellion|title=800ºC|text=Vi fryser ihjäl. Det är så kallt. Stackars barn. Men snart blir det varmt. Ja, vi fryser ihjäl. Det är så kallt. Stackars barn. Men snart blir det varmt. Det blir 800 '''grader'''. Du kan lita på mig, du kan lita på mig. 800 '''grader'''. Du kan lita på mig, du kan lita på mig.|t=We're freezing to death. It is so cold. Poor children. But soon it'll be warm. Yes, we're freezing to death. It is so cold. Poor children. But soon it'll be warm. It'll be 800 '''degrees'''. You can trust me, you can trust me. 800 '''degrees'''. You can trust me, you can trust me.}}
# {{lb|sv|geometry}} [[degree]] (angular unit)
#: {{ux|sv|Vinkeln är 11 '''grader'''|The angle is 11 '''degrees'''}}
# {{lb|sv|geography}} [[degree]]
#: {{ux|sv|två '''grader''' öst|two '''degrees''' east}}
# {{lb|sv|algebra}} [[degree]]
#: {{ux|sv|x² - 4x + 4 {{=}} 0 är en andra'''grads'''ekvation / en ekvation av andra '''graden''' / en ekvation av '''grad''' 2|x² - 4x + 4 {{=}} 0 is a quadratic equation / a second-'''degree''' equation / an equation of '''degree''' 2}}
# {{senseid|sv|rank}} [[grade]], [[rank]] (especially in the military and academia)
#: {{ux|sv|en officers'''grad'''|a '''grade''' of officer}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''grad'''beteckning|'''rank''' insignia}}
#: {{ux|sv|ha en doktors'''grad'''|have a doctorate ("doctorate '''grade'''")}}
#: {{ux|sv|stiga i '''graderna'''|rise through '''the ranks''' (idiomatic, generally)}}
# {{lb|sv|cooking}} A measurement of [[acetic acid]], corresponding to 6 cl of a 24% [[solution]] or 12 cl of a 12% solution.
#* {{quote-web|1=sv|date=12 June 2012|work=My little bakery|title=Inlagd löksill|trans-title=Pickled onion herring|url=https://mylittlebakery.wordpress.com/category/konserverat/inlaggningar/|text=Lag: 3,5 dl vatten; 0,5 äggkopp salt; 1 '''grad''' ättika.|t=Pickle: 3.5 dl water; 0.5 egg cup salt; 1 '''degree''' vinegar.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=sv|date=14 November 2017|author=Minna Wallén-Widung|journal={{w|Allas|lang=sv}}|title=9 oväntade sätt att använda ättika på|trans-title=9 unexpected ways to use vinegar|url=https://www.allas.se/hushall/9-ovantade-satt-att-anvanda-attika-pa/122874|text={{...}} späd 2 '''grader''' ättika med vatten till 0,5 liter.|t={{...}} dilute 2 '''degrees''' vinegar with water to 0.5 liters.}}

