==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*meli}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*mélit}} (''*mel-it''), with the athematic suffix ''*-it'' that indicates commestible substances (compare IE ''[[*sép-it]]'' «wheat»). Cognate with {{cog|grc|μέλι}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌹𐌻𐌹𐌸}}, {{cog|xcl|մեղր}}, [[Hittite]] ''milit'' and [[Luvic]] ''mallit-''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|mel/mell<3.N.I>}}

# [[honey]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|3|743-744|quote=colligit errantēs et in arbore claudit inānī<br/>Liber et inventī praemia '''mellis''' habet.|trans=''Liber gathers the wandering [bees] and confines them in a hollow tree,<br/>and he has the rewards of discovering '''honey'''.''<br/>(See {{w|Liber}} – the Greek {{w|Dionysus}} or Roman Bacchus – and ''{{w|The Discovery of Honey by Bacchus}}''.)}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Matthew 3:4|quote=[...] esca autem eius erat lucustae et '''mel''' silvestre.|trans=And his food was locusts and wild '''honey'''.}}
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Truculentus|371|notes=ed. by Friedric Leo, ''Plauti Comoediae vol. 2'', 1896, Berlin: Weidmann|quote=Heia, hoc est '''melle''' dulci dulcius.|trans=Ah! This is sweeter than sweet '''honey'''.}} 
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} [[sweetness]], [[pleasantness]]
#* {{Q|la|Quintilian|Institutio Oratoria|3|1|5|quote=Sed nos veremur ne parum hic liber '''mellis''' et absinthii multum habere videatur|trans=But I fear that this book will have too little '''sweetness''' and too much wormwood.}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively|term of endearment}} [[darling]], [[sweet]], [[honey]]
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Bacchides|18|quote=cor meum, spes mea / '''mel''' meum, suavitudo, cibus, gaudium|trans=My heart, my hope, my '''honey''', sweetness, food, delight.}}

