==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|non|ko}}, from East {{inh|sv|non|ko}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*kūz}}, from {{inh|sv|ine-pro|*gʷṓws||cow}}. Cognate with {{cog|non-own|kýr}} and {{cog|en|cow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/kuː/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-ko.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|c}}

# [[cow]]; female [[cattle]]
#: {{uxi|sv|Många '''kor''' bor i stall under vinterhalvåret.|Many '''cows''' live in stables during the winter.}}
# a female member of a number of other species, such as [[elk]]
#: {{uxi|sv|Jag såg en '''älgko''' och hennes kalv när jag var i skogen.|I saw an '''elk cow''' and her calf when I was in the forest.}}

